window.IH_LORE = {"intro":[{"type":"h2","text":"Intro"},{"type":"p","text":"You have died or otherwise transmigrated from your original world. Your soul and whatever comes with you finds itself in a new world with new surroundings: the world of Isekai Hell. During your trip, you are made aware of god. The entity speaks with you familiarly and tells you many things. Why you were chosen. Where you were going. What became of the things you left behind. For some of you, you have a world to get back to and must discover the way. For some, you have nothing worth returning to and must make the most of this new life. For others, it is unclear where you came from if you came from anywhere else at all."},{"type":"p","text":"When describing the world you were going to, god mentioned many things about the world. The people were as diverse as the animal life back on your home world. What you would call fantasy races and magic existed. With that revelation came the explanation about how magic worked and how you would be able to grow and acquire power and influence in time. However, god was particularly vague when it came to what you actually had to do in this new world. It was also noted that there would be others such as yourself in the world and that god intended to bring more as he was able."},{"type":"p","text":"As you near your end of time with god and are about to awaken in the new world, he answers the remaining question hanging in the air,"},{"type":"p","text":"\"...This world is forever stuck in place. Whether it's demon lords, plague, war, or other natural disasters, the world refuses to progress in development. Through mass loss of life, discovery, and culture, the inhabitants of the world can barely stave off moving backwards in their struggle for a better tomorrow. Your mission, should you accept it, is to save the world from its perpetual stasis. Otherwise, live as you please...\""},{"type":"p","text":"Next thing you know, you are waking up to your new reality, life, and/or memories."},{"type":"h2","text":"Isekai Hell: The World"},{"type":"p","text":"To the humans, it is Terra. To the beastkin, it is Gaia. To the fae, it is Prime. The world of Isekai Hell is vast and full of fantasy, mystery, danger, and heart. What's more, it is a living world that will grow and change with time as role players explore it and tell their Isekai stories. This place will be a growing, living compendium of the Isekai Hell world. All content must be approved by Novama or a Lore mod before contributions may be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Ryke: Grade F-C"},{"type":"p","text":"East Empire: Grade E-B"},{"type":"p","text":"The Republic: Grade E-B"},{"type":"p","text":"See of Fae: Grade E-B"},{"type":"p","text":"West Empire: Grade D-B"},{"type":"p","text":"Continental Lake: Grade D-A"},{"type":"p","text":"The Grand Duchy: Grade D-A"},{"type":"p","text":"Kingdom: Grade D-A"},{"type":"p","text":"Sky Nation: Grade D-A"},{"type":"p","text":"Widersia: Grade D-A"},{"type":"p","text":"First Continent: Grade B-S"},{"type":"p","text":"Things yet to come…"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/world-01.webp","alt":"world lore image 1"},{"type":"h2","text":"The Great War"},{"type":"p","text":"The Great War only lasted a few years and ended 50 years ago (as of 2021 irl). Although some would claim longer due to border skirmishes and other tensions. Reasons for the war vary and who is at fault depends on who is asked. Many would cite racial tensions. Others would claim cultural differences or simply resource grabs. Whatever the justifications for why it started, the core reason for how bad it got boiled down to \"the others are a blight upon the land that must be erased\". The East Empire, Fae See, and Beast Republic fought until nearly all military strength had been exhausted. Peace was the only option to ensure no foreign invaders would seize control as well as avoid mutual total annihilation. In the ensuing truce, the wasteland between the feuding countries--scarred by battle and polluted with magic and death--was ceded by the East Empire, which had majority control of the region at the war's close. There was speculation as to the reasoning behind this concession, but, ultimately, the hill country between the region and the rest of the East Empire would make it difficult to hold the land if they refused the truce terms. This land served as a buffer zone between the nations and became formally known as the Protectorate of Ryke."},{"type":"h2","text":"Chronicles of the East-See War"},{"type":"p","text":"War had returned to the 2nd continent, ending the 50 year peace and risking the world's progress once again. After a series of terrorist acts around the East-See border, both nations declared war on each other. While it wasn't clear to the Fae people if they truly had started the war, it was public opinion that the Fae were the aggressors in this case with the destruction of the Empire border town, Chachail."},{"type":"p","text":"When the Fae declared war on the Empire, the humans were conveniently already prepared for war, using Chachail as a rallying cry for their people and to gain public sympathy. With rolling war machines of magic and human ingenuity and enslaved beastkin escorting them, the Empire's armies were formidable. All war capable men were drafted to fight. One of the leading human units were the Feet of Hermes legions from Ghenitus."},{"type":"p","text":"Large swaths of forests in the See burned. Anything that ran out would be mercilessly hunted. Anything that remained would be cooked or mowed down by the war machines rolling through the inferno."},{"type":"h3","text":"The See’s Response"},{"type":"p","text":"The Fae were not surprised by the Empire's swift retaliation and had been preparing to mount a counter offensive. Despite their fewer numbers and vulnerability imposed when leaving their vast forests, the Fae were stronger than they were 50 years ago. Many of the veterans from that war were still alive and their insights would lead a blitz into Empire territory as the Empire's forces massed to march into the forest assuming they would have to. The Fae had a plan and a powerful weapon."},{"type":"p","text":"A tremor is felt in the southern regions of the Empire. Entire cities crumble as the ground ruptures. Ravines spanning miles carve the landscape, isolating some on plateaus without access to their surroundings. When the shaking stops, those left alive offer thanks to their gods, but this was only the beginning…."},{"type":"h3","text":"Trade Impact"},{"type":"p","text":"The Empire’s trade had been disrupted, but their surplus of orichalcum and mythril were now redirected to the war effort. That which wasn’t used in the war became the new Empire currency as bartering orichalcum and mythril became acceptable payments under the assumption that their respective values would skyrocket once external trade resumed."},{"type":"p","text":"Both sides would find themselves in great need for more mundane supplies and resources. Both sides would petition the surrounding nations for aid, but their petitions would go unanswered. However, trade would eventually hit a fever pitch after the brief disruption. The Duchy was supporting the Fae nation with its wealth of magical study and technology. The other nations, specifically the West Empire would seize the opportunity to capitalize on the trading opportunities and wouldn’t be choosy about the side they dealt with. Trade aside, the other nations would notice a heightened sense of racial tensions. The Fae were looked at with a sharper eye. Were they up to something normal or up to something extreme? What about the Humans? Could they be trusted not to take their war to the next step and stir up another continental war?"},{"type":"p","text":"Ryke was definitely not missing out on trade despite noting shortages in precious metals and magical materials, but there was an even greater pressing issue: Infestation. The terrorist act by the Fae in the Empire was apparently to release a bio weapon in the nation that preyed upon her people and devastated the town and surrounding region for many miles. Several adventurer and mercenary requests were posted by the Empire to aid them in dealing with the issue while they continued to prioritize their war effort with the Fae. The call would be answered, but it was unclear if those that answered would be enough. Not much information was getting back to the Adventurer Guild. Apparently, several scouts investigating the site were missing…"},{"type":"h3","text":"The Infestation Begins"},{"type":"p","text":"The scratching in the walls never went away, but no one bothered to investigate. Now it is far too late. They came from the south empire. That’s all anyone could say when asked about the bugs now roaming the lands. Ravenous. Unstoppable. Like a plague of locusts that is only satiated with blood and flesh, these insectoids ravage everywhere they reach."},{"type":"p","text":"Early assessments believed that deep expanses of water or high walls would suffice in stopping them, but these merely slow them down. When you face them, you do not face one, but many, and the many do not hesitate to sacrifice themselves to get at their next morsel. Drowning themselves to create causeways across water. Scrambling over each other, piling up into heaps to cross obstacles. When they have completely consumed an area and are still hungry, they cannibalize their own. Every means they employ is to further their persistence, and there is very little they won’t do to that end. Even metal and stone doors wouldn’t keep them out indefinitely. The bugs came and surged upon the land in thousands upon thousands in number. There was talk that there were even stronger or smarter bugs roaming the lands, leading the rest, but that was more theory than living eyewitness testimony."},{"type":"h3","text":"Several months have passed…"},{"type":"p","text":"The infestation proved a greater threat than originally thought and has claimed a large swath of territory that threatens to cut off the fighting forces to the south and also expand north east into the Empire interior. The Fae, despite leaving behind their forest line, have gained ground and are effectively pressing the Empire back. The forest burning didn’t last long before they were put on the defensive and forced to contend with town destroyers they did not have good solutions for contending with."},{"type":"h3","text":"Paizu Shifting"},{"type":"p","text":"Meanwhile, there was a rumbling in the Paizu mountains. It was as if the very earth raged. On the winds that blew through the peaks, a single phrase was repeated as a maddening mantra: “I am forgotten.” The mountains quake and shift daily. People in the surrounding plains claim the skyline of the mountains is changing. There are only harbingers of what’s to come."},{"type":"h2","text":"Chronicles of the Eastern Realms"},{"type":"subtitle","text":"The Accord of Necessity and the Shadow of the Hive"},{"type":"p","text":"In the annals of our time, it is recorded that in the year of the Twilit Sun, two great nations—long embattled and steeped in enmity—set aside their strife to confront a dire threat. The East Empire, a bastion of human ambition modeled upon the grandeur of ancient legacies, and the Fae See, a sanctified realm of devout fae who venerated the elemental forces and the living deity known as the Spirit King, found themselves compelled into an uneasy alliance."},{"type":"p","text":"The cause of this concord was the emergence of a monstrous horde—a ravenous swarm of chitinous beasts emanating from the unknown and dwelling within the depths beneath the eastern frontiers. This hive, led by a calculating queen, devoid of malice yet resolute in her intent to expand and nourish her progeny, posed an existential threat to all organic life. The Fae, possessing ancestral knowledge of these creatures from a time immemorial, forewarned that the swarm's hunger knew no bounds and would consume the very essence of the lands if not dealt with."},{"type":"h3","text":"The Peace Talks"},{"type":"p","text":"The peace negotiations, henceforth known as the Accord of Necessity, were fraught with tension. The East Empire, bearing the scars of recent assaults they attributed to Fae sabotage and the unleashing of the hive upon their territories, approached the table with distrust and thinly veiled animosity. The Fae See, guided by their spiritual doctrines and the wisdom of the Spirit King, sought harmony but remained wary of the Empire's intentions."},{"type":"p","text":"Despite these undercurrents, the Empire emerged with significant concessions in their favor. Territorial rights were realigned, and trade agreements were established that benefitted the Empire's coffers. The Fae See, valuing the greater good and the sanctity of life above material gains, acquiesced to these terms to ensure a united front against the hive."},{"type":"h3","text":"The Campaign Against the Hive"},{"type":"p","text":"United, though not unified in spirit, the two nations embarked upon a perilous campaign to quell the hive's expansion. The East Empire deployed their legions, bolstered by mages adept in the arcane arts, wielding magic bombs devised to obliterate the hive's subterranean chambers. Concurrently, the elite forces of the Fae See undertook a series of diversionary tactics, employing their innate connection to nature and elemental forces to mislead and scatter the swarm."},{"type":"p","text":"In the depths of the earth, battles raged. The Empire's magic bombs found their marks, collapsing several of the hive's egg chambers and stymying the immediate growth of the swarm. The Fae See's diversions were executed with such finesse that many of their finest warriors returned unscathed, a testament to their strategic acumen and perhaps, some whispered, the blessings of the Spirit King himself."},{"type":"p","text":"However, victory bore a heavy cost. The Empire's forces suffered grievous losses, their ranks decimated by the relentless onslaught of the hive's defenders. The Fae See mourned the fallen but counted few among them, their losses mitigated by the success of their tactics."},{"type":"h3","text":"Aftermath and the Shadow of Future Conflict"},{"type":"p","text":"In the wake of the campaign, a tenuous peace settled over the lands. The hive, though wounded, was not vanquished. The queen retreated deeper into the labyrinthine caverns, her resolve unshaken. It was whispered among sages that she bided her time, her brood recovering, waiting for the moment to surge forth once more."},{"type":"p","text":"The East Empire, emboldened by their negotiated gains yet humbled by their losses, turned inward to rebuild. Their distrust of the Fae deepened, seeded by envy and the perception of betrayal, as rumors spread that the Fae had orchestrated the initial emergence of the hive—a claim the Fae vehemently denied."},{"type":"p","text":"The Fae See returned to their sacred groves and crystalline spires, their people seeking solace in prayer and communion with the elements. They remained vigilant, aware that the Empire's gaze might soon turn hostile once more. The Spirit King, in his wisdom, urged his people to prepare not just for the threat below but for the shadows looming in the hearts of men."},{"type":"h3","text":"Epilogue"},{"type":"p","text":"The grand hall of the Jade Fang Clan's ancestral estate was adorned with tapestries depicting legendary beasts and heroes of old. Lanterns cast a warm glow upon the polished jade floors, reflecting the opulence of one of the most powerful beastman families in the West Empire."},{"type":"p","text":"Patriarch Lao Shen sat upon his carved throne, his golden eyes gazing thoughtfully into the depths of a steaming cup of tea. The silence of the hall was interrupted only by the soft footsteps of a figure emerging from the shadows."},{"type":"p","text":"A cloaked beastman approached, his feline features partially concealed beneath his hood. Without a word, he knelt before Lao Shen, presenting a sealed scroll marked with a sigil known only to the inner circle of the clan."},{"type":"p","text":"Lao Shen accepted the scroll, but before breaking the seal, he spoke in a measured tone. \"What news do you bring from the East?\""},{"type":"p","text":"The operative's tail flicked subtly. \"The seeds we planted have taken root,\" he said cryptically. \"The alliance between the East Empire and the Fae See falters. Their efforts against the subterranean threat yielded... limited fruit.\""},{"type":"p","text":"A faint smile tugged at the corner of Lao Shen's mouth. \"And our unseen hands?\""},{"type":"p","text":"\"Guided events as intended,\" the beastman replied. \"Subtle interventions ensured that neither side could claim total victory. Resources are depleted, trust wears thin, and whispers of doubt grow louder among their ranks.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Lao Shen nodded slowly, his gaze distant. \"The merchants report increased demands?\""},{"type":"p","text":"\"Indeed. Their need for our goods and expertise has never been greater. They turn to us for what they lack—supplies, arcane knowledge, even counsel.\""},{"type":"p","text":"The patriarch leaned forward. \"And what of the deeper currents?\""},{"type":"p","text":"The operative hesitated for the briefest moment. \"There are... movements in the shadows beyond our own. Agreements have been honored, and certain interests align with ours, for now.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Lao Shen's eyes narrowed, but he did not press further. \"Very well. Continue to observe. Ensure our influence remains... discreet.\""},{"type":"p","text":"The beastman bowed his head. \"As you command.\""},{"type":"p","text":"As the operative melted back into the shadows, Lao Shen unsealed the scroll and read its contents by the flickering light. The words confirmed what he already knew—the delicate balance of power was tipping in their favor. A prolonged conflict between the East Empire and the Fae See would open avenues for the Jade Fang Clan to expand their reach, both economically and politically."},{"type":"p","text":"Lao Shen rose from his throne and walked toward the expansive window overlooking the moonlit gardens. The night air was filled with the scent of jasmine and the distant sound of flowing water."},{"type":"p","text":"\"Let the East grapple with their woes,\" he mused softly. \"We shall be the silent beneficiaries of their discord.\""},{"type":"h2","text":"New Patent Holds the Line Against the Infestation"},{"type":"p","text":"Aedrianna Belmonte, a human from Ryke, in cooperation with Dread Mage Ammadeus Belmonte of the Grand Duchy, has patented a pesticide capable of holding the bugs at bay. The intervention is twofold: the first, a putrid aerosol, wards away giant insects, while the second, a sinister mixture of animal fats and specific poisons meant to be planted in the nests, causes issues with reproduction and growth. This revolutionary invention has been distributed to the nobility of Ryke and leadership in the Otenzian Empire (East)."},{"type":"h2","text":"Shifting Earth Brings New Wave of Threats to Second Continent"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/world-02.webp","alt":"world lore image 2"},{"type":"p","text":"A series of catastrophic earthquakes shook the Second Continent, tearing open countless enormous chasms across the land. Entire roads, forests, and settlements were damaged or destroyed, while many people disappeared into the newly formed holes and remain missing."},{"type":"p","text":"In the Fae See of Chaeron, the quakes shattered an ancient seal beneath the forest, unleashing swarms of demonic Hell Moths upon the realm. Facing overwhelming losses, the Cardinals ignited the sacred Life Tree, sending a beacon across the continent that called allies from every nation."},{"type":"p","text":"The response was immediate."},{"type":"p","text":"Warriors, adventurers, healers, mercenaries, knights, and mages answered the call from every corner of the world. Some organized defensive lines around settlements while others escorted refugees through burning forests."},{"type":"p","text":"Military commanders established coordinated kill squads to contain advancing swarms. Scouts searched relentlessly for nests, while healers struggled to keep pace with mounting casualties. Veteran monster hunters identified weaknesses in the demons' strange anatomy, allowing defenders to bring down creatures previously thought nearly invincible."},{"type":"p","text":"Entire campaigns were fought over days as soldiers pushed through forests to destroy nests, secure supply routes, evacuate civilians, and reclaim villages one battle at a time."},{"type":"p","text":"The cost was severe. Villages burned. Ancient forests were scarred. Countless soldiers and civilians perished defending one another."},{"type":"p","text":"Through the gathered effort of many, those unlikely and expected alike; the Giant Hell Moths were defeated. Or at least those that made it through the rift that had been opened by the earthquakes."},{"type":"p","text":"It soon became apparent throughout the continent that the massive earthquakes had opened many large holes across the land. And many people have been reported missing. An insurmountable amount of damage has been done to cities and villages alike."},{"type":"p","text":"One of said tectonic shifts happened in the Continental Lake. Resulting in a whirlpool, and the release of a two headed Hydra that encroached on the shore of the Grand Duchy or Roran. It was quickly dispatched by a swift response from adventurers."}],"countries":[{"id":"ryke","name":"Ryke","aliases":["Ryke","Isekai Hell - Ryke"],"summary":"The starter country for this roleplay and likely the one to have the most content in the beginning. Most of this information will have already been present in the lore page for new members. That information and more will also be made available here. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to canon.","theme":{"accent":"#d7b45a","accent2":"#b12d39","glow":"#72c1b6","deep":"#18090c","motif":"trade"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"Ryke"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - Ryke"},{"type":"p","text":"The starter country for this roleplay and likely the one to have the most content in the beginning. Most of this information will have already been present in the lore page for new members. That information and more will also be made available here. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to canon."},{"type":"h2","text":"Country - Protectorate of Ryke"},{"type":"h3","text":"National Emblem"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/ryke-01.webp","alt":"ryke lore image 1"},{"type":"p","text":"Sporting several rivers, some of which are massive in size, the country is rich in plant life and animals. Most of the country is covered in temperate deciduous forests and grassy fields. A few of the water ways are encased in temperate rainforest. Surrounded on all sides by powerful nations larger than they are, the protectorate of Ryke walks a narrow line of neutrality and diplomacy. A series of mostly wise rulers has allowed for the country to see a boom in trade and culture as it acts as the buffer zone between the 3 countries that surround it as well as countries from even further away thanks to intercontinental waterways. Located in the eastern continent and north east of the eastern continent's central lake."},{"type":"p","text":"To the far east of the country there is hill country mostly covered in Tiagas with a few Tundra areas."},{"type":"h3","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/ryke-02.webp","alt":"ryke lore image 2"},{"type":"h3","text":"Population - <1,000,000"},{"type":"p","text":"The small country unsurprisingly has a smaller population than the kingdoms and empires it sits by. Most of the population are humans with a healthy amount of faefolk like the elves, dwarves, and others. To a lesser degree, but notable, there are also many of the Beastfolk. Lizardmen and Predator feline species being fairly abundant among their number."},{"type":"h3","text":"Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"Ryke is one of the freest trading nations in the world. Anyone can start up a business and sell off their creations or goods they buy from producers. The competition is fierce, but there is no government intervention. Ryke, as a country, has certain stipulations placed on it by its neighbors that they must give favorable trade deals equally and in abundance."},{"type":"p","text":"The currency in Ryke and accepted in the three major nations is called Rykes. While the surrounding nations may have their own currencies or thoughts on trade, Rykes are considered most stable, widely circulated, and accepted at this time. Rykes are metal elongated coins that come in copper, silver, gold, and platinum versions. The average peasant working a skilled job generally lives on 100 Rykes a day (food, lodging, basic purchases). 1 ryke = 1 copper ryke. 10 rykes = 1 silver ryke. 100 rykes = 1 gold ryke. 1000 rykes = 1 platinum ryke. Due to advantageous trading arrangements for other nations, Ryke is more favorable for merchants than craftspeople. Better and more specialized crafts are imported from other nations, but Ryke has a wide variety of goods to offer as well. Making money on every transaction that passes through her, Ryke is a prosperous country acting as the trade up for the eastern half of the continent."},{"type":"h3","text":"Security"},{"type":"p","text":"Common in several major cities, especially in the Protectorate of Ryke, as well as smaller towns, a magical item known as Black Orb is in circulation. Possessed by the law enforcing body of the area, the black orb is used to determine criminals and monsters from normal travelers. Titles will appear on the black orbs surface when used. When a user places their hand on the orb, the titles that show will be specifically theirs. The titles shown will only be criminal titles or monster titles. No other titles will be shown. Monsters and criminals will be prevented entry into the city or town and in some cases killed on the spot or hunted down with the discovery."},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel"},{"type":"p","text":"While the predominant forms of travel are on boats in the water ways and animal drawn wagon/carriages, there is a 2nd option: Portals. Magic portals cover the world. Most are hidden away in dungeons, deep forests, and treacherous mountains, but a few towns and all major cities have one. Portals allow for travel between any 2 portals instantly. However, they are limited in size, can act as borders between some nations, and can only warp and individual to another portal location they have already been to. Due to the constraints of its use and potential for abuse, most portals are heavily guarded. Black Orbs tend to be used on those passing through portals. Portal travel is not cheap, costing several Rykes per leg of the journey."},{"type":"h3","text":"Capital - Ryken"},{"type":"p","text":"A city built and kept alive by the country's largest river: Kabnak, it sees several tons of goods flowing in and out of its ports on a regular basis. It is by far the most prosperous city in the country and where most of the nobility reside. The massive palace of the royal family sits above all and is able to survey the lifeline of the city and country with ease: its water and road ways. Despite being the capital of a protectorate, what the city and country lacks in military might, it makes up for in wealth. Making enough money from trade to rival other nations, the country is able to afford its talented Adventurers and mercenaries. The official currency of Ryken is called Rykes."},{"type":"h3","text":"Factions"},{"type":"p","text":"Major groups of individuals working together to influence events in Ryke and beyond are listed here. This is not a complete list, but can give a starting point to those interested in involving their characters in such things. Among those not listed, there are whispers of various criminal and monstrous groups as well:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Nobles"},{"type":"p","text":"Ryke has a diverse faction of nobles responsible for the governing of the protectorate. Among the nobles, there are many sub functions that answer to one foreign body or special interest or another. Nobles purely interested in the governing of just Ryke's people are far and few between. With the power to levy taxes, raise armies, and get audiences with local leaders of other factions including other nobles, they are some of the most powerful people in the country on paper."},{"type":"h4","text":"Royalty"},{"type":"p","text":"King Akio the Wise - A former resident of the Beasts' Republic, He's a lion beastman."},{"type":"p","text":"Queen Eirene - A human formerly of the East Empire, is known for being quite the diplomat."},{"type":"p","text":"Prince Orion - The firstborn, is a fae despite his parentage. He was blessed by the spirit king while still in the queen's womb and was born with a heightened mana level that impacted his physiology. He has a thirst for knowledge more than anything. very in tune with his people and the culture."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/ryke-03.webp","alt":"ryke lore image 3"},{"type":"p","text":"Appearance:"},{"type":"p","text":"Princess Sakura - The secondborn, beastwoman taking the strength of her father and the grace of her mother. More of a fox-related breed of beastman than the lion type of her father. Despite being secondborn, she is predicted to be the next heir since the nations agree fae are better as advisers than leaders due to their longer life spans that don't mesh as well with the people they would rule over."},{"type":"h4","text":"Duchies and Counties"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/ryke-04.webp","alt":"ryke lore image 4"},{"type":"p","text":"Duchy of Seroria (Human)\nRuled over by Duke Thaddeus Halgorn Seroria. A seasoned diplomat with ties to the surrounding nations. He was instrumental in the peace and abundance that Ryke sees today."},{"type":"p","text":"Count Hadi Sadek (Half-Elf)\nRules over the county of Sadek, previously known as the County of Light. A veteran and scholar, who was favoured by the current Seroria Duke to resolve the issues of the former County of Light."},{"type":"p","text":"Countess Amara Nightshade (Fae)\nRules over the county with the most forests in the duchy just north of Sadek county an enigmatic and alluring fae, she has made an effort to draw in others of her kind as well as magic scholars and inventors."},{"type":"p","text":"County Bartholomew Ironwright (Human)\nGoverns the most northern county belonging to Seroria. An industrious man, he governs in a way that favours the trades and crafts that move through his county. Serves to help control the financial prosperity of the duchy and the nation as a whole."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Ludd Garanth (Human)\nA twelve-year old human noble, heir to the Garanth Barony to the north of Ryken, which currently happens to be in a regency of his chamberlain."},{"type":"p","text":"Duchy of Brysta (Fae)\nRuled over by Duchess Elysia Vanth Brysta. A patron of the Imperial Logia Academy of Ryken and a savvy businesswoman. She has led the nation and maintained her duchy through her various innovations in trade and the arts."},{"type":"p","text":"Count Eldrin of Sylvarin (Fae)\nCount Eldrin rules over Sylvarin, a region known for its lush, verdant forests, which are home to a variety of valuable herbs and medicinal plants. Eldrin, as a fae, has an intimate connection with nature, and his rule has been marked by a careful balance of utilizing natural resources while preserving the beauty and health of the forests. He has worked closely with Duchess Elysia to establish Brysta as a hub of knowledge and innovation, using his deep understanding of the forest's bounty to aid in research and education. Eldrin has a slender, elegant figure, with gossamer wings reflecting the colours of the forest canopy. His rule has seen a blossoming of trade in herbal remedies and natural medicines, further enhancing the economic prosperity of Brysta."},{"type":"p","text":"Countess Isolde of Valyra (Human)\nCountess Isolde governs Valyra, a region rich in precious metals and minerals. She is a strong and ambitious leader, leveraging the natural wealth of Valyra to attract skilled craftsmen and engineers to her land. Under her rule, Valyra has become known for producing high-quality tools, jewellery, and mechanical devices, which are traded throughout Ryke and beyond. Isolde is a tall, commanding figure, often seen wearing intricately designed jewellery made from the metals mined from her lands. Her strong leadership and strategic trade policies have greatly contributed to the economic growth of Brysta and the prosperity of Ryke as a whole."},{"type":"h4","text":"Adventurer's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"The guild spans the globe but has country specific branches that answer to the rules and authorities therein. It is a place respected as the goto to request things done and have them done. The ranks of the guild are made up of warriors, mages, and many other talents from around the world. Just about any task that comes with a financial reward will get done. Due to their military might, they are closely monitored by the Noble factions. Their vast needs for equipment and supplies make the patron favorites with the Merchant's guild."},{"type":"h4","text":"Merchant's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"A loose association of trade groups that control the trade and commerce of a region. They are responsible for the acquisition, distribution and create of many goods the world over. Most companies and businessmen are affiliated with the Merchant's guild or one of its affiliates. While the Nobles can set taxes on trade, travel, and entry among other things, it si the merchant's guild that determines base pricing and where shops are allowed to open and do business. More than one town has had its supply of necessary commodities shortened by a displeased Merchant's guild. They regularly hire the Adventurer's guild as protectors and escorts."},{"type":"h4","text":"Church"},{"type":"p","text":"While there are several faiths in Ryke, there is an organized body of believers that establishes which faiths are worthy of worship and which are heresies, cults, and extremist groups. This faction generally has the favor of the people and is one respected by all other factions for one reason or another. Supported predominantly by the donations of the people and other factions, they dole out miracles and blessings in good measure. It is said they have performed such feats as bringing a [god] to meetings and raising the dead back to life."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/ryke-05.webp","alt":"ryke lore image 5"},{"type":"h3","text":"Culture"},{"type":"p","text":"Angel Statues"},{"type":"p","text":"Solemn statues, resembling that of celestial entities or aerials, are often built in the graveyards around Ryke in order to remember the fallen who do not possess tombstones, graves or a place in which to remember them."},{"type":"p","text":"Credits - Cinders (Visual Novel) | Contributed by Elvario"},{"type":"h3","text":"Ryken Adventurer's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"This branch of the Adventurer's Guild is located within Ryke's protectorate. It is a faction of diverse and capable adventurers that tend to be the go-to individuals for any number of requests. Their ranks consist of warriors, mages, and a variety of more exotic talents that all total up to any odd job being well within the Guild's collective capabilities. Whether those capabilities are put to work depends on the amount of financial compensation."},{"type":"p","text":"Main Hall"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/ryke-06.webp","alt":"ryke lore image 6"},{"type":"p","text":"The main hall of the Guild displays an homage to their notable members by lining the walls of the lavish space with the seals of different adventuring parties. This décor represents their members' strength and the dedication to their work - and how the Guild is unafraid to flaunt their might."},{"type":"h4","text":"NPCs"},{"type":"p","text":"Edvar - Grizzled half-orc and acting guildmaster for the Ryke Adventurer Guild [Ryke]. He is a double-axe wielding veteran adventurer moved to the position of guildmaster."},{"type":"p","text":"Lathryn Goddard - Warden and Leader of the City Defence Force through the Adventurers Guild in Ryken."},{"type":"h3","text":"The Imperial Logia Academy of Ryken"},{"type":"p","text":"The Imperial Logia Academy of Ryken is one of the premier educational institutions in the Protectorate of Ryke. Thousands of applications pour into the academy's limited acceptance rate. The academy sits within the confines of the capital city, Ryken."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Macer’s Tavern"},{"type":"p","text":"A cheap, although verily cushy, tavern located in the capital of Ryken, of Ryke. Although, despite its cosy aesthetics and atmosphere, it is known to serve quite… strange dishes, for example, ‘Rockworms.’"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Grand Art Gallery"},{"type":"p","text":"The newly reformed Grand Art Gallery of Ryken. Its design and architecture is only possible thanks to a cooperation with specialists from the Grand Duchy. A mysterious being called 'Neco-Arc' was seen here recently."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Norroburry Village"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/ryke-07.webp","alt":"ryke lore image 7"},{"type":"h4","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"p","text":"A small village located in the eastern, near some of the slightly more mountainous areas of Ryke bordering the Empire. The economy of the village is heavily reliant on the nearby mines being operated, as they are known to produce valuable materials for the rest of the country. They have a local militia to keep them safe, a big boarding house to house seasonal workers for the mines and a beautiful view of the Norroburry Lake."},{"type":"p","text":"Irwin Stonewolf - Head of Militia in Norroburry"},{"type":"p","text":"Simin - Dwarven mine overseer in Norroburry"},{"type":"p","text":"Lady Catherine Felinus - former noble, C-grade buddy tamer, keeps 101 cats"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - The City of Azuran"},{"type":"p","text":"The city of Azuran is nestled along the southwestern border of Ryke, becoming a major trade city in the southwest region. Many merchants come inside Ryke and outside come to this city due to the access of goods from the country right across the border. The border had shifted from time to time, over the centuries; however currently, the city was in the Protectorate of Ryke's territory. The city originally started out as a small village but as the borders moved money came to the village as trading became its main source of income. Many people set up their shops in the village as it slowly expanded over time turning it into a thriving trade city. Many of the upper class are known to have black market dealings and there are even rumors of a terrorist organization calling this city home."},{"type":"p","text":"Recent Events"},{"type":"p","text":"Entrance Exams (start of fall semester)"},{"type":"p","text":"Monsters for Tuition Program (fall break)"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - The Celestine Academy for Seekers of Lore and Legends"},{"type":"p","text":"The campus sprawls across the verdant foothills bordering the city of Azuran. Towers of shimmering stone house arching halls filled with star-charts, trophies from quests, and relics of mythic heroes. The legendary Celestine Spring flows through the grounds, said to have miraculous healing properties.Brief History: Founded 132 years ago by the great half-elven scholar Celestine Silverquill, the academy collects knowledge and artifacts from ages past in order to prepare new generations of adventurers. Many famous legends have passed through its halls."},{"type":"p","text":"Example Tenured Faculty (full-time/ex-adventurer/longterm):"},{"type":"p","text":"Headmaster Iando Starseeker: A wise silver-haired elf who has led the academy for over a century. His skills in divination and foresight are unparalleled."},{"type":"p","text":"Professor Esmuse the Song Mistress: An eccentric half-elf bard who fills the campus with music and teaches poetry, storytelling and legends."},{"type":"p","text":"Sir Braxus Dragonheart: The bold dragonborn paladin oversees combat training and strategy in the famous Hall of Valor. He claims to be an ancestor of Infernox."},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Detailed Sir Braxus"},{"type":"p","text":"Wilderness Master Cedar's Shadow: This wood elf ranger disappeared into the Great Forest 100 years ago. Some say his spirit still guides students in dreams.More fantasy-style faculty to come!"},{"type":"p","text":"The Crow: Whispers spread each year among the students; some recognized the figure as The Crow, a mysterious Tengu professor known for their elusive nature and rumored exploits. He once uncovered the Lost Tomes of Eldar, possesses a seemingly infinite assortment of adventure maps, and a robe of living black shadows swaths their body."},{"type":"p","text":"Example Adjunct Faculty (part-time/adventurers/contract-basis)"},{"type":"p","text":"Eris Granstone"},{"type":"p","text":"Lysandra Swiftgear, A Gnome Ethical and Legal Advisor. As a highly skilled legal scholar, Lysandra possesses a vast knowledge of the laws, treaties, and ethical codes governing the actions of individuals and nations. Her gnomish aptitude for invention also translates into a knack for logical reasoning and puzzle-solving."},{"type":"p","text":"Others..."},{"type":"p","text":"Example Students"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Example Students"},{"type":"h4","text":"Feasting Hall of Champions"},{"type":"p","text":"The campus was open, it's gates thrown wide for the annual Entrance Exam for new hopefuls. For those who paid the entrance fee, more of a down payment on their tuition, they could enjoy a fabulous breakfast followed by competition against other hopefuls to join one of a handful of new cohorts. Each cohort would be tested and evaluated, but first everyone would enjoy breakfast."},{"type":"p","text":"Inside the vaulted Feasting Hall of Champions, magical light streamed through tall rainbow prisms that sent multicolored light through the arched windows and across the long feast tables. A sumptuous buffet welcomed new hopefuls and those second and third years who were coming back after the long adventuring break in-between semesters. The academy was practical and balanced education with active field work. The Feasting Hall was filled with nervous excitement, the air charged as the newcomers took their seats among the colorful banners hanging from ceiling rafters. Today marked the start of their trials!"},{"type":"p","text":"There were many entrances into the hall, and amidst one of the bustling entry halls, three sneering second-years stood blocking a pair of the grand doors to the Feasting Hall. Most hopeful had never been on campus and so usually had no idea they could simply go to another entrance. Bartholomew Voralcrest, a tall wizard with a wild shock of black hair like living shadow, grinned wickedly as he denied entry to the anxious first years."},{"type":"p","text":"A few who had tried last year and failed, knew of other entrances and wandered away from the commotion, but without making a big deal of it. They just shook their head and sighed before moving off for another door. However, most were here for the first time and observed the scene nervously. They oscillated between keeping their distance and wanting to eat before the exam. The scent of the food just beyond made many salivate. For many, they paid the entrance fee just to experience this breakfast in the celebrated hall to dream, even though they knew it would never come to be. And now they were forced to keep their distance or pay, not wanting to provoke the intimidating trio."},{"type":"p","text":"Vaulted ceilings towered overhead, sunlight streaming through massive stained glass windows depicting epic tales of legends who had passed through these hallowed halls. Long tables were piled high with extravagant foods - fluffy pastries dripping with honey, juicy hams glazed with spices, towers of colorful fruits and cheeses."},{"type":"p","text":"The newcomers eagerly filled their plates and found seats among the other students. An energetic hum of conversation filled the hall as they swapped stories, compared programs of study, and marveled at the wonders surrounding them. Many second and third year students welcomed the newcomers warmly."},{"type":"p","text":"After the anxiety of the morning, the mood lightened considerably as the new recruits enjoyed the camaraderie and bountiful feast. Their initial challenges outside faded into memory as they immersed themselves in the celebrations."},{"type":"h4","text":"The Celestine Spring"},{"type":"p","text":"This ancient spring flows from a cave covered in colorful mosaics, depicting Celestine Silverquill's discovery of the magical waters. The perfectly clear pool is said to have rejuvenating properties - drinking or bathing in it restores vitality and health. Students flock to the spring before exams or difficult quests. The waters glimmer an ethereal blue-silver hue under the moonlight. Many couples have had moonlit trysts beside the enchanting spring."},{"type":"p","text":"Nervous whispers circulated as the newcomers were led in groups along winding paths that followed the glittering streams flowing from the legendary Celestine Spring."},{"type":"p","text":"The crystalline waters burbled merrily over moss-covered rocks. Intricate mosaics depicting the spring's mythical origins lined the passageways, hints of magic glimmering in the tiles. The first years paused to sip from the rejuvenating waters, gathering their courage before entering the testing chambers."},{"type":"h4","text":"Museum of Lore and Legends"},{"type":"p","text":"This hallowed hall contains artifacts collected the past century by adventurers and scholars. Towering fossilized dragon bones form a dramatic centerpiece, coming from an ancient red dragon called Infernox who once terrorized the kingdom. His skull alone is larger than a carriage. Other highlights include the shattered Blade of Andariel, ring armor worn by the famous dwarf Grun Stoneheart, and a rare phoenix feather quill. Scholars study the relics while dreaming up quests to find more. There are always new wings and vaults being expanded as the museum continues growing."},{"type":"h4","text":"Shade Hall and the Crow"},{"type":"p","text":"Unlike more illustrious and grand occasions, today students and low-ranked adventurers, mixed in groups, filled into Shade Hall of the Celestine Academy. This large room was concave, with a gently sloping spiral walk way around it that slopped down towards a flat section in the middle and like most halls had doors at each cardinal point. It was dimly lit, shadows dancing along walls adorned with ancient books and artifacts. The air with a buzz of anticipation. The setting sun cast a golden glow through tall stain glass windows, signaling the approach of twilight when the stain glass seemed to come alive with shifting patterns."},{"type":"h4","text":"The Crypt of the Autumn Equinox"},{"type":"p","text":"Each Autumn Equinox an ancient crypt, a relic of a time shrouded in mystery, said to conceal secrets and treasures of unimaginable worth, awakens.\""},{"type":"p","text":"The map showed a labyrinthine crypt marked with arcane symbols and cryptic notes. The crypt seemed to have eight entrances at each cardinal point and in-between. The Crow's finger traced paths through the corridors, pausing at a chamber marked with an enigmatic sigil. \"These halls will test your skill, courage, and thirst for knowledge. But beware, the crypt guards its secrets fiercely, with ancient guardians and long-forgotten curses.\""},{"type":"p","text":"With a sigh, he paused, \"Those of you gathered are being offered an opportunity during semester break to pay for your tuition and further your course work. Not all of you are students, others are vetted adventurers or potential recruits for the next semester. This event starts with our students of course, but others are invited to support them in their studies. It's important that they are exposed to all aspects of this life. For those of you outside our illustrious academy, fame and glory can be found.\""},{"type":"p","text":"He gestured to the map, the crypt shifts but these records are from last year. \"Look at it if you want. You'll have until midnight to prepare as you see fit. Then we will meet at the South Quad and I'll lead you to the crypt.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Amidst the preparations, snippets of conversation floated in the air. \"They say The Crow knows passages in the crypt that aren't on any map,\" a grizzled adventurer shared in a hushed tone. \"And I heard the crypt is cursed, that not all who enter find their way back,\" a student replied, his voice tinged with both fear and excitement."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Noghe Village"},{"type":"p","text":"A small and quite quiet, gloomy village located in the hilly and mountainous areas of the country of Ryke. The village has various residents who tend to their own gardens and small farms, cultivating various crops as means of food. The Village is known to be very near to a Tribe of Trolls with which they are now in a truce."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Wendy's Trading Post"},{"type":"p","text":"A rest stop which is located somewhere in the countryside of Ryke. The rest stop is a relatively modest tavern and a trading post, on the side of a road called Wendy’s Trading Post. The rest stop is run by the Matriarch, Wendy, and her family. The place is welcoming and is well for those who wish to rest and get a few drinks before continuing their adventures."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Sootspire Village"},{"type":"p","text":"A hamlet located in the far eastern parts of the County of Sadek, in the Caelia Barony. The village’s infrastructure and architecture are largely aligned with the settlement’s focus on mining. The village mainly exports various ores and coal due to being located close to the hills. Its residents are mostly quite strong and taller on average compared to the average person."},{"type":"p","text":"Berk - Owner of the Tavern and Inn of Sootspire. Ex-Husband of Hestia in Stonewall."},{"type":"p","text":"Hallr - Prospector and overseer of the mine in Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"Jarek - Blacksmith in Sootspire. Triplet brother of Gobán and the smith in Kirkwall."},{"type":"p","text":"Prisca - Elder and Mayor of the village Sootspire."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Town of Faeremeadow"},{"type":"p","text":"A small farming town in the south tip of Ryke that lies in between the See of Fae and the East Empire. They are known for their production of corn, wheat, and cattle. The population consists mainly of Humans and Beastfolk, with occasional Fae passing through. It has a single large inn and tavern in the center of town, and most of it's tradesman make a living off repairs and special requests. A small market street that sells clothing and food lines the main road."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Arborhaven"},{"type":"p","text":"A city formerly surrounding an ancient tree located in the far south of Ryke on the border of the See of Fae. The citizens worship an exalted tree spirit of the ancient tree, [Aegrizora]. After the heroics of a small group, the deity that resided within the tree was freed and disappeared, taking the giant tree with it. Now Arborhaven is left recovering from the suspicious happenings of a cult and losing its local deity and main attraction."},{"type":"p","text":"It was revealed recently that the tree had been planted on a leyline. Looking to restore the former glory of the lost tree, a Starbloom Cypress sapling has been planted in its place. There are claims this species of tree connects the realm of the dead with that of the living."},{"type":"p","text":"Credits - Arborhaven: @sachi_chiko on Twitter | Contributed by Elvario"},{"type":"h4","text":"Aegrizora"},{"type":"p","text":"Aegrizora: Aldo Domínguez on Artstation | Contributed by Elvario"},{"type":"h2","text":"Festival of Renewal"},{"type":"p","text":"Submitted by Serphan"},{"type":"p","text":"Season / Time of Year: The first day of Autumn."},{"type":"h3","text":"What It Celebrates / Purpose:"},{"type":"p","text":"As the autumn winds pluck the vibrant leaves from their branches, the residents of Arborhaven prepare for the Festival of Renewal. The citizens of Arborhaven travel to the forest near the city to perform a renewal ceremony for their souls. People express their frustrations, regrets, and burdens either out loud or in writing before burying them under the ground or throwing them into the wind. Similar to how autumn leaves need to fall to make room for new blooms, so must these harmful emotions and thoughts go in order to make room for the positivity to sprout in the new season."},{"type":"p","text":"The renewal allows people to let go of all the negativity that weighs them down and free their souls. The significance of this festival is to cleanse the spirit and release the soul from negativity that corrupts and holds it down, much like Aegrizora's release from prison."},{"type":"h3","text":"How They Celebrate / Traditions:"},{"type":"p","text":"Citizens travel to the forest for the renewal ceremony. This can be done with groups or individually. Oftentimes, people will attend with their families or friends."},{"type":"p","text":"Written confessions are placed on paper crafted from the leaves of the previous year, which can be found quite easily in the marketplace."},{"type":"p","text":"At night, blue and golden lanterns are released to honor the light of the heroes who helped free Aegrizora."},{"type":"p","text":"A popular game includes hiding and finding glowing orbs around the ancient tree. When you find one, you can break it to retrieve a sweet treat from inside."},{"type":"p","text":"There is a harvest feast paired with spiced drinks and sweets. This is just a joyful celebration of being clean and looking forward to the future. Not to mention a celebration of Aegrizora's release."},{"type":"h3","text":"Festival Scene:"},{"type":"p","text":"At dawn on the first day of Autumn, blending with the smell of roasted nuts and the smoke of the fires lit in preparation for the night's feast, blue and gold lanterns bathe the city of Arborhaven in a sacred light. Carrying satchels of the traditional confession papers, large leaves, or just the spirit of their tongue, the townspeople come together garbed in warm colors to mirror the autumn delights of the ancient tree that lies in the center of their great city."},{"type":"p","text":"People travel to the heart of the forest, and there, each person lets go of their confessions, letting the wind scatter them, or bury them at the roots, after whispering faint voices into it. The burdens are believed to fade with the warm Autumn wind, leaving the soul light, clean, and unbothered."},{"type":"p","text":"Following the renewal, the people return to Arborhaven, where a sea of blue and golden lights illuminates the night. They dance until the stars give way to dawn, filling the streets with laughter, games, and music in celebration of their refreshed spirits. Songs of legend and triumph fill the air as tables brim with rich food, sweet treats, and spiced drinks."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Kananto Village[1]"},{"type":"p","text":"A fortified village located by the northern borders of Ryke. The village now lies abandoned after the undead murdered all its inhabitants. Currently, the village is overrun and inhabited by monsters."},{"type":"p","text":"Credits - Cliff Childs @cliffsconcepts | Contributed by Elvario"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Kirkwall[1][2]"},{"type":"p","text":"A village close to the Ryke-Eastern Empire border. Situated just before the [Border Hill]; the Village is on the cusp of becoming a Town. Although industry is lacking, the agricultural scene is actually quite prosperous. Nearby, in the forests of Kirkwall, is a small village of elves."},{"type":"p","text":"Credits - Forge of Empires (Game) | Contributed by Uasal"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Border Hill"},{"type":"p","text":"Located on the eastern border of the [Caelia Barony], Sadek County of Ryke is a military outpost severely lacking fortifications. The closest one can get to the ancient battlefield without entering is the East. A single stone tower, surrounded by natural cliff walls to funnel enemies."},{"type":"p","text":"Credits - TBD | Contributed by Uasal"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Looming Circles"},{"type":"p","text":"Ancient ruins of a civilization that time had long forgotten. Who, or what, made these impossibly large, impending rings is believed to be unknown to even the oldest of spirits. Some say they are meant to be features of something, others say they are gateways to splendour, yet the true purpose of these structures remains elusive."},{"type":"p","text":"Credits - Luka Mivsek on Artstation | Contributed by Elvario"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Osun[1][2][3]"},{"type":"p","text":"The capital city of Sadek County; located in the north-western part of the county. The citizens are kind and welcoming in nature. Various small markets and stalls line the city’s streets. This is also where festivals are sometimes held in praise of the God of the Sun, Leilosis. This is also where the residence of the count is located, notable for its [Sun Court] which acts as a 'throne' room for holding audiences, and the [Round Table], which was once the base of operations and heart of the former count, Linneus Light's, [Order]; yet has now been abandoned and repurposed."},{"type":"p","text":"Credits - @LightBox라이트박스 on Artstation | Contributed by Elvario"},{"type":"h4","text":"Streets Of Osun"},{"type":"p","text":"@Kotakan on Artstation"},{"type":"h4","text":"Sun Court"},{"type":"p","text":"Credit TBD"},{"type":"h4","text":"Round Table"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - The Underbelly"},{"type":"p","text":"This large, almost otherworldly city, located directly beneath Ryken, is aptly named the Underbelly. Inhabited by criminals and fueled by bloodshed, this place has commonly been called 'Ryken's darker half'. Where Ryken is the capital belonging to Ryke's nobility and law-abiding citizens, the Underbelly is considered the capital for Ryke's dishonorable and chaotic outcasts."},{"type":"p","text":"Now offering debauchery with a cheeky new name: the Full Cheeks restaurant is considered the most 'high class' restaurant in the Underbelly. Equal opportunity cheek stuffing can be found here. Oh, and they have food too. (Source)"},{"type":"h3","text":"The Bloody Defiance"},{"type":"p","text":"Located within The Underbelly, this arena perfectly symbolized the violent and lawless nature that makes the city beneath Ryken its 'darker half'. Within these stone walls, looked upon by towering statues and zealous spectators, combatants shed their blood. This is where the strong rule. This is where the weak go to die."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - ??? | Contributed by Elvario"},{"type":"h4","text":"Legend - Auregnog's Amulet"},{"type":"p","text":"Within the shadows of the Underbelly, below Ryken, a legend persists through the whispers of those who believe. Rumors of an amulet leading to a magical prison, and vault, used by the former nobles of Ryke from the earliest days on the continent. Believers claim it was used more recently by Auregnog, legendary former leader of the Underbelly who was known as 'The Champion', though the legend offers no clues to the whereabouts of the amulet or Auregnog currently."},{"type":"h4","text":"Secret Prison"},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - Bezduch"},{"type":"h4","text":"Auregnog, \"The Champion\""},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - AnttiHako"},{"type":"p","text":"NPC - Lykra"},{"type":"p","text":"Since Auregnog's defeat, she has taken the title of \"The Champion\" and currently reigns over the Underbelly. Despite a tainted past, she holds tentative control of the unruly populace. She warded off a recent attack on the Underbelly, garnering her the respect of many."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Kronum Village"},{"type":"p","text":"With the forests of Ryken to the west, and the Paizu Mountains to the east, Kronum sat at the edge of the Glattzdan Hills and was no stranger to defending itself from the various monsters that saw fit to try and nab livestock from them from time to time."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Yemaya Ruins"},{"type":"p","text":"The former city of Yemaya, located in the Caelia Barony in the Sadek County of Ryke, which was burnt down into ruins. However, It is now being rebuilt and recovering with the current population of a village.[1]"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Stonewall, Seat of Caelia Barony in Sadek County"},{"type":"p","text":"Stonewall Castle serves as the residence of Baron Regula Caelia. Its central location within the barony and fortified walls make it an effective location for the seat of power. Within its walls it features all the staples to sustain medieval life, including a barracks, armory, and smithy."},{"type":"h4","text":"NPCs"},{"type":"p","text":"Aldwin - Mayor and elder of Stonewall."},{"type":"p","text":"Ezekiel Hayward - Guard captain in Stonewall of the Caelia Barony."},{"type":"p","text":"Gobán - Blacksmith of Stonewall. Pictured with his daughter, Aileen."},{"type":"p","text":"Hestia - Owner of the Tavern and Inn of Stonewall. Ex-wife of Berk in Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"Saffron - Store owner in Stonewall who has severe mood switches between being on or off the job."},{"type":"p","text":"Sven - Militia leader and woodcutter/carpenter in Stonewall."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Lupinvale Town"},{"type":"p","text":"Lupinvale is a town lost to time that was founded a few years after Ryke. Visitor that have escaped have recorded the village seemingly triggers an onslaught of hallucinations. The remains of Lupinvale is believed to be cursed."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Bloody Bohemia"},{"type":"p","text":"Built on the bones of the former circus troupe known as 'Bloodslayer's Menagerie', Bloody Bohemia is a ramshackle encampment that was hastily built and poorly maintained. It is comprised of a group of trailers, cages, and a singular circus tent, which survived the demise of the Menagerie. After the execution of their former ringmaster, a few of the more destitute and physically disabled sideshow “freaks” banded together and claimed the one remaining circus tent and a few immobile living trailers and empty cages as their own, erecting a small camp outside Sootspire with financial support and law enforcement provided by Baroness Regula. The Baroness's contribution has created a foundation on which the remaining crew and newcomers may create a new, friendlier, circus."},{"type":"p","text":"Perhaps a savvy businessman or visionary artist might transform Bloody Bohemia into a wholesome or upscale entertainment venue, though it seems just as likely a criminal element or unscrupulous individual may return it to the kind of blighted shantytown freakshow it was as BloodSlayer’s Menagerie."},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Kruhrin Village"},{"type":"p","text":"NPC info here"},{"type":"p","text":"Kruhrin, also known as \"the Village of Three Bears\", lies in the mountains on Ryke's eastern border. The village is spread across three terraces carved out on top of each other into the side of a lesser mountain. The lowest terrace is the common area where guests are housed in the sole inn inside the village, while the topmost tier has the guard barracks and town hall where the members of the council and esteemed guests are kept more comfortable. The village as a whole features sturdy architecture with slightly larger dimensions for the tall, hefty frames of the bearkin."},{"type":"p","text":"The populace of Kruhrin is predominantly bearkin, all of which migrated to their present location from the Republic at the end of the war 50 years ago. The ones that led this exodus, Lady Bao, Master Jia, Misha, and Sifu Akim, became leaders in the village. After experiencing a divine encounter, Akim separated himself and a handful of followers to go deeper into the mountains and establish a dojo and shrine to the bearkin deity known as Torben the Alpha and his esteemed right hand named Orson. The remaining three leaders presided over Kruhrin village as a council of three, each member embodying one of three principles: strength, wisdom, and cunning."},{"type":"p","text":"Orson's Feast: Kruhrin holds an annual week-long festival called Orson's Feast. Throughout the week, animals are butchered and roasted en masse to feed the bearkin and any guests that arrive. Contests are held on three separate days, each dedicated to trials based on the three pillars of strength, wisdom, and cunning. The winners of these contests are strongly considered as possible replacements should one of the councilbears become unable to fulfill their office. On the final day of the feast, a pilgrimage is made by the faithful from Kruhrin out to the dojo managed by Sifu Akim. About midday, villagers and those at the dojo then form a procession that climbs a certain rise to the appointed location where they commune with Orson."},{"type":"p","text":"Recent Events"},{"type":"p","text":"A mysterious plague swept through Kruhrin resulting in many casualties (Source)"},{"type":"p","text":"Lady Bao and Master Jia were replaced respectively by Beni, the rabbitkin former aide to the council, and Beh'zig, the local bearkin tinkerer (Source)"},{"type":"h1","text":"Caelia Barony"},{"type":"h1","text":"Caelia Barony"},{"type":"subtitle","text":"Country of Ryke, Sadek County"},{"type":"p","text":"Caelia Barony, is the smallest barony in Sadek County. It is governed by Baroness Regula Caelia."},{"type":"p","text":"After purchase of the [Healthy Barony] asset, it now includes the basics:"},{"type":"p","text":"Loyal mayors and leadership over the villages and towns of the Barony that see to the day to day and carry out the will of the baroness."},{"type":"p","text":"Defence - your walls and defence will be workable. Not the best, but not destroyed or crumbling. Men at arms to use them and defend them as well. Mostly locals trained to be soldiers with some being militia or mercenary forces to supplement, but not much."},{"type":"p","text":"Money - your fields produce healthy crops, you have skilled artisans like smiths, carpenters and weavers in the domain. You are connected to trade routes that are safe enough for the times and functioning markets to sell Barony production and bring in outside goods."},{"type":"p","text":"Religious groups sanctioned by Ryke can operate in the area with some degree of security and fellowship."},{"type":"p","text":"Minimum education is available so nobles can lead, crafters can craft and everyone can understand and know the decrees coming down from the baroness."},{"type":"p","text":"You have functional roads or routes between settlements in the Barony. Storage places for siege or hard times or general asset management, clean water sources."},{"type":"p","text":"Enough funds for the occasional festival or local tradition. Local Guilds like merchant, crafters, or adventurers. At least 1 inn or tavern in most settlements."},{"type":"p","text":"At least one healthy natural resource like your planting fields. Others may need extra work if that Barony wants to expand."},{"type":"p","text":"Law and order needs to be good enough folk to acknowledge and uphold the decrees of local or baron rules and laws."},{"type":"p","text":"Healers of some form are present in the Barony. Generally at least one per major village or town."},{"type":"p","text":"Means of negotiation trades and treaties with neighbours."},{"type":"p","text":"Locations:"},{"type":"p","text":"Capital Town Stonewall – population ~600\nA walled town in the middle of barony. Known for its keep and for being the general 'hub' of the barony."},{"type":"p","text":"Village Sootspire – population ~250\nA fairly large mining village in the north-east of the barony. Known for its mountain and its tough and large inhabitants."},{"type":"p","text":"Village/Town Kirkwall – population ~???\nA farming village in the south-east of the barony. Known for its Hunters, its advanced agriculture and its odd two-mayor political system."},{"type":"p","text":"City Ruins/Village Yemaya – population ~100\nThe ruins for a former city in the north-west of the barony, currently lived in by only a few people. Known for being the location where the Fell Blight happened."},{"type":"p","text":"More main locations to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Stonewall\nCountry of Ryke, Sadek County, Caelia Barony, Capital Town: Stonewall.\nFrom: Cyrili, the Farming Hamlet | The Fantasy Sandbox\nThe walled capital town in the middle of barony. Known for its keep and for being the general 'hub' of the barony.\nFeatured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – An RP introducing the Capital Town and some of its key NPC's."},{"type":"p","text":"Our Battle Shalt Be Legendary! – An RP detailing the legendary battle between Ethel and Aria."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Starting point of an RP regarding the baroness' flight lessons and a visit to the mining village Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"Treasure in Ruins Starting and end point in an RP visiting the ruins of Yemaya to look for rumoured treasure."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Burgers – The up and coming chef Todo Sawl get his franchise of burgers going in Hestia's tavern, The Keg."},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Trouble – Advisor of Caelia Retili Loxinofican is tasked to test and supervise a meeting between the (unofficial) mayor Aldwin from Stonewall and (acting) mayor Benjamin from Yemaya as they discuss the option of sending extra aid to Yemaya."},{"type":"p","text":"Nice To Meat You – Stonewall's butcher, Erkan Flann, challenged Todo Sawl to cook a variety of meat dishes from rare meats."},{"type":"p","text":"[Isekai Hell]'s Kitchen – Todo Sawl is ready to settle down, but before he can do so, he has to deal with a sudden influx of chefs from all around the world that are striving to learn from him as his sous-chef."},{"type":"p","text":"A Spearheaded Encounter - Seth Leventis encounters Janja Berger and Ethel."},{"type":"p","text":"Beauty's In The Eye Of The Beholder - Ryan Kylieth is out for sketching lessons with his girlfriend Aileen."},{"type":"p","text":"Definitely Not a Drinking Contest – Zuì Dàmāo joins an event in the Keg."},{"type":"p","text":"A Mother's Advise - Amanda Steelhaven has a conversation with Rosalia."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Reforged – A Slice of Life RP displaying the results of Regula's [Healthy Barony] purchase, including placing down Ringo's shrine and forging some gear for folk."},{"type":"p","text":"Heaven Let Your Light Sh(r)ine Down – Simple RP about fixing up Ringo's shrine."},{"type":"p","text":"A Bathhouse Is For The Greater Good! – RP attempting to start work on a Bathhouse by gathering materials in Sootspire Mine with Regula and Amanda Steelhaven."},{"type":"p","text":"(Caelia Barony) – It's A Matter of Faith – RP about Regula gathering her allies to help convince some Ryke clergy that she's not starting up a cult."},{"type":"p","text":"Hammer-on quality. – RP about Regula and Ryan Kylieth setting up some business deals for the barony."},{"type":"p","text":"A Tithe! A Tithe! My Shrine for a Tithe! – RP about mending relation with the church after cult accusations by making the money roll. Mostly takes place in Ryken, but is about the shrine in Stonewall and the stir it caused."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Associated Locations Images."},{"type":"p","text":"Aldwin's Living Room – Living room of the acting mayor of Stonewall."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness' Chambers – The baroness' personal room in the Stonewall Keep."},{"type":"p","text":"Bloody Delicious – A butchery located next to the General Store, ran by Erkan Flann."},{"type":"p","text":"Farmer's Cabin – A cabin a bit outside the city walls, home of Gwenith."},{"type":"p","text":"Forge in Stonewall – A forge ran by Gobán and his daughter Aileen."},{"type":"p","text":"Just Outside of Stonewall – An open field, sometimes used for duelling."},{"type":"p","text":"The Keg – A tavern and inn ran by Hestia and her daughter Amika."},{"type":"p","text":"Regula's Forge – A private forge owed by the baroness, located in the keep."},{"type":"p","text":"Rosalia's Room – The baroness' mother's room in the Stonewall Keep."},{"type":"p","text":"Stables – Behind the inn/tavern, owned by Hestia, but used by most folk in the town."},{"type":"p","text":"The Twice Flipped Coin – A general store ran by Saffron."},{"type":"p","text":"Training Grounds – A training area used by the guards and militia, behind Stonewall's Keep."},{"type":"p","text":"Associated NPC's"},{"type":"p","text":"Aileen"},{"type":"p","text":"Aldwin"},{"type":"p","text":"Amika"},{"type":"p","text":"Erkan Flann"},{"type":"p","text":"Ethel"},{"type":"p","text":"Ezekiel Hayward"},{"type":"p","text":"Gobán"},{"type":"p","text":"Gwenith"},{"type":"p","text":"Hestia"},{"type":"p","text":"Rosalia"},{"type":"p","text":"Saffron"},{"type":"p","text":"Sherwood"},{"type":"p","text":"Sven"},{"type":"p","text":"Aileen\nFull Image & Source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://rick_dj.artstation.com/projects/3dvyDg"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nShe was born and raised in Stonewall, where she learned blacksmithing work from her father Gobán. Her mother died when she was young, but she had two uncles (triplets with her father) to help look after her."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:\nRelatively shy and prefers to stay more passive in bigger crowds. Loves to adventure and explore in her free time. When someone gets under her skin too much or gets her to panic, her first instinct tends to be to try hitting them with her trusted hammer."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"She likes blacksmithing and would gladly help people learn the basics."},{"type":"p","text":"Having another girl to talk with, regarding love affairs, to see how to bring her relationship with Ryan Kylieth to a new level."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – The RP in which her father slingshotted her into a relation with Ryan Kylieth."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – An RP where her relationship with Ryan Kylieth got more serious."},{"type":"p","text":"Kirkwall, Baroness who? – The RP where Ryan Kylieth officially became her boyfriend!"},{"type":"p","text":"Nice To Meat You – Was a judge on Todo Sawl's meat cooking challenge."},{"type":"p","text":"Beauty's In The Eye Of The Beholder – After having been separated for a while, she decides to surprise her boyfriend Ryan Kylieth with a date just outside Stonewall."},{"type":"p","text":"Aldwin"},{"type":"p","text":"Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Ezume Kichirô"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nAn older man who lived most of his life in the barony. He's always tethered between positions of symbolic and actual power and currently functions as the acting mayor of Stonewall."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:\nHe's known for bing a bit of a schemer, always looking for new intrigue and never shy to voice his opinions. Whilst he's not a bad person, he often gives off the sense that he's plotting something potentially bad."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Listening to the latest news regarding political intrigue whilst enjoying a cup of tea is always a welcome option. He's also eager to voice his opinions on political topics and might give (potentially useful) advice to those that entertain him."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – Had a short run-in with Retili Loxinofican leaving a a less than ideal first impression."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Offered Retili Loxinofican some information as a peace offering and to further embellish the records of his family's history in the barony."},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Trouble – Discusses sending additional aid to Yemaya with mayor Benjamin, under supervision (and being tested by) Retili Loxinofican."},{"type":"p","text":"Definitely Not a Drinking Contest – Ended up joining an event that was definitely not a drinking contest with Zuì Dàmāo joining in."},{"type":"p","text":"Amika\nSpoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: cute fairy and shena the draw (elona) drawn by harusame_(rueken) | Danbooru"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nDaughter of Hestia and Berk. Runs the tavern/inn in Stonewall together with her mother, after the latter divorced."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:\nShe takes after her mother in both looks and personality. Always eager to chat with (paying) customers and giving them her advice to the best of her extent."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"A good person to run into after a long day of work, winding down in the tavern, trying some drinks, striking up a conversation about anything or nothing."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – Served Retili Loxinofican and his men some of the tavern's ale."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Burgers – Together with her mother, she helps Todo Sawl get his franchise of burgers going, whilst he helps them earn more in their tavern."},{"type":"p","text":"[Isekai Hell]'s Kitchen – She's asked to help Todo Sawl as a judge for those competing to become his new sous-chef."},{"type":"p","text":"Ethel\nFull Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Ironlily"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nTrainee guard in Stonewall. Self-proclaimed 'Guardian of Life' and 'Defender of the Stonewall'. Has some strong defensive ability, but is rather clumsy when attacking."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:\nShe has an odd, medieval-ish speech pattern and tends to live in her own (fantasy) world. She might've been dropped a little hard on her head as a kid."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Always looking for new challengers to duel with!"},{"type":"p","text":"Takes a quick liking to those indulging her in her fantasies and odd manner of speech."},{"type":"p","text":"If OOC time allows, could be used to practice Effectiveness Rules on both ends (similar as to 'Our Battle Shalt Be Legendary!)."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – Declared Aria to be her rival."},{"type":"p","text":"Our Battle Shalt Be Legendary! – Had an amazingly epic battle with her rival Aria that she ended up losing to."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Joined the others in their journey to Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Burgers – Wanted to challenge Todo Sawl to a duel, but fell for his burgers and pledged to protect his craft instead."},{"type":"p","text":"Nice To Meat You – Was a judge on Todo Sawl's meat cooking challenge."},{"type":"p","text":"A Spearheaded Encounter – Ran into Seth Leventis whilst arguing with Janja Berger."},{"type":"p","text":"Ezekiel Hayward\nFull Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Edmond Trevelyan by slugette on DeviantArt"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nGrew up in the capital, became a soldier and made some promotions until he got promoted to Guard Captain in the barony. Has now held that position for a few years and is still making the most of it."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:\nNormally a fairly calm and rational person, can be strict when needed. Not one to rush into things."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"With his heart broken by a love he knows he can't attain, he might need some professional advice."},{"type":"p","text":"He's also always eager to train new recruits to aid the barony (the go-to person for barony guard/soldier connections)."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Our Battle Shalt Be Legendary! – Showed up to fall in love with Aria at first sight."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Joined the others in their journey to Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"Definitely Not a Drinking Contest – Ended up joining an event that was definitely not a drinking contest with Zuì Dàmāo joining in."},{"type":"p","text":"Gobán"},{"type":"p","text":"Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://rick_dj.artstation.com/projects/3dvyDg"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nBlacksmith in Stonewall. Never spoke much, but spoke even less after he lost his hand and stopped speaking almost entirely after he lost one of his wife Works the smithy with his daughter Aileen. Has two triplet brothers (one in Sootspire, one in Kirkwall)."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:\nHe rarely speaks and shows very little emotion."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"He might indicate someone walking in to smith something to prove themselves worthy. With his daughter's hand already having been handed out, it's unclear what they'd be worthy of, other than some hints or of seeing the man himself at work."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – Had Ryan Kylieth smith something to prove he was worthy of earning his daughter's hand."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Send off Ryan Kylieth to find (and charm) his daughter."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Burgers – Gave Todo Sawl's burger extremely high praise by spending an entire word on calling them 'good'."},{"type":"p","text":"Gwenith\nFull Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://rebeccaoborn.artstation.com/projects/ox3RO"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nUsed to do lots of farming work, including as an orchardist, through-out various areas in Ryke. Recently settled in the barony to keep doing research."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:\nAn overall pleasant woman that might be a little rough around the edges at times, but who means well."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Always willing to have someone over to try her herbal tea types or to discuss agricultural research."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Queen, The Tank, The Sword and their Weapon Transport – Was working as an orchardist heading for the capital."},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – Gave Amanda Steelhaven some advice on agriculture and some tea."},{"type":"p","text":"Hestia\nFull Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: shena the draw (elona) drawn by harusame_(rueken) | Danbooru"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nRuns the tavern/inn in Stonewall with her daughter, after divorcing her husband Berk."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:\nAlways eager to chat with (paying) customers and giving them her advise to the best of her extend."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"A good person to run into after a long day of work, winding down in the tavern, trying some drinks, striking up a conversation about anything or nothing."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Asked Micah to take care of her horse, Laverne."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Burgers – Together with her daughter, she helps Todo Sawl get his franchise of burgers going, whilst he helps them earn more in their tavern."},{"type":"p","text":"[Isekai Hell]'s Kitchen – She's asked to help Todo Sawl as a judge for those competing to become his new sous-chef."},{"type":"p","text":"Definitely Not a Drinking Contest – Ended up hosting an event that was definitely not a drinking contest with Zuì Dàmāo joining in."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Reforged – Getting a lot of sudden visitors in the morning."},{"type":"p","text":"Rosalia\nFull Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Adelheid"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nMother to Regula Caelia. Worked as a prostitute in Ryke, until her daughter got the nobility title, after which she moved over and retired."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:\nOne of the kindest souls you'll ever find. Always willing to offer a listening ear, a hug or a few kind words of comfort and advise."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Always there to comfort and help those in need, loves to socialize with those in the barony. Also gives pretty good fashion advise."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Mother's Day – A day spent with her daughter Regula and Aria."},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – Travelled to Stonewall accompanied by Pierre Rothel."},{"type":"p","text":"Definitely Not a Drinking Contest – Ended up joining an event that was definitely not a drinking contest with Zuì Dàmāo joining in."},{"type":"p","text":"Saffron\nFull Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: sheikah by onisuu on DeviantArt"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:\nHer grandmother (Prisca) moved to Ryke with her mother (Tisiphone) after her father died by East Empire soldiers. She herself was raised in Sootspire, but she had the option to take over a store in Stonewall and went for it. Her brother Sherwood works as a scout. She's been working the in The Twice Flipped Coin for a few years now."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"She's extremely business-oriented and 'boring' and 'cold' whilst on the job."},{"type":"p","text":"When not working, she's curious, extroverted and a pretty nice person."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:\nShe loves to learn about new things, either for profit or just out of curiosity. She knows a lot about all sorts of trade going on in the barony, more so than folk might assume at first."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – Had a short conversation with Retili Loxinofican."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Had a long conversation with Teuihua and later met the group again in Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Burgers – She sold some goods to Todo Sawl and later enjoyed his salad and onion rings."},{"type":"p","text":"Definitely Not a Drinking Contest – Ended up joining an event that was definitely not a drinking contest with Zuì Dàmāo joining in."},{"type":"p","text":"Sherwood\nSpoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From:"},{"type":"p","text":"https://www.artstation.com/artwork/D59q1n"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"His grandmother (Prisca) moved to Ryke with his mother (Tisiphone) after his father was murdered by East Empire soldiers. He himself was raised in Sootspire, but he later joined the guards as a scout whilst his sister works in the general store Stonewall. Works together with the Adventurer's Guild a lot."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"Extremely shy, but eventually knows how to talk when he gets to know someone well enough."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Wants to learn to be a little less shy."},{"type":"p","text":"Can teach people a lot about the area, navigation, survival or nature."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – Made his awkward first introduction."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Was asked to join the group on their travel to Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Sven"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From:"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"Born and raised in Stonewall. Decided to join the militia at a young age, despite working as a carpenter and logger almost full-time. His considerable strength eventually made him militia leader."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"He's a rather cold and distant person, but might warm up to people should they earn his respect. The latter can be done through carpentry or strength."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Those wanting to train with the strongest might want to challenge him, but he'd rather teach folk wood-working."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Start Of Something New – Met some folk and just told them to get out the way."},{"type":"p","text":"Nice To Meat You – Was a judge on Todo Sawl's meat cooking challenge."},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Reforged – Helping out with the shrine as a carpenter."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Aldwin's Living Room"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall – Aldwin's House – Living Room"},{"type":"p","text":"From: HD wallpaper: Fantasy, Room, Fireplace | Wallpaper Flare"},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness' Chambers"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall – Baroness' Chambers."},{"type":"p","text":"From: From court to castle: The magnificent film sets of Mary Queen of Scots - Film and Furniture"},{"type":"p","text":"Bloody Delicious"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Stonewall - Butchery."},{"type":"p","text":"From: Medieval meat shop, illustration Stock Illustration"},{"type":"p","text":"Farmer's Cabin"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall – Farm."},{"type":"p","text":"From: Download wallpapers by subject art"},{"type":"p","text":"Forge in Stonewall"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall – Forge."},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://www.artstation.com/artwork/0nnVRy"},{"type":"p","text":"Just Outside of Stonewall"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Just outside of Capital Town: Stonewall."},{"type":"p","text":"From: Grasslands by JKRoots on DeviantArt"},{"type":"p","text":"The Keg"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall – Tavern."},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://i10.photobucket.com/albums/a147/Darsunne/0a55608e9d52edec15d4c6455736ec45_zpste7hezy9.jpg"},{"type":"p","text":"Regula's Forge"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall, Keep, Regula's Forge."},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://mchiarag.artstation.com/projects/1ZoG3"},{"type":"p","text":"Rosalia's Room"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall – Rosalia's Room."},{"type":"p","text":"From: prompthunt: interior illustration, a medieval fantasy lodging room, bed, window, washbasin, mirror"},{"type":"p","text":"Stables in Stonewall"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall – Stables."},{"type":"p","text":"From: Whittengrove Stables"},{"type":"p","text":"The Twice Flipped Coin"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall – General Store “The Twice Flipped Coin”."},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://yangsh.artstation.com/projects/mq5GNd"},{"type":"p","text":"Training Grounds in Stonewall"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Capital Town: Stonewall – Training Grounds."},{"type":"p","text":"From: Medieval Training Yard"},{"type":"p","text":"Sootspire\nCountry of Ryke, Sadek County, Caelia Barony, Mining Village: Sootspire.\nA mining village at the foot of a mountain (which is ironically called Sootspire Hill).\nFeatured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"A Noble Hunt! – The late Count Light and some mercenaries slaughtered goblins raiding the village and defeated a dangerous beast in the nearby mountain forest."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – The baroness and her party visited the village and met some of its more (in)famous inhabitants."},{"type":"p","text":"A Bathhouse Is For The Greater Good! – RP attempting to start work on a Bathhouse by gathering materials in Sootspire Mine with Regula and Amanda Steelhaven."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Associated Locations Images."},{"type":"p","text":"Road to Sootspire – A long and rocky road between Stonewall and Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"The Ironbender – Sootspire's smithy, owned by Jarek."},{"type":"p","text":"Rockemead Ale – Sootspire's Tavern, owned by Berk."},{"type":"p","text":"Sootspire Mine – Sootspire's main source of income. Most people work here or in jobs related to this mine."},{"type":"p","text":"Tree of Promises – A tree that grew atop the grave of the Fae mayor's son. Every so often, the tree grows fruits that are shared between the Fae and Humans as a symbol of their friendship and cooperation."},{"type":"p","text":"More locations to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Associated NPC's"},{"type":"p","text":"Berk"},{"type":"p","text":"Ebenezer"},{"type":"p","text":"Hallr"},{"type":"p","text":"Janja Berger & Cayde Ramminger"},{"type":"p","text":"Jarek"},{"type":"p","text":"Prisca"},{"type":"p","text":"Tisiphone"},{"type":"p","text":"More NPC's to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Road to Sootspire"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Road to Sootspire"},{"type":"p","text":"From:"},{"type":"p","text":"https://www.pinterest.jp/pin/42502790218844422/"},{"type":"p","text":"The Ironbender"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Sootspire: Smithy"},{"type":"p","text":"]"},{"type":"p","text":"From:"},{"type":"p","text":"Moradin"},{"type":"p","text":"Rockemead Ale"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Sootspire: Tavern"},{"type":"p","text":"From:"},{"type":"p","text":"Warm lit friendly medieval fantasy tavern inn, lanterns, concept art interior, adventuring dungeons and dragons. Stock Illustration"},{"type":"p","text":"Sootspire Mine"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Sootspire: Mine"},{"type":"p","text":"From:"},{"type":"p","text":"HD desktop wallpaper: Video Game, Planet Alcatraz download free picture #705128"},{"type":"p","text":"Tree of Promises"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Sootspire"},{"type":"p","text":"From:"},{"type":"p","text":"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/e7/42/ef/e742ef43ed2e561bb96785201e671598.jpg"},{"type":"p","text":"Berk"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Dogan"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"Ex-husband of Hestia (owner of Stonewall's Tavern), father of Amika. His wife left him with his daughter due to no longer wanting to live in Sootspire, deeming it too unsafe and being unhappy there. He stayed behind on his own."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"He likes to be seen as a tough guy and isn't shy about giving off such vibes. Talking about his wife is a very sensitive topic. He does love to roast meats and is amazing at it, which is probably earning him more coin than selling booze."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Might spark up a conversation with those that manage to come across well enough and/or those that appreciate his roasted meats. Sometimes shares some rumours about what's going on in Sootspire. He knows extremely much about everything that's going on around the entirety of Caelia Barony and will keep talking once someone gets him to start."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Talked to some people and told Retili Loxinofican a whole lot about everyone in Sootspire and then some."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Ebenezer"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Mine"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"He worked as a miner in Sootspire, but found his real passion when he joined in with Count Light to slaughter goblins. He especially enjoyed the order to kill the woman and children. Now he mines enough to get by, but spends just as much time trying to look for any remaining goblins to kill."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"People often smell him before they see him. He's foolish enough not to commit crimes against humans, but eager to get brutally violent against [monsters] whenever he can. He loves to make that clear to just about anyone willing to listen."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Always down to have some folk accompanying him on a goblin hunt. Eager to tell them all about it as well."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Made a 'great' first impression on Amanda Steelhaven."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Hallr"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://soijohn.artstation.com/projects/0XVmey"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"Works as a prospector and miner. Is considered extremely talented at his job and ended up being one of the figures with relatively high authority in the village. He worked in other places through-out Ryke as well, but found the most promising place to stay around to be Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"He's insanely strong and likes others that are as well. He doesn't like weak folk. He can be short and grumpy, but has a mostly 'good' heart to him."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"He's always willing to teach folk a few mining or prospecting tricks and take them to the mines or mountain. However, his real passion is displays of strength. He's always down to duke it out in a weight lifting match or to provide folk some feedback."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Met the party travelling to Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"Nice To Meat You – Was a judge on Todo Sawl's meat cooking challenge."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Janja Berger"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Anila"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"A sheep-girl shepherd that loves her job and flock. She used to herd her sheep north of Sadek County, but moved further south after an encounter with a gnoll. Now mostly herds her flock in Caelia Barony, between Sootspire and Stonewall. She'd surprisingly strong and capable of fighting off threats to her and her flock."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"Cheerful, eager to chat with new folk after a long day alone in the field."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Occasionally asks adventurers to help her deal with wolves, monsters or bandits that might threaten her flock. Also eager to sell wool, teach some shepherding or hang out in the middle of nowhere."},{"type":"p","text":"Cayde Ramminger"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://pixabay.com/illustrations/ram-sheep-horns-animal-mammal-7695726/"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"Born to become the hottest ram in the block. Named after a real hero and living up to the name."},{"type":"p","text":"Has a very high value as a breeding ram due to producing valuable enough offspring."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"Very protective of his flock. Janja is part of his flock."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Journey Through the Eastern Outskirts – Met a doggo priest and the alchemist Cayde and helped them deal with a dangerous gnoll."},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Met the party on their way to Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"A Spearheaded Encounter – Ran into Seth Leventis whilst arguing with Ethel."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Jarek"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: https://www.artstation.com/artwork/nYgL81"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"Triplet brother to Gobán and Bart and a smith. The only one to remain unmarried out of the three of them. He's always working on the equipment for Sootspire's mine and made a fair fortune from it, but doesn't even seem to consider retiring."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"Values his craft and nieces (Aileen and Cynthia) and not a whole lot else."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"He could always use help mass producing items for the mines, as it's relatively easy smithing work that gets boring quickly. He's also willing to show how to refine raw ores in turn."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Met the party at the Tree of Promises."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Prisca"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Witches - Coliandre"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"“Many years ago, long before any of you were born, I lived with my with my family in The See, on the border with Ryke. On an unfortunate day, we got captured by slavers, who tried to smuggle us through Ryke and into the East Empire. Their got stopped by my daughter in law, Tisiphone, who managed to free us in this very Barony. However, we learned that the slavers had already killed my son."},{"type":"p","text":"For a moment, our rage got the better of us. That day, my daughter in law and I swore we'd make all Humans pay for their crimes. We intended to destroy this village and any other, before we'd eventually be killed ourselves. However, just as we were about to start our slaughter, a tree grew from my sons remains. On it were flowers blooming more beautiful than any we'd ever seen, which soon turned into fruits sweeter than we'd ever tasted. That's when we knew. My son didn't want us to take vengeance against the humans. After all, why would he grow such a beautiful tree on the lands in which he was killed? Looking at the tree calmed us and set us straight. During the many years since then, we've lived here in harmony with one another instead. Today, like so many days before, the tree is once again blooming. A sign of my sons continuing wish for us to live in harmony. I'd like to ask you all, old residents and newcomers alike, to accept its fruits as a sign of our co-existence.”"},{"type":"p","text":"She is currently the acting mayor of Sootspire. She is the mother of Tisiphone and grandmother of Sherwood and Saffron."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"For an ancient Fae, she is relatively 'modern' in the sense that she can grasp Humans well. She is mostly known to be a kind old woman with great advise, but can be terrifying to those that threaten the well-being of her people."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"She's always willing to hear people out or impart her wisdom on them. She guards the 'Tree of Forgiving' planted on her son's grave, which sometimes grows fruit that is shared as a symbol of friendship. Visitors are often invited to partake and listen to her story. Or to listen to her stories in general. She has a fair few of them."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Met the baroness and her party and told them her story at the Tree of Promises."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Tisiphone"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From: original drawn by pigeon666 | Danbooru"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"She once lived in the See with her mother and (young) children, but her husband was killed by slavers whilst they were taken. She managed to kill the slavers and escape, but was about to go on a Human-murdering rampage when she was stopped by seeing her husband's remains grow a fruit-bearing tree. Still unable to let go of her past, she now wanders the border between Ryke and the East Empire to hunt down slavers, sworn to keep avenging her husband over and over again for as long as her Fae lifespan allows her to do so."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"She's forgiven humanity as a whole, but still searches out slavers to murder. She knows fully well to stay on the Ryke side of the border and has learned a fair few tricks to avoid criminal titles whilst doing her 'job', yet is still disliked by the East Empire for obvious reasons."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"She's always looking for people with a shared ideology, but doesn't respect one easily. She's an extremely strong warrior and might not be eager to hang with those that can't prove themselves to be the same. She'll go to great lengths to free slaves. Sometimes she puts out request to the Adventurers Guild to help with bandits."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Baroness, Take Flight! – Briefly met the baroness and her party at the Tree of Promises."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Yemaya\nCountry of Ryke, Sadek County, Caelia Barony, Village/City Ruins: Yemaya\nStill looking for a good image for Yemaya after the Fell Blight and planning to make some sort of map in the future.\nThe remains of what was once a city, Yemaya, now has the population of a small village left living in it.\nFeatured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"An Interlude Pt. 1 - One of the city's nobles brought a terrible curse, the Fell Blight, down upon the city. It spawned hostile creatures from other realms that endangered everyone and everything. After some battles and relief efforts, the city's balance was still in jeopardy, as many had died or were missing and one of the heroes, Michael ended up a murderer and vandal."},{"type":"p","text":"Project 10 – Michael successfully created a project to raise the dead and bring back a lot of the missing, yet this went a little too well, causing the entire Sol County to be split off from Ryke. The city suddenly boomed in population. Ryke was quick to react to it, by executing Count Light, excommunicating Michael, disbanding their Order, chasing out the cultists and quickly appointing new people to fully reincorporate the territory. After all these events, the city eventually got left abandoned by most, some fleeing Ryke along with the cultists, some returning to their homes, some unable to live there due to their homes not having been rebuilt, others still fearing that the Fell Blight lingers and even more people being unable to cope with the death of lord Light and excommunication of Michael."},{"type":"p","text":"The Postlude – A discussion happening before and after the above mentioned events."},{"type":"p","text":"Treasure in Ruins – Exploring some ruins in the city to find a treasure supposedly left there by previous nobles."},{"type":"p","text":"Knightly Duties (Or Something Similar) – Knight Siegfried goes to find and rescue some missing kids."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Associated Locations Images."},{"type":"p","text":"Small Side-Path – a small path connecting the road from Stonewall to Yemaya and from Stonewall to Sootspire. A great location for flight practice, picnics or herding sheep."},{"type":"p","text":"Road to Yemaya – the road between Stonewall and Yemaya, mostly goes through grasslands with some smaller patches of forest along the way."},{"type":"p","text":"Central Street – the ruins of some of the city centre. A hub and meeting place for those that remain in the city."},{"type":"p","text":"Dungeon Entrance – an impressive entrance to an underground maze, once used by the former nobles as trail ground, now lies mostly abandoned."},{"type":"p","text":"Treasure Room – a room that was fille with treasure and books on magic, before being discovered and emptied in Treasure in Ruins."},{"type":"p","text":"Yemaya Hillside – A relatively rough and beautiful landscape north of Yemaya."},{"type":"p","text":"More locations to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Associated NPC's"},{"type":"p","text":"Benjamin"},{"type":"p","text":"Crowly"},{"type":"p","text":"Eva"},{"type":"p","text":"Ratnam"},{"type":"p","text":"More NPC's to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Small Side-Path"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Road between Stonewall and Yemaya – Side-path in the direction of Sootspire"},{"type":"p","text":"From:"},{"type":"p","text":"Speedpaint 59 Motley Grass by RHADS on DeviantArt"},{"type":"p","text":"Road to Yemaya"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Between Stonewall and Yemaya"},{"type":"p","text":"From: HD fantasy path wallpapers | Peakpx"},{"type":"p","text":"Central Street"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia, Yemaya, City Centre"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Fantasy Ancient City Ruins HD wallpaper | Pxfuel"},{"type":"p","text":"Dungeon Entrance"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia, Yemaya, Below the City"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Thinking on Dungeon Fantasy Games"},{"type":"p","text":"Treasure Room"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryken, County of Sadek, Barony of Caelia. Yemaya, Maze, Treasure Room"},{"type":"p","text":"From: Fantasy Treasure/[Url][/Center] Images – Browse 0 Stock Photos, Vectors, and Video"},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Benjamin"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image & Source"},{"type":"p","text":"Source:"},{"type":"p","text":"https://www.artstation.com/artwork/b5aora"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"He once intended to start working for Baron Dashi as an experienced combat butler, but ended up in Yemaya after the latter retired. There, he witnessed the events throwing the city into ruins and ended up helping out with the aftermath. People started respecting his knowledge and skill enough to start considering him their mayor, so he has currently defaulted to being the acting mayor of Yemaya."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"He's a gentleman first and warrior second. However, he's proud to combine those whenever possible. He's not as much a natural mayor as he's a natural leader, so whilst his leadership is strong, his political intrigue is not."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"He's always willing to teach the art of being a combat butler or battle maid to those interest, be it the fighting part or the serving/etiquette parts."},{"type":"p","text":"Occasionally, he'll request some aid in keeping Yemaya's ruins clear of monsters through the adventurer's guild."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Treasure in Ruins – Met the party and discussed things with the baroness."},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Trouble – Discusses receiving additional aid for Yemaya with mayor Aldwin, under supervision (and being tested by) Retili Loxinofican."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Ratnam"},{"type":"p","text":"Spoiler: Full Image & Source"},{"type":"p","text":"Source:"},{"type":"p","text":"https://www.artstation.com/artwork/6bODl5"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"He's been working with the Adventurer's Guild as a ruins explorer for a long time, earning him some recognition and fame despite his somewhat unsocial attitude. Rumour has it that he got cursed by his own book, other rumours say he exchanged part of himself with a [beast] to make his book come alive. Other rumours state he's gotten cursed by a Fae cardinal. Whatever is true, it's clear he's rather odd, but also competent at his job."},{"type":"p","text":"He's currently going through the ruins of Yemaya, as there's much left of value in them to uncover and the source of the Fell Blight is still not fully uncovered."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"He's not the most social person, tending to be short and impatient. He also tends to forget giving others his name more often than not."},{"type":"p","text":"His book, called Elly, tends to start drooling a lot at the mention of Treasure."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"If there's new ruins or places to explore in the area that need a more experienced adventurer to tag along, there's a fair chance he'll be put on the mission. For better or worse."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Treasure in Ruins – Aided the group in their exploration of the maze below Yemaya."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Eva\nSpoiler: Full Image & Source"},{"type":"p","text":"(Ignore the bells.)"},{"type":"p","text":"Source:\nhttps://feheroes.fandom.com/wiki/Lethe:_Gallia's_Valkyrie"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"A Neko/Catgirl kid that, together with Crowly, grew up in an orphanage in Ryke. They were treated badly, so they ran away. They lived their lives as thieves for a while, but eventually tried turn their lives around to live more honestly in Caelia Barony, where they were hiding out in the ruins of Yemaya."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"She's curious, secretly likes it when people tug her tail, loves fish and can be rather mischievous. She likes to trick and mislead people. Considers Crowly her younger brother."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"She's always eager to learn more and hopes to become an adventurer one day."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Queen, The Tank, The Sword and their Weapon Transport – she tried to rob Regula and her party along with Crowly, but failed."},{"type":"p","text":"Treasure in Ruins – Was discovered in the first room of the maze below Yemaya, from where she and Crowly had been trying to get to the treasure. Joined the party for parts of the maze."},{"type":"p","text":"Knightly Duties (Or Something Similar) – Knight Siegfried goes looking for her after she goes missing."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Crowly\nSpoiler: Full Image & Source"},{"type":"p","text":"(Ignore the weapon.)"},{"type":"p","text":"Closest source I could find:\nhttps://nl.pinterest.com/pin/789044797200261164/"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"A Kenku kid that, together with Eva, grew up in an orphanage in Ryke. They were treated badly, so they ran away. They lived their lives as thieves for a while, but eventually tried turn their lives around to live more honestly in Caelia Barony, where they were hiding out in the ruins of Yemaya."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"He tends to echo what Eva says, but sometimes adds something new to a conversation. He's easily terrified of something."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"He'll tag along with whatever Eva does."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Queen, The Tank, The Sword and their Weapon Transport – he tried to rob Regula and her party along with Eva, but failed."},{"type":"p","text":"Treasure in Ruins – Was discovered in the first room of the maze below Yemaya, from where he and Eva had been trying to get to the treasure. Joined the party for parts of the maze."},{"type":"p","text":"Knightly Duties (Or Something Similar) – Knight Siegfried goes looking for him after he goes missing."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."},{"type":"p","text":"Kirkwall"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryke, Sadek County, Caelia Barony, Boarder Town: Sootspire."},{"type":"p","text":"Kirkwall is a Village on the Ryke and Eastern Kingdom border. Situated just before Boarder Hill the Village is on the cusp of becoming a Town in its own right. In fact many would argue it already should be recognised as a town but the internal divisions of the village have rendered this argument mute. With two mayors of very opposing views recognised within the village, it takes quite a lot of negotiation for pretty much anything to get done and with no oversight from the previous Baron or Lord the village has grown sporadically and in an unorthodox way."},{"type":"p","text":"Houses funnel in a line following a narrow gritty road that makes it nearly impossible for carts to navigate. Likewise, the industry is practically non-existent outside of a lone bakery and carpenters. Water is supplied by two wells. Although the industry is lacking the agricultural scene is actually quite prosperous."},{"type":"p","text":"Just outside of Kirkwall itself, there are currently four farms producing quite a bounty. Amanda Steelhaven introduced Crop Rotation to her family's farm several years ago and since then it has slowly been adopted by the other farms in the region allowing for the mass growth of Wheat, Barley, Turnips and Colver. Beef and Wool are also produced on the farms. This is Kirkwall's main source of income and food. In fact, Kirkwood has been making quite a tidy sum by trading excess food to the Highgrove Barony."},{"type":"p","text":"With that in mind lets touch on the current divide within the village. Kirkwall was ignored by the previous Baron and Count despite its tactical position and growth. Combine this with the fact that at the same time, the town received favourable trade deals with the Highgrove Barony as well as off-the-record relief efforts and you have your dilemma. Thats right, Kirkwall has begun to lose loyalty toward Celia Barony. On one hand, you have Mayor Kirk whose ancestors settled the city leading the pro-Celia side of things, and on the other, you have Mayor Levin. Both are very respected individuals within the community and both represent a future the people of Kirkwall wish to see brought to fruition."},{"type":"p","text":"Kirk wishes to see the village elevated to a town and industry expanded to better support the people and economy."},{"type":"p","text":"Levin wishes to see Kirkwall elevated to a town and brought into the Highgrove Barony, who have treated the village far more favorably. Though radical in design the plan to join Highgrove has a decent level of support and stands to net the village a sizable profit in all regards."},{"type":"p","text":"The people of Kirkwall are before all else a community. Everyone in Kirkwall knows one another and very little happens without knowledge of it spreading. Always keen to lend a hand the people of Kirkwall respect hard work and diligence above all else. If you need help with anything don't be shy to ask, you'll find many more than happy to do so! Just be sure you're giving it your best too, as the people of Kirkwall hate two things. Those that are lazy and those who lead without example."},{"type":"p","text":"Do you need help building a barn? Sure no problem! But you best be the first person on-site and the last to leave!"},{"type":"p","text":"Lastly let it be known that the people of Kirkwall are very welcoming to outsiders, and a very diverse bunch given the proximity to the border. That said, no amount of magical apparatus could compare to the Kirkwall survivance system that is the elderly. One wrong move, one slip up, one breach of trust or slight toward its inhabitants and the people of Kirkwall will show you just how terrifying they can be."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Kirk"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Kirk is one of two Mayors In Kirkwall. Unsurprisingly he is a descendent of the original founder of Kirkwall and as such his family is very well respected and trusted. He is the Grandfather of the 'Hunter's' current leader - George Ironclaw. Mayor Kirk is a friend of the Fey."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"A kind and wise old man, Mayor Kirk seldom says a lot but when he does you can count on it being of importance. The man is a good person at heart and looks out for all those in Kirkwall as though they were his family. He tends to bump heads with the other Mayor quite often though."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Kirk is sure to offer some words of advice to anyone in need of it during their stay in Kirkwall. They may not even realize who he is."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Levin"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Levin is one of two Mayors In Kirkwall. A calculating and shrewd old man Mayor Levin is the type to seek out a profit over all else. For that reason, he was entrusted as treasurer when the town went through its agricultural boom. Now an economic powerhouse within Caelia Barony, Kirkwall has Mayor Levin to thank for its financial prosperity and now close ties to the merchants guild."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"Calculating, shrewd, and blatantly rude. Mayor Levin is not a likable man but he is very good at what he does. Almost too good, so much so there are rumors floating around that he may be a puppet of sorts."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Mayor Levin is Likely to show himself when there is an opportunity to make money in Kirkwall or when large sums of money are being exchanged."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"Lydia Woodpine"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Local Lumberjack and Carpenter. Her Family has been the village Carpenters since its creation. A very well-respected individual who's deceivingly strong."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"A fun and upbeat kind of woman Lydia takes every day as it comes and is not the type to worry about the little things in life. She can get along with pretty much anyone and is very reliable when it comes to quality materials."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"If one gets lost in the woods and isn't met by an elf, it's likely Lydia who'll guide them back to town or save them from a pinch."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"TBD"},{"type":"p","text":"Cyntia Stroop"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Local Baker. An extremely rich woman by happenstance of the current industrial situation within the village who is very single and very ready to mingle. Very unlucky."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"A kind and caring individual Cynthia is a motherlike individual who will dote on anyone if given the chance. She is a hopeless romantic."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Cynthia is a very popular baker and so can be found at her bakery 9/10 times"},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"h4","text":"Fantasy - [Isekai Hell] (Caelia Barony) – Baroness, Take Flight!"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. Events take place a week after The Start Of Something New and Our Battle Shalt Be Legendary!. The pace is likely going to be roughly 48 hours per round, but might be quicker if certain people move faster..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"George Ironclaw"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"Leader of the village's hunters. George is essentially to Kirkwall what the guard captain is to Stonewall. An extremely strong ranger type George and his falcon 'Littlefoot' are the boogymen who those that do wrong in the area fear."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"A Flirtatious and roguish type of man. George is a hero to the people of Kirkwall and though he can cause quite a stir and was quite troublesome in his youth the man's cheeky and flirtatious mannerisms are what make him so easy to talk to. Despite his power, he remains a down-to-earth boy who can't help but ruin the tension of a serious situation. He can also be quite lazy at times."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Anyone committing serious crimes within the Kirkwall area will meet George eventually. That being said he often appears to flirt with pretty adventurers who have gotten lost on their way to Kirkwall. You know, to help them not be lost, not to hit on them, that's outrageous."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"Ash Wolfgang"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"Ash is the owner of the local tavern and an information broker"},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"A cautious type Ash is well able to decern those who mean good and bad with but a look. He is charismatic and well-able to keep a target locked in conversation regardless of the topic mentioned. He knows everything about the goings on in Kirkwall."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Anyone looking for Information, lodging, or a drink will find him at the 'Wolf's Rest Tavern'"},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"Nekomia Twobell"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"'Just a Merchant'"},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"Nekomia is an enigma but a very friendly one."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"Ask Uasal to play this character as she is of importance"},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"The Kirkwall Hunters"},{"type":"p","text":"Ashley, Fiona and Drew"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"The village's hunters and guardians. Directed by George these three hunters in particular are notable figures in the community. The sole reason farms such as those developed can remain unharmed by those animals or monsters that would wish to see them come undone. Ashley in particular is George's right hand."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"Ashley is a complex and cold character. Fiona a shy and reserved powerhouse. And Drew... Drew is... well he's very lazy but one hell of a trapper and shot."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"These three replace your general purpose guards but are each at least C Grade characters. With Ashley being a B."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"Border Hill"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryke, Sadek County, Caelia Barony, Kirkwall: Border with the East."},{"type":"p","text":"A Military outpost severely lacking fortifications. The closest one can get to the ancient battlefield without entering the East. A single stone tower, surrounded by natural cliff walls to funnel enemies."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"Elven Village of 'Kirkwall'"},{"type":"p","text":"Country of Ryke, Sadek County, Caelia Barony, Kirkwall: Deep within the Kirkwall Forest."},{"type":"p","text":"A small elven colony located in the Kirkwall forest. Isolationist by nature the elves keep to themselves and prefer to be left alone. Though not hostile by nature they are secretive and call the forest their domain. Only the 'Hunters' are permitted entry as well as Mayor Kirk and Cynthia the Baker. One should note that though Lydia is not and should not be permitted entry she often ends up within the village drinking with the inhabitants."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Graded - [Kirkwall Village] (Caelia Barony) – Kirkwall, Baroness who?"},{"type":"p","text":"This RP is part of the Isekai Hell universe. Check the links above to learn more about it. The pace is going to be roughly 48 hours per round with some leeway for circumstances arising. This RP will be an introduction to the Kirkwall Area All prepared information on npcs and the like will be..."},{"type":"p","text":"www.rpnation.com"},{"type":"p","text":"Erkan Flann\nSpoiler: Full Image and source"},{"type":"p","text":"From:"},{"type":"p","text":"https://www.artstation.com/artwork/a2XGL"},{"type":"p","text":"Backstory:"},{"type":"p","text":"A butcher, born and raised in Stonewall. Always wanted to become a butcher and is passionate about his job. He's obsessive about trying to ensure nothing goes to waste when he butchers something."},{"type":"p","text":"Personality:"},{"type":"p","text":"Can be a little scary and intimidating, but he is a professional when it comes to meat and butchering."},{"type":"p","text":"Interests/RP involvement options:"},{"type":"p","text":"He might ask folk to bring in rare monsters and/or animals as things for him to butcher, as he wants to hone his craft by attempting to butcher more types of meat."},{"type":"p","text":"Featured in:"},{"type":"p","text":"Barony Burgers – Sold Todo Sawl meat for his burgers."},{"type":"p","text":"Nice To Meat You – Was the challenger and a judge for Todo Sawl's meat cooking challenge."},{"type":"p","text":"More features to be added."}]},{"id":"east","name":"Otenzian Empire (East)","aliases":["Otenzian Empire (East)","Isekai Hell - Otenzian Empire (East)"],"summary":"The eastern edge of the Second Continent and home to the most Humans in the known world. It is separated from the rest of the continent by a long mountain range and hill country that acts as a natural barrier. It has a Greek and Roman style. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to the canon for the East Empire.","theme":{"accent":"#e0a34c","accent2":"#a72f22","glow":"#f0c36e","deep":"#1d0e08","motif":"imperial"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"Otenzian Empire (East)"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - Otenzian Empire (East)"},{"type":"p","text":"The eastern edge of the Second Continent and home to the most Humans in the known world. It is separated from the rest of the continent by a long mountain range and hill country that acts as a natural barrier. It has a Greek and Roman style. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to the canon for the East Empire."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/east-01.webp","alt":"east lore image 1"},{"type":"h2","text":"Current Situation"},{"type":"p","text":"East Empire is currently at war with the neighboring See nation. Fae See nation has a vast military power advantage despite their fewer numbers. To further hinder Empire efforts, they also have a giant bug infestation along their southern border with the Fae as well. Suppliers of basic supplies, mercenaries, and adventurers are needed in large numbers. General acceptance of Fae has turned into open persecution and execution within the nation. Additionally, Humans from this nation are met with scorn by the other nations or indifference at best, seen as being starters of the war. The war risks dragging other nations into the conflict and reigniting a continental war after a 50 year peace."},{"type":"h2","text":"Country - East Empire"},{"type":"p","text":"Formally known as the Otenzian Empire, the empire was created when the current ruling regime conquered the surrounding neighbor nations east of the Paizu Mountains several centuries prior. Since that time, the empire has risen to prominence in the 2nd continent as the greatest Human nation and one of the most advanced technologically in a mundane fashion. Ruled by an Emperor, the country is divided up into provinces that are governed by Emperor appointed governors and rule is enforced by Emperor appointed commanders that enforce national and governor interests within the province. Assisting the Emperor in running of the Empire, there is also a senate made up of senators that assist in the nation's legislation process. Senators are elected by the provinces they represent. Despite the public nature of the elections, the only winners tend to be those endorsed by the emperor or direct relatives of former senators."},{"type":"p","text":"The land of the empire is a wealth of resources and most especially precious metals they are able to procure from their numerous mines. They have a healthy and thriving slave trade that is fully legal. It helps drive progress and productivity despite not being as advanced in magic like the See or the Duchy. The nation is very developed as it pertains to cleanliness, travel, hygiene, and sporting events."},{"type":"h4","text":"Notes on Slavery:"},{"type":"p","text":"Constructs/Beastkin that fight/kill innocents (creatures without criminal titles) trying to apprehend them results in the construct/beastkin receiving criminal titles in most cases"},{"type":"p","text":"East Empire beastmen exception: There's a handful of beastmen acknowledged as having just enough brain cells to be independent creatures as opposed to house pets."},{"type":"p","text":"These have the noble faction's blessing in the form of title and paper work that can be used to get freedom, but they still may occasionally get apprehended. In such cases, lawful slavers will have to honor the asset, while criminal slavers won't care."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/east-02.webp","alt":"east lore image 2"},{"type":"h3","text":"Population - 5,900,000"},{"type":"p","text":"This large country has the most Humans in the world. It also has a large beastman population although their total numbers are not known nor fully added to the census count. A fraction of Beastmen are free and considered citizens of the Empire, but they are a 2nd class treated lesser than all others. Fae are generally welcomed and encouraged to live in the nation despite few choosing to live there. The war has changed that stance toward Fae. Constructs are in abundance within the country. While most automatons from the old war have been decommissioned, there are still many that serve more peaceful purposes. Monsters in the nation can be quite dangerous at times but they are arguably fewer in number than most other places due to being the furthest from the West Coast were most find their way to shore."},{"type":"h3","text":"Capital - Otenzel"},{"type":"p","text":"A port city and part of the major trade route by sea and on land into Widersia, Otenzel is located on the southern east coast. The Emperor and Senate reside in the city. It is a city bathed in wealth and at the cutting edge or progress for the nation's various developments in daily life and civil engineering. The arena is just as much a draw as the many public bathes the city offers to all classes of society. It is the sort of city that could host a party even if its borders are shrinking from invasion."},{"type":"h3","text":"Security"},{"type":"p","text":"Common in several major cities, especially in the Protectorate of Ryke, but also in the Empire, as well as smaller towns, a magical item known as Black Orb is in circulation. Possessed by the law enforcing body of the area, the black orb is used to determine criminals and monsters from normal travelers. Titles will appear on the black orbs surface when used. When a user places their hand on the orb, the titles that show will be specifically theirs. The titles shown will only be criminal titles or monster titles. No other titles will be shown. Monsters and criminals will be prevented entry into city or town and in some cases killed on the spot or hunted down with the discovery. Many towns and villages are protected by local squads of soldiers answering to a captain of some kind."},{"type":"p","text":"The vast eastern sea makes for great trade but also for the most piracy seen anywhere in the continent. East Empire has a very developed navy for the purposes of curbing some piracy as well as making sure they can trade with nations further west."},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel"},{"type":"p","text":"While the predominant forms of travel are on horses, ship, or carrier slaves, there is a another option: Portals. Magic portals cover the world. Most are hidden away in dungeons, deep forests, and treacherous mountains, but a few towns and all major cities have one. Portals allow for travel between any 2 portals instantly. However, they are limited in size, can act as borders between some nations, and can only warp and individual to another portal location they have already been to. Due to the constraints of its use and potential for abuse, most portals are heavily guarded. Black Orbs tend to be used on those passing through portals. Portal travel is not cheap, costing several Rykes per leg of the journey."},{"type":"h3","text":"Factions"},{"type":"p","text":"Major groups of individuals working together to influence events in the Empire and beyond are listed here. This is not a complete list, but can give a starting point to those interested in involving their characters in such things. Among those not listed, there are whispers of various criminal and monstrous groups as well:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Nobles"},{"type":"p","text":"The ruling class of The Empire, as noted previously are Emperor, Senators, Governors, and to a degree the military. Although Senators are chosen by the people, the real choice mainly remains in the hands of the Emperor or by blood. Due to the empire being so large and being made up of many peoples and mixing cultures, the ruling class are equally diverse with the hand of an Emperor bringing all together. The strength of an Emperor can make or break the Empire and is a lifetime appointment. Depending on the position, it is more for prestige than for any actual ruling power though. Most officials are put in place by the emperor and made to follow and enforce his decrees. At present there are 32 Senators, 16 Governors and 16 commanders. There are 5-7 generals leading the east empire armies at any one time based on survivability and need."},{"type":"h4","text":"Adventurer's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"The guild spans the globe but has country specific branches that answer to the rules and authorities therein. It is a place respected as the goto to request things done and have them done. The ranks of the guild are made up of warriors, mages, and many other talents from around the world. Just about any task that comes with a financial reward will get done. Due to their military might, they are closely monitored by the Noble factions. Their vast needs for equipment and supplies make the patron favorites with the Merchant's guild."},{"type":"h4","text":"Merchant's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"Despite the wealth they bring to the nation, the Merchants are not a particularly powerful faction in the nation. Their precious metals trade and slave trade are very well off. However, many of the advances the country has to trade with are not in high demand by other nations beyond their precious metals. The slave trade is still underground in most nations. Merchants are regularly squeezed by the noble class to assist in the latest war effort."},{"type":"p","text":"Church: The faction's power is on the rise and is one of the only factions not oppressively under the watch by the noble class."},{"type":"h3","text":"Religion - Many"},{"type":"p","text":"Most humans and even beastmen slaves worship one or more gods. the gods of the east empire tend to be from the Roman pantheon. It is so prevalent that those with no god or only 1 god are ridiculed publicly is foolish. It is one of the few nations where the church isn't directing them to crusade against another nation despite their present war situations. Although other factions don't actively interfere in the religions of the nation, the denominations and factions within the church are highly competitive with one another and actively poach members from each other when possible."},{"type":"h3","text":"Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"The Empire has its own paper currency called the Imperials (IMP's), but must use Ryke's coin currency, the ryke, anywhere beyond its borders. The Imperial changes with each new Emperor in order to have that ruler's face on it. The country's main exports are slaves, mythril, and orichalcum. Some of the best ship builders in the world also happen to make the East Empire their home."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/east-03.webp","alt":"east lore image 3"},{"type":"h2","text":"Emperor of The Eastern Empire - Tiberian Valerius"},{"type":"p","text":"The current emperor of the Eastern Empire; A middle-aged unmarried human. Formerly, he was a soldier who served during civil disputes among the provinces. Tiberian has since risen to power through political and military manoeuvring. The previous emperor, Tiberian's predecessor, mysteriously passed away as well."},{"type":"p","text":"Exempt from the ongoing war with the fae, Tiberian has presided over a peaceful and productive period in the Eastern Empire. He has yet to produce an heir and frequently leads his armies near the frontlines—to the dismay of his generals."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/east-04.webp","alt":"east lore image 4"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Zhaojun City"},{"type":"p","text":"A city located in the Yang Province of the Eastern Empire, built with the architecture and aesthetics of [Western Empire] in mind. The city is particularly known for its great leisure district. [Baron Honda], a frequent visitor, is suspected of bearing shady connections with the leisure district and the underworld."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/east-05.webp","alt":"east lore image 5"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Guifei City"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in Yang Province"},{"type":"h3","text":"Qilan's Crescent"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/east-06.webp","alt":"east lore image 6"},{"type":"p","text":"Qilan's Crescent is a crescent-shaped arch of temperate deciduous forest that surrounds the western outskirts of Guifei City. It is covered in thick and winding shrubbery with tall layers of canopies. A difficult, over-grown environment for some, but many smaller or skittish creatures call this place home."}]},{"id":"republic","name":"The Republic","aliases":["The Republic","Isekai Hell - The Republic"],"summary":"The northern beastman country for this roleplay and likely one of the next visited countries after Ryke. Has a Japanese theme and aesthetic. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to canon for The Republic.","theme":{"accent":"#8fc06e","accent2":"#3f7447","glow":"#c4d89f","deep":"#09140c","motif":"wild"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"The Republic"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - The Republic"},{"type":"p","text":"The northern beastman country for this roleplay and likely one of the next visited countries after Ryke. Has a Japanese theme and aesthetic. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to canon for The Republic."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/republic-01.webp","alt":"republic lore image 1"},{"type":"h2","text":"Country - The Republic"},{"type":"p","text":"Formerly known as Kuridan, the Republic is a collection of ruling bodies called Shogunates. Each shogunate is a collection of powerful family clans within a particular region of the country. The Shoguns that rule do so as a council that regularly meets to vote and discuss matters of state. Unlike a traditional Shogunate that is passed down through heredity, the shoguns and those that serve them are chosen by the people through bouts of strength and cunning. All members of the ruling class are just as proficient on the battlefield as they are in the shogunate council. The country is further north so they can experience harsher winters and more temperate summers, but their southernmost tip to the west can experience the opposite, making them a country of extremes. Much of their land is covered in river fed rainforests and hill country. The people have taken great strides in cultivating the land and making the most of the monsters that plague them to grow their power."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/republic-02.webp","alt":"republic lore image 2"},{"type":"h3","text":"Population - 5,700,000"},{"type":"p","text":"This large country has quite an abundance and variety of beastmen for its people. While some fae find themselves making settlement in the more secluded edges and depths of the nation, the country is very much beastman territory. Constructs are practically non-existent and are likely outnumbered by the monsters that are regularly hunted by the populace. Humans are few in number due to tensions with East Empire. While humans are welcome, only the strong are respected."},{"type":"h3","text":"Capital - Okiro"},{"type":"p","text":"Built on the banks of the continental lake west of the major river heading north to the Sea, the capital enjoys a bounty of seafood, sea travel, and trade. While not as much a central hub as Ryke, it still serves as a stop off point for most countries and cities wishing to trade from the west. A major hub for the merchant, adventurer, and noble factions. It is quite a happening place for global news and less than ideal beastman behavior."},{"type":"h3","text":"Security"},{"type":"p","text":"Common in several major cities, especially in the Protectorate of Ryke, as well as smaller towns, a magical item known as Black Orb is in circulation. Possessed by the law enforcing body of the area, the black orb is used to determine criminals and monsters from normal travelers. Titles will appear on the black orbs surface when used. When a user places their hand on the orb, the titles that show will be specifically theirs. The titles shown will only be criminal titles or monster titles. No other titles will be shown. Monsters and criminals will be prevented entry into city or town and in some cases killed on the spot or hunted down with the discovery. Many towns and villages are protected by a militia of peasant soldiers led by a Samurai."},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel"},{"type":"p","text":"While the predominant forms of travel are on boats in the water ways and beastmen runners, there is a 2nd option: Portals. Magic portals cover the world. Most are hidden away in dungeons, deep forests, and treacherous mountains, but a few towns and all major cities have one. Portals allow for travel between any 2 portals instantly. However, they are limited in size, can act as borders between some nations, and can only warp and individual to another portal location they have already been to. Due to the constraints of its use and potential for abuse, most portals are heavily guarded. Black Orbs tend to be used on those passing through portals. Portal travel is not cheap, costing several Rykes per leg of the journey."},{"type":"h3","text":"Factions"},{"type":"p","text":"Major groups of individuals working together to influence events in the Republic and beyond are listed here. This is not a complete list, but can give a starting point to those interested in involving their characters in such things. Among those not listed, there are whispers of various criminal and monstrous groups as well:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Nobles"},{"type":"p","text":"The ruling class of The Republic, as noted previously are individuals chosen through battle and competition by the people they would eventually represent. As such, they are not just the ruling class, but also the warrior class for the nation as mentioned in Security. They are the most prestigious faction of the nation and all work hard to join their ranks someday or fill a role in service to them. They keep a strict code of conduct that promotes chivalry and honor above self. There are 15 shogunates that make up the council and beneath them are a multitude of Daimyo and Samurai that lead their armies and help enforce their laws/decrees."},{"type":"h4","text":"Adventurer's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"The guild spans the globe but has country specific branches that answer to the rules and authorities therein. It is a place respected as the goto to request things done and have them done. The ranks of the guild are made up of warriors, mages, and many other talents from around the world. Just about any task that comes with a financial reward will get done. Due to their military might, they are closely monitored by the Noble factions. Their vast needs for equipment and supplies make the patron favorites with the Merchant's guild."},{"type":"h4","text":"Merchant's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"There is no shortage of sly beastmen making up this faction in their nation. Should you have the coin, they have the wares. Despite the nation's hardline against any and all slavery, the merchant guild has come up with clever ways to have people work for them to perform services for extended periods of time without paying them. Also illegal, they can peddle drugs from foreign countries. The country has a love/hate relationship with outside trade. A necessary evil for many, an evil which the merchant guild happily undertakes. For this reason and others, the merchants are the most despised faction in the nation."},{"type":"h4","text":"Church"},{"type":"p","text":"This faction is an after thought to the people of the republic. While there are many shrines and temples around the country and while they have believers and practitioners a plenty, it is not like a church with regular attendance or tithe. They are generally seen as a necessary third party to the mortal world that helps guide the masses and give them insight into the divine. With such readings and words, the church in Kuridan can sometimes sway the council of Shoguns."},{"type":"h3","text":"Religion - Many"},{"type":"p","text":"The beastmen predominantly worship the gods found in the japanese pantheon but all of them are beastmen as well as spirits said to be in all things (separate from fae spirits, these are believed to be divine in nature). A few old former slaves worship the greek/roman gods of their former masters. They exalt the principles of hard work, perseverance, justice, and righteous anger. Unlike what is commonly thought, they do not praise rage and savagery. Believing themselves to be above the common beast of the field, any trait that lacks proper restraint is thought to be unbecoming a proper beastman. Most cultists in the nation worship evil or savage gods that revel in blood and violence. Such cults are slain when found, but typically relish the violence all the same. The clergy of the beast nation have similar practices and appearances to Shinto priests."},{"type":"h3","text":"Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"Although the Republic has its own coin currency called the BeastYen (BY's), it trades predominantly in Ryke's coin currency, the ryke. This makes it easier to exchange goods with other nations, especially those with political reasons for refusing to stock BeastYen. Although the Republic has no shortage of trade, they are not particularly wealthy. They are rarely the first to discover or innovate anything. Even their claim to fame: superior martial weapons, are made with techniques former slaves were taught by their human masters several decades prior. Their stamina and powerful bodies have made their nation come out ahead in labor intensive crafts such as the harvesting of monster parts, some mining, and rice production (a main staple despite the many carnivorous beastmen that reside in the nation)."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/republic-03.webp","alt":"republic lore image 3"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - The Holy City of Vegard"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/republic-04.webp","alt":"republic lore image 4"},{"type":"p","text":"A small city located in the far northeast of the continent. It has a wide population of various types of beastfolk. The city is uniquely located on a small island off of a cliffside, only accessible by a connection of bridges. It is an important city in various religions, most notably Syncretism, as it is common to take a pilgrimage there. A few Syncretist Cardinals are known to have been born in this city. The Paladin Order of Virtus has its main base in this city."},{"type":"p","text":"Nana Roshan - Bunnyfolk Healer and Medic in the Holy City of Vegard"},{"type":"p","text":"Wallace - Mayor of the Holy City of Vegard"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - The Paizu Mountains"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/republic-05.webp","alt":"republic lore image 5"},{"type":"p","text":"A mountain range that borders the Beast Republic and the Eastern Empire, various creatures call this place home. Though there are rumors that there lives a Cardinal of the Syncretist Church. There are not many who would pass through the region so lightly due to the danger of the mountains and other manner of creatures. Many travelers have died in the region due to the giants that live in the mountains all the while looking for the rumored Cardinal that calls the region home."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Nan Gau Region"},{"type":"p","text":"Shogun: Unnamed kitsune from Clan Yamimoto"},{"type":"h4","text":"Region Map"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/republic-06.webp","alt":"republic lore image 6"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Nan Pass"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/republic-07.webp","alt":"republic lore image 7"},{"type":"p","text":"A remote village on the eastern side of the Beastmen Republic, the village was formerly known for its mining industry. A town full of blacksmiths and miners; due to the remote location close to the Paizu mountains, there is a small detachment of guards to keep the peace. Recently the village's population was significantly cut down due to a sudden monster raid, and is recovering."},{"type":"h2","text":"Festival of Twin Lights (Sōsei no Akari)"},{"type":"p","text":"Submitted by Moonberry"},{"type":"h3","text":"Where It Takes Place"},{"type":"p","text":"Nan Pass Village and throughout the Nan Gau region of the Republic, especially mining settlements in the Paizu Mountains. Late summer, during the time of meteor showers when the skies are clearest and ore trade is strongest before autumn harvest."},{"type":"h3","text":"What It Celebrates / Purpose"},{"type":"p","text":"The Festival of Twin Lights honors both the strength of the people and the blessings of the land. It is held to give thanks to the mountains for their ore and protection, and to the heavens for guidance and dreams. It symbolizes the “two lights” that sustain the village: the fire of mortal strength by day, and the lanterns and stars of the night sky. Some local myths speak of a flame wolf and a crane of starlight—guardian spirits who bless the people when strength and gratitude are shown together."},{"type":"h3","text":"How They Celebrate / Traditions"},{"type":"p","text":"Daytime Trials: Villagers compete in feats of strength and endurance, such as ore-carrying, hammer-striking contests, and wrestling. Children join in simpler versions like balancing stones or rope-pulling."},{"type":"p","text":"Trial of Stone: In the afternoon, villagers carry marked stones up a slope and place them at a mountain shrine as a sign of resolve."},{"type":"p","text":"Feasting: Families share rice cakes shaped like wolves and moons, grilled fish, hearty broths, and sweet dumplings dusted with colored sugar to mimic ore-dust."},{"type":"p","text":"Night Ritual: At dusk, miners crush ores into powder and toss them into the bonfire, creating sparks of many colors. Lanterns carrying wishes are released into the sky while the flames are praised as the “voice of the mountain.” Children whisper their wishes to the stars before letting their lanterns go."},{"type":"h3","text":"Festival Scene:"},{"type":"p","text":"The clang of hammers carried through Nan Pass like a heartbeat. Sparks leapt from the forge in steady bursts, while children shrieked with laughter as they tried to heft painted stones or topple one another in dusty games. The air smelled of hot iron, grilled fish, and sweet dumplings, all threaded through with woodsmoke from the festival fires."},{"type":"p","text":"Aedrianna walked between her father and grandmother, her small hand lost in Thaddeus’s firm grip. Her pale yukata shifted with every step, the sleeves hanging too long for her thin arms. She coughed once into her wrist, but her eyes never stopped following the chaos of color and sound around her."},{"type":"p","text":"“Even the smallest stone teaches balance,” Thaddeus said, nodding toward the children wobbling beneath their burdens. His smile was tired, rimmed with soot, but still gentle."},{"type":"p","text":"Aedri shook her head quickly, pressing close against his side. “I’d only drop it,” she admitted, her voice quiet, resigned."},{"type":"p","text":"Elouise’s chuckle was low, carrying more warmth than amusement. “Strength takes many shapes, Thaddeus.” She came forward with her ever-present pouch at her hip, kneeling to offer her granddaughter a dumpling dusted with glittering sugar. “Yours is not in stone, little one. Yours will be in the things you craft.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Aedrianna took it, murmured a thank you, and nibbled the edge. Her gaze lingered on her grandmother longer than the treat, as though she understood more than she should. Elouise, for her part, met that look with a steady patience, speaking to her as though the girl could grasp truths beyond her years."},{"type":"p","text":"The festival rolled into twilight, the drums replacing the hammer-song. Villagers gathered along the river with their lanterns, painted with wolves, cranes, and stars. The bonfire roared, fed with powdered ore that burst into vivid greens and blues, the sparks spiraling upward to meet the night sky."},{"type":"p","text":"Thaddeus helped his daughter steady the lantern she had painted herself. Its spirals of bright colors were clumsy, but she held it as though it were fragile glass. He lit the wick, then rested his hand over hers. “When you let go, it carries thanks to the mountain, and your wish to the stars.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Her lips pressed tight, eyes lowered. “What if they don’t listen?” Elouise, lantern cradled against her arm, leaned near. “They listen,” she said with quiet conviction. “But they only eep what you mean. So speak it true."},{"type":"p","text":"The candle’s warmth tugged at the lantern, urging it upward. Aedrianna bent her head close, whispering a secret into the flame so soft it was lost in the noise of the crowd:"},{"type":"p","text":"“Please… let me be strong enough. Let me see the world.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Her hands opened."},{"type":"p","text":"The lantern rose, shivering, then climbing with sudden grace. Higher and higher it drifted until it joined the river of lights already gliding across the sky. Above, stars shimmered like watchful eyes; below, the bonfire cracked with its colored sparks. For a breathless moment, mountain and sky reflected one another—twin lights answering in harmony."},{"type":"p","text":"Aedrianna lifted her hand as though to follow it, her small chest lightened by the release. Somewhere in that glow, she felt her wish had been heard."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Five Thousand Peony Blossoms, Masanori Geisha House"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in The Republic, The Nara no Nox Shogunate, The Koyake Clan‘s—Masanori Domain. The Koyake are one of the three founding families of the Nara no Nox Shogunate, owning one of the largest rice territories blessed by the [Shrine of the Fallen Blossom]. The Masanori’s are one of the esteemed branch families established over the ensuing centuries. They have consistently reached high standing within the military, shrines, and shogunate’s bureaucracy. An honourable family, nobly regarded for their speciality in logistics. As a result, they have garnered affluence and are well-connected."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Shrine of Fallen Blossoms"},{"type":"p","text":"The shrine in which many cherry blossom trees grow and flower almost every year. This is where the annual [Cherry Blossom Festival] is held, a celebration of the cherry blossoms. It is believed that misfortune is brought about when celebrating the blossoms after they’ve fallen. [The Fallen Spears] are charged with protecting the Shrine, one of the most powerful samurai units of the Koyake Clan."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Shrine of the Cleansed Curses"},{"type":"p","text":"A newly established Shrine under the divine protection of Uriel, the Shield Archon. Reborn from the darkness of the Nightmare Swamp after the purification. The shrine—which serves as resting quarters for Uriel's celestial forces—is carved out within the trunk of Aegrizora; The sacred tree which emerged towering from the swamp's remnants. The surrounding hillocks of the surrounding lake are for conversation, contemplation, and camping."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Tower of Paizu Mountains"},{"type":"p","text":"A tower standing in the [Paizu Mountains] of the [Beast’s Republic]. The tower is inhabited by various mouse maids and the powerful Syncretist cardinal, Zolius—who is obsessed with attempting to define what is ”Good” via peering into the future. The cardinal is said to possess Supernatural [Intelligence] and [Healing]."},{"type":"p","text":"Interior"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Frozen Giant's Hand"},{"type":"p","text":"The hand of a giant outstretched and frozen beneath the snow—big enough to become a landmark. Located within the [Paizu Mountains] of The [Beast’s Republic]."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Gala'Kraoth"},{"type":"p","text":"A recently discovered island to the north of the second continent. Though largely unexplored, there have been signs of reptilian inhabitants as well as sightings of elementals. The Republic branch of the Adventuring Guild is posting jobs to explore the area."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Fort Nan Gau"},{"type":"p","text":"An old military outpost, which long stood abandoned in the Republic's north. A village has taken root around the outside of the fort and has slowly become akin to a castle town."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Yale Village"},{"type":"p","text":"Yale is a quiet village located near a river and some spikey hills in southern Kuridan. Its inhabitants are almost exclusively Driders--most notable among them being Anansi the guard captain and Gudina, who is in charge of the village's agriculture. The village relies on a system of growing corn/maize for consumption and for feed for their chicken-sized caterpillars, which they raise for meat and silk alike. They then use their manure to fertilise the fields. Yale is known to produce high quality silk, both from the caterpillars and Driders themselves."},{"type":"p","text":"The village of Yale won't have to worry about their crop routine falling apart for the foreseeable future, though they will likely reach out to the Adventurer's Guild to ask someone to investigate what caused the [Monster] moles to show up at their doorstep to begin with."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Shi Shogunate of the Ginji Domain"},{"type":"p","text":"The populated area is known as Hisuzuki, a farming settlement that works like a checkpoint between bigger towns and cities, where merchants and travelers rest before resuming their journeys. The Sanmari Tea House that sits near the edge of the village is of moderate renown within the domain and slightly beyond. The source of its fame are the owners: three sisters that run different facets of the business. One sister, Amari, runs hospitality, receiving guests and providing refreshment. Another sister handles entertainment through song and dance. The third sister handles finances and other matters that don't involve clients."},{"type":"h3","text":"Sanmari Tea House"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Gearshift Gorge"},{"type":"p","text":"A small village nestled in the Republic between a river and the North-Eastern border of Ryke, populated by a mix of Beast and Human. Just over half of the residents have prosthetics, which vary in complexity but appear to be uniform in being mostly fashioned from wood. The well-traveled might describe Gearshift Gorge as a blend of Widersia's society and the Republic's culture and architecture."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Taeko Village"},{"type":"p","text":"Taeko Village sits in the far east of the Republic against its border with the East Empire. The settlement is largely neglected by the daimyo that lords over the region due to its poor rice harvests."},{"type":"h4","text":"Yoshio"},{"type":"p","text":"Elder/Leader of Taeko Village, an old goat man."},{"type":"h2","text":"Funanori no nageki (Sailors Lamentation)"},{"type":"p","text":"Submitted by Tellusoil"},{"type":"h3","text":"Where It Takes Place"},{"type":"p","text":"Konpeki no shinju and other settlements at the northern sea border of the Republic at the end of fall, beginning of winter, before the frost sets in"},{"type":"h3","text":"What It Celebrates / Purpose"},{"type":"p","text":"To honour those lost at sea and to ask the sea for safety in the winter months to come"},{"type":"h3","text":"How They Celebrate / Traditions"},{"type":"p","text":"During the day, preparations are made for the evening's festivities. Children painting lanterns, silent prayers for the dead. Most businesses would close down earlier if the situation allowed it."},{"type":"p","text":"At dusk, the festival begins."},{"type":"p","text":"As the sun is setting, the people of the village gather at the sea's edge."},{"type":"p","text":"They will place wooden boats in the water. The boats carry a paper lantern and offerings for the ones lost at sea or for the sea itself."},{"type":"p","text":"As the sun sinks into the horizon, the boats are released onto the sea."},{"type":"p","text":"With song and prayer, people watch the boats drift onto the sea as the light of day vanishes, and the only thing seen on the horizon is the light of the boats."},{"type":"h3","text":"Festival Scene"},{"type":"p","text":"Day has come and gone. The blue sky is now painted in red and orange as the people of Konpeki no shinju gather at the beach just outside the fishing village. Many people were carrying small boats with them as they stood there on the salty early winter afternoon."},{"type":"p","text":"Noelle stood among the people. Next to her stood a tall woman with long blond hair and dark blue eyes. The woman placed her hand on the small head of Noelle. \"Come, sweety. Let us place ours,” the woman said with a warm smile. “Okay, mommy,” little Noelle said."},{"type":"p","text":"The two walked to the water’s edge. Noelle’s mother placed the boat in the water. “Well, would you look at how pretty this lantern is. Did you do this?” Noelle’s mother said, to which Noelle looked at her with a proud smirk. The paper lantern was decorated with several childish doodles made by little Noelle. Fish, birds and even one of her and her mother's faces."},{"type":"p","text":"“Come, it's almost time. Let us prepare our offers” Noelle's mother took a few things from her pouch. A picture, an incense stick and a package wrapped in paper. “What is that?” Noelle asked, curiously looking at the paper-wrapped package. “Oh, this?” Noelle's mom carefully unwrapped the package, revealing three homemade onigiri “They're my offering. I made them myself”, her mother said “But I thought we were here to offer something to appease the sea people, not poison them?” Noelle said deadpan, to which her mother grabbed her ear, “EH! My cooking is not that bad!” she said, smiling but with anger underlying her words.\"Ouch! Ouch! Ouch! Okay okay!! Your cooking is not the worst!!” “Better”, Noelle’s mom let go of her ear."},{"type":"p","text":"Noelle’s mom continued to place the items on the boat. The opened package of onigiri in front of a photo of the face of a male albatross-beastkin, “Who’s the bird man?” Noelle asked. “Oh, he? he was someone I knew from before I found you”, she said with a sorrowful gaze. “Was he your boyfriend?” That question startled her mom, but she soon let out a chuckle, “Husband actually”, she said,”YOU WERE MARRIED!?\" Noelle exclaimed, surprised. “What’s wrong with that?” She said with a threat under her voice, “Noooothing…” Noelle said, seeing her mistake in her words. Her mom let out a sigh. “Yes, he was the kindest, sweetest man I could even wish for. He showed me a world I could never have imagined existing,” she said sorrowfully, “where is he now?” Noelle asked, “Oh, he’s not here anymore. One day, he sailed out to the northern sea and hasn’t come back since” A tear started to form in Noelle's mother’s eye. When Noelle noticed her mother about to cry, she quickly hugged her leg “Don’t cry, mommy. I’m sure your husband didn’t want to leave you alone”. Her mother looked down at Noelle with a smile “It’s okay, sweety. I’m not angry. That’s just how the sea is. She giveth and she takes... Although the sea has taken my sweet Richard, she also gave me you” Her mom patted Noelle’s head softly."},{"type":"p","text":"“Don’t you also have something to offer too?” Noelle's mom asked the little mermaid, “Oh yeah!” Noelle put her hand in her pocket and pulled out a seashell string necklace “Tadaa!” “How lovely. Now go place it with the rest” “will do” Noelle skipped to the boat and placed the necklace next to the Onigiri."},{"type":"p","text":"It was time. The setting sun had already kissed the horizon’s edge. The people gathered, lit up the candles in the lanterns, and pushed the festival boats onto the seawater. The boats floated like a parade towards the horizon as the final beams of light of the sun slowly faded behind the horizon’s edge, every boat carrying offerings to the sea. Some had carved wooden figurines as an honour to the gods, and some had bottles of alcohol for the sailors lost at sea. Some had food, and others had letters to those who were dearly missed. All were handed over to the sea waves as the sky turned dark with night. The boat's light shone bright in the distance. The citizens of Konpeki no shinju kept watching until the last light also faded on the horizon before returning to the village."},{"type":"p","text":"“I would not have minded to have met Richmond”, Noelle said, yawning as she walked back to town holding her mother’s hand. “It’s Richard, sweetie”, her mother corrected her, \"And I’m sure he would also have loved it to have met you”"}]},{"id":"fae-see","name":"See of Chearon","aliases":["See of Chearon","Isekai Hell - See of Fae"],"summary":"A southern country sandwiched between the East and West Empires, the See is home to the most Fae in the known world. It unsurprisingly models itself after a religious nation with many temples, shrines, and holy sites throughout its many forests. Its people are very devout and link magic, nature, and themselves together in a balance that serves as worship to their deities, which happen to be the strongest and oldest o","theme":{"accent":"#75d7b7","accent2":"#6c4cab","glow":"#a8f0dd","deep":"#071411","motif":"fae"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"See of Chearon"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - See of Fae"},{"type":"p","text":"A southern country sandwiched between the East and West Empires, the See is home to the most Fae in the known world. It unsurprisingly models itself after a religious nation with many temples, shrines, and holy sites throughout its many forests. Its people are very devout and link magic, nature, and themselves together in a balance that serves as worship to their deities, which happen to be the strongest and oldest of their kin: the great primordial spirits. Their cities are built in, on, and around nature rather than clearing it out of the way. It gives their nation a very distinct feel and style compared to most other nations aside from Widersia. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to the canon for the See of Fae."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/fae-see-01.webp","alt":"fae-see lore image 1"},{"type":"h3","text":"Current Situation"},{"type":"p","text":"See of Fae is currently at war with the neighboring East Empire nation. Fae See nation has a vast military power advantage despite their fewer numbers. Suppliers of basic supplies, mercenaries, and adventurers are needed in large numbers. General acceptance of Fae has turned into open persecution and execution within the East Empire nation. Additionally, Humans from the East Empire nation are met with scorn by the other nations or indifference at best, seen as being starters of the war. The war risks dragging other nations into the conflict and reigniting a continental war after a 50 year peace. The Fae, although initially defending themselves, are not clearly dominating in the war and seemingly pressing for defeating the East Empire if not conquering it outright."},{"type":"h2","text":"Country - See of Fae"},{"type":"p","text":"Formally known as the See of Chearon, the See is one of the oldest nations in the Second Continent. Supposedly founded and formed by the ruling primordial spirits, the nation is one of the few to survive consistently when disaster sweeps the other nations with spoken word records that go back thousands of years while most other nations only have a few hundred years of history or less. Due to its age and ability to pass down wisdom through the ages, in addition to the average member of their populace living for hundreds of years, the See is populated by the greatest number of skilled workers in the world. Arguably, they have the best craftsmen in the world too, but that title has been recently hotly contested by a neighboring nation."},{"type":"p","text":"The nation is ruled over by their Pope, the Spirit King, with absolute authority. The equivalent of a living [god] on the mortal plane, the Spirit King is generally inactive as it pertains to the day to day activities of his people. Beneath the Spirit King are his cardinals, each taking on an element or aspect of the Spirit King faith. They act as the mouth pieces of the king and relay to the most devout of the Fae clergy guidance and blessing that may benefit and best shepherd the Fae nation's people."},{"type":"p","text":"The land of the See is filled with many resources but predominantly the bounty of nature from its forests. Fruits that won't grow anywhere else in the world. Medicinal herbs so potent but so hard to cultivate elsewhere. And an abundance of fauna and other mysterious yet to be discovered by the rest of the continent at large. More than the Humans of the Otenzian Empire (East) have their eyes on the nation of the See. Their ability to export living wood as hard as steel and lighter than mithril is no small feat among other such products only the See can provide."},{"type":"p","text":"Despite their old age and vast wisdom, they can feel especially dated and conservative in their views of the world and their role in it. Their faith is paramount followed by the wellbeing of nature and their people. The rest of the world could burn for all they care and it has in the past without them lifting a finger to aid."},{"type":"h3","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/fae-see-02.webp","alt":"fae-see lore image 2"},{"type":"h3","text":"Population - 500,000"},{"type":"p","text":"This large country has the most Fae in the world. However, that is not much. Fae rarely reproduce and when they do it is in small numbers. Additionally, their long development phase makes it difficult for them to regain their numbers in the face of any disaster. The war from 50 years ago wiped out many of their number and they have yet to replenish the number of adult Fae from that time. The See of Fae is one of the few countries in the world that permits the murder of Humans without garnering a murder title. In the same way humans feel nothing over swatting a mosquito, the Fae have long since believed all other sentient races are inferior to the point of barely being more than the insects that crawl underfoot. Humans rarely live in the See or last long if they do. Beastmen capable of living with the abundance of nature are much more welcome and do live in the See in great numbers although not to the point of eclipsing the Fae. While generally indifferent to most matters beyond their borders including slavery, the beastmen have been able to find shelter from the Empires on either side that indulge in that trade. Constructs are not particularly welcome in the See but they are not turned away. Regarded as a lesser form of Fae that will never reach its true potential, Constructs that escape the East empire find themselves in a very treacherous land but at least they are free of Humans for what remains of their existence. Monsters are abominations that are destroyed on sight but there are some that find their way into the Fae and lurk within its depths."},{"type":"h3","text":"Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"Internally, the Fae do not have a currency of any kind. They typically barter, exchanging goods for service or service for service and goods for goods. Encouraged to live communally to have the least impact on the land as possible, the Fae that do so typically leverage the resources of the entire commune to do their trades which are for specialty goods needed by the commune as a whole. Churches/temples are the first taken care of during times of abundance and are the first to aid their congregations during hard times."},{"type":"h3","text":"Security"},{"type":"p","text":"Most Fae have the means to appraise as their endless curiosity prevents them from sparing anyone or thing privacy. On the same coin, most Fae also have means of fooling or blocking Appraisal, so it can be a particularly difficult place to know anything for certain and much more likely to lead to misunderstandings and extra hardship, situations that the Fae sometimes revel to see others in. Despite the general vibe of peace and easy going that the Fae exude most of the time, the likelihood of dying at any moment is just as high if not higher in the Fae See."},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel"},{"type":"p","text":"While the predominant form of travel is on foot there is another option: Portals. Magic portals cover the world. Most are hidden away in dungeons, deep forests, and treacherous mountains, but a few towns and all major cities have one. The most portals in the world have been found within the See of Fae. Portals allow for travel between any 2 portals instantly. However, they are limited in size, can act as borders between some nations, and can only warp an individual to another portal location they have already been to. Due to the constraints of its use and potential for abuse, most portals are heavily guarded although it is impossible to guard them all in the See. Portal travel is free within the See nation."},{"type":"h3","text":"Capital - Bishri"},{"type":"p","text":"A port city and part of the major trade route by sea and on land into Widersia, The Republic, Ryke, and The Duchy, Bishri has a location in trade rivaled only by Ryke. Located on the northern edge of the See on the Continental Lake's south east coast, the only thing holding it back is the national stance of being reluctant to trade beyond its borders except with those it trusts or has strong enough reason to. Although none of the great spirits reside in the city exclusively, the each have temples dedicated to them and their deified peers. It is a city sacred to the See people beyond almost any other site. Said to be the place with their great spirits first ended their voyage and disembarked in the 2nd continent shortly before the founding of the See, every street, stone, building, and statue is said to be holy. Even the water that laps against her shores is now claimed to be blessed. It is so holy that no creature is permitted to enter the city unclean and no shoes or head coverings may be worn."},{"type":"h3","text":"Factions"},{"type":"p","text":"Major groups of individuals working together to influence events in the See and beyond are listed here. This is not a complete list, but can give a starting point to those interested in involving their characters in such things. Among those not listed, there are whispers of various criminal and monstrous groups as well:"},{"type":"h4","text":"Nobles/Church/Religion"},{"type":"p","text":"The ruling class also happens to be the head of the Religious faction as well in the See. The pope is simultaneously the king and the religious leader for the nation, both handling the faith and spirituality of his people as well as ensuring their safety and wellbeing in a more worldly capacity. In line with that form of governance, the See Fae has the largest religiously controlled military in the world. While the Pope has ruled since anyone can remember, the Cardinals are occasionally replaced. Cardinals are typically always clergy that have ascended to a spiritual state comparable to the divine. The upper ranks of the clergy all began as humble priests and temple staff."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/fae-see-03.webp","alt":"fae-see lore image 3"},{"type":"p","text":"Pope - …"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/fae-see-04.webp","alt":"fae-see lore image 4"},{"type":"p","text":"Darkness Cardinal - She's cold and cruel but gentle. Darkness is an uncaring place, but all-encompassing and rarely sudden. Merely inevitable. The duality between being lost alone and in the dark vs being tucked secure under the covers at night"},{"type":"p","text":"Earth Cardinal - ..."},{"type":"p","text":"Fire Cardinal - ..."},{"type":"p","text":"Ice Cardinal - ..."},{"type":"p","text":"Light Cardinal - ..."},{"type":"p","text":"Lightning Cardinal - ..."},{"type":"p","text":"Metal Cardinal - ..."},{"type":"p","text":"Water Cardinal - ..."},{"type":"p","text":"Wind Cardinal - ..."},{"type":"h4","text":"Adventurer's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"Present but nearly non-existent. The people of the See have few worries for this world, so jobs are scarcely put in and Humans, the most likely to be adventurers, are far and few between. Typically they get Adventurers from other nations on special cases to resolve particularly troublesome situations."},{"type":"h4","text":"Merchant's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"To the Merchant Guild's despair, the nation is reluctant to trade anything with anyone, so everything traded typically requires approval by members of the church overseeing the wellbeing of the nation and her resources. While the Merchant Guild is more influential than the Adventurer's Guild, it is only by a little bit. The one edge it holds onto despite external trade being stunted is internal trade is booming with more and more exquisite products being produced by the skilled crafters within the nation."},{"type":"h4","text":"Criminal Faction"},{"type":"p","text":"While treated not much differently from monsters if discovered, there is a criminal element within the Fae Nation. In addition to religious outcasts, you also have Fae who are born of and/or revel in violence and destruction and go out of their way to sow seeds of it within and beyond the Fae nation where possible."},{"type":"h3","text":"Religion - One"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/fae-see-05.webp","alt":"fae-see lore image 5"},{"type":"p","text":"All Fae worship the King of Spirits and his Cardinals as living [gods] on the mortal plane. Their tenets are predominantly about caring for the world and their fellow Fae. While there is no pressing to completely suppress the chaotic or whimsical urges inherent to Fae, there are many verses of their faith that encourage Fae to find the most productive outlets for their most chaotic and destructive tendencies. Overall, it leads to a populace of Chaos that always teeters on the edge of collapse but never does and it works fine for the Fae to leave things at that. It's not uncommon for many Fae to hold the opinion they are superior to the other sentient races, but that belief is reinforced by their religion which calls upon them to guide the other races and make the hard decisions best for the world when times require."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Alladell Village"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/fae-see-06.webp","alt":"fae-see lore image 6"},{"type":"p","text":"Alladell Village in the Fae See has several pokemon, namely an onix, helping out with the acquisition and creation of stone trinkets that are sold to neighboring regions. The trinkets are treated as luxury items and may one day see the village prosper."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Refara's Sound"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/fae-see-07.webp","alt":"fae-see lore image 7"},{"type":"p","text":"A town on the southern coast of the See, nearing the eastern bay, Refara's Sound is a retreat that provides exotic luxury and wild beauty to its citizens and visitors from all over the continent. It boasts many eateries, inns, artisans, and entertainers who make a living off visitors' gold – an irregularity compared to the surrounding settlements of the See. The city proper rests atop a large cliff overlooking the bay, while a smaller section below provides housing for the locals."},{"type":"p","text":"Lady Shaylan"},{"type":"p","text":"Refara's Sound is governed by Lady Shaylan, a haughty Sphinx unafraid of wielding her perceived social superiority over others for the good of her city."},{"type":"p","text":"Hajira"},{"type":"p","text":"Her assistant, Hajira, is a level-headed, hard-working woman with an apathetic outlook toward most things that aren't related to Lady Shaylan and her interests."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - ??? | Contributed by StarPrincessVal"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Curse Cleansing Pool"},{"type":"p","text":"Legends tell of a place hidden within the southwestern wilds of the See - a natural spring that rests amidst ancient ruins. It calls to those beset with curses, and should they enter the spring, it may cleanse them under the light of a full moon. There are records of those successful, and while the results vary, all claim the cleansing has strengthened them in some capacity. On the other hand, there are no records of those who failed. Simply put, they are never seen again - as if they vanished into the woods. To this extent, much remains unknown about the power this spring holds."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Wmgroth"},{"type":"p","text":"A settlement located in a boreal forest in the southern parts of the See. An active location for commerce in the See with a market square abundant with merchants. An enormous tree is forged with dwellings out of giant mushrooms toward the centre of Wmgroth, spread out from the centre are more private dwellings. The majority of Wmgroth residents are wealthier than the average person."},{"type":"p","text":"Security in Wmgroth includes appraisal orbs, a wooden wall with a protective dome conjured with magic over the settlement, as well as [Treant] wall guards. The wall contains four primary entrances in all cardinal directions."},{"type":"h4","text":"Gate"},{"type":"h4","text":"Beyond The Gate"},{"type":"h4","text":"Centre Market"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Applegrove"},{"type":"p","text":"A small town on the outskirts of [Bishri], providing lodging, storage, and services for those trying to enter the holy capital. Infrastructure conforms to the natural landscape, being built into and around the lofty trees, streams, and large rocks heavy with moss. The population is mostly dwarves, elves and halflings—although other Fae aren’t unheard of."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - J.C. Staff; DanMachi"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - The Matron’s Henge"},{"type":"p","text":"A magic stone ring that lies within Bishri proper. It is attended by a druidic circle led by an [elf] named Zephirin. They perform numerous magical rites for the church. The ring itself lies within a natural, shallow pool in the center of a copse of trees. The Matron's Circle is adorned in the shades of the earth. They occasionally take on members from other Circles for apprenticeship, before returning them to their home Circle."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - South Bishri, Airship Port & Customs Gate"},{"type":"p","text":"The city's major airship dock, residing in the southern end of Bishri. It mainly receives commercial and industrial vessels from [Widersia] and the [Grand Duchy of Roran], but it has several small docks for private or small commercial ships. Passengers and cargo are subject to inspection and approval by customs agents. Anything that is deemed 'unclean' is outright denied or forced to undergo a cleansing ritual."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Lodeli Woods"},{"type":"p","text":"A magical forest with a dense canopy that blocks out sunlight. Glowing mushrooms and luminous crystals grow from the trunks beneath the canopy, providing the area with dim light."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - The Healing Garden"},{"type":"p","text":"The Healing Garden is a place hidden away in one of the many vast stretches of dense forests in the See of Chearon. It is a place where many come to find healing, especially for more severe injuries, yet the journey there is arduous and difficult. On arrival the person in question is permitted to stay in a dedicated cabin for guests while they figure out what is expected of them. Many find themselves working in the gardens, doing simple house chores or repairing the buildings. Once someone's character has been proven worthy of healing, they will meet the Garden's master Eirlys."},{"type":"h4","text":"Eirlys"},{"type":"p","text":"A powerful Dryad with the power to heal many diverse injuries and/or curses. Known to offer promises of safe travels back home to those she heals, but how much sway she has or how far it reaches outside the Garden is debatable. Appears to have her own method for discerning the character of an individual, which former guests claim is based on one's dedication to maintaining the Garden in various ways. What she gleans from her trials results in the guest either gaining her favor and healing, or her displeasure and a sudden excommunication from the Garden. The latter forceful removal from the Garden prevents all attempts to re-enter and is frequently accompanied by an arduous trip home fraught with hardship."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - The Ruins of M’lyrna"},{"type":"p","text":"A few walls and outbuildings remain standing in this hamlet on the border of the Fae See. The area has seen heavy fighting with multiple rounds of airstrikes and artillery bombardments. The husks of dead monster bugs--including the shattered hull of an enormous bug tank--are strewn around the town limits."},{"type":"p","text":"There are no Human, Fae, or Beastkin remains, but a small graveyard of hand-painted markers stands on the outskirts of town; the names of the dead being slowly faded and washed away by sun, rain, and snow."},{"type":"p","text":"Despite the heavy fighting and numerous casualties, the place has an aura of peace about it, lacking the usual restless spirits that haunt such places where violence has been done."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Mycothra"},{"type":"p","text":"An underground fae village composed of fungal species of Fae people with the village elder Myco Mossevalli as an overseer. Many buildings are carved out of large mushrooms with naturally occurring decor like moss. Bridges connect the village together. Sizable fluorescent shrooms are used similar to street lights."},{"type":"h4","text":"Myco Mossevalli"},{"type":"p","text":"A purple mushroom fae. The Village elder of Mycothra entrusted with overseeing the underground Fae See settlement. While a strategic businessman and caring in his own ways, Myco is weary and somewhat pessimistic due to all the years of conflict he’s lived through. Since losing loved ones in war, he is more focused than ever on keeping Mycothra safe from outside threats."},{"type":"p","text":"Myco Mossevali has an office in Mycothra where he plays a role as a central arbiter from his mossy, mushroom encrusted tower in the center of Mycothra."},{"type":"h4","text":"Sporfyn"},{"type":"p","text":"Gatekeeper"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Eraza Town"},{"type":"p","text":"Positioned near the See's border with the East Empire, Eraza Town was a more traditional fae settlement. When the war between the East Empire and Fae See erupted, however, it became a convenient gathering point for all manner of refugees escaping the carnage. This has resulted in a state of overpopulation in Eraza, with beastkin quickly overtaking the fae as the majority."},{"type":"p","text":"Overpopulation is both helping and hurting Eraza:"},{"type":"p","text":"Well-Fortified (Boon) - The town has no shortage of bodies to defend it should an incursion happen. The dense population of beastkin in particular is a great deterrent to many a conflict with reasonable creatures that possess self-preservation instincts."},{"type":"p","text":"Labor Force (Boon) - The surplus population is full of idle hands ready to be put to work. Projects to improve the town can be accomplished more quickly assuming proper leadership is applied."},{"type":"p","text":"Food Shortage (Bane) - Many hands to work means many mouths to feed. Beastkin are especially ravenous."},{"type":"p","text":"Illness (Bane) - Many bodies and not enough space to properly house them or deal with waste properly has created the perfect storm for illness to arise and move quickly through the populace."},{"type":"p","text":"Target (Bane) - The bug nation is drawn to dense population areas as good food sources."},{"type":"h2","text":"Event - Overshadowed Eclipse"},{"type":"p","text":"The pink and green moon cross each other, creating a window of time that lasts three days and allows for certain rituals. Mysteriously, the event is only ever reported from locations in the Fae See."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Glymergloom"},{"type":"p","text":"A fae village located within a dense woodland area where fae magic appears to keep it within its own state of eternal night. The area is left unmarked on common maps. All first-time arrivals are given a tedious or difficult 'trial' in order to make use out of unwanted outsiders. Is it a rite of passage or just an annoying obstacle to deter the less determined? Business is preferably done through trade of physical goods or labour. Glymergloom has a surprisingly low wildlife population, but some uncommon and rare species of bioluminescent and magical fauna can be found here."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Ignis Volcano"},{"type":"h3","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - DarkKitsune"},{"type":"p","text":"A small, burnt biome in the corner of the Fae See that is home to a dense population of fire related elementalist fae. The area centers around a volcano magically kept in dormancy by the church of fire carved into its base. The volcano is surrounded by a river of lava that is kept molten by the same magic that silences the volcano. All fire and heat sources are contained within the boundary of the scorched area. Andesite trees litter the area."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - DarkKitsune"},{"type":"p","text":"Aidan - Deaconess that oversees the care of attendees as well as facilitates trials with fire and magic of C-grade."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - The Spear of Aelphi"},{"type":"p","text":"The Spear of Aelphi is known as a landmark and relic that was used to destroy the surrounding forest for miles on impact during the war of the races. It appears as a jagged, spike-like mountain, littered with treacherous ravines and glimmering trails of magic residue."},{"type":"p","text":"Secret: What is less known is that it also serves as a slumbering, artificial volcano with certain forces ensuring it remains dormant."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - The Dreamgorge"},{"type":"p","text":"A secluded community of sheepfolk within the Fae Sea who revere and carefully guard Somnara, a tree which grants imagination physical form. After a recent incident, the Dreamgorge has become isolationist, allowing only those respected widely among the fae, within its borders."},{"type":"h3","text":"Somnara"},{"type":"p","text":"A magic tree which can give physical form to the imagination of sentient beings. The imagined works persist so long as the \"dreamer\" remains nearby. A smaller tree is now growing beside it, focused entirely on sustaining Yume’s continued existence."}]},{"id":"west","name":"Ororoot Empire (West)","aliases":["Ororoot Empire (West)","Isekai Hell - West Empire"],"summary":"The Western Empire, also known as the Ororoot Empire, stands as a majestic realm on the western coast of the 2nd continent. Governed by a strict class system with the Emperor at its pinnacle slaves as its base, this nation thrives on a complex economy driven by trade, magical innovations, and a unique synergy with both monsters and beastmen. Its capital, Quang, a bustling port city, serves as the heart of commerce, b","theme":{"accent":"#d4b45d","accent2":"#8b5b25","glow":"#91c18a","deep":"#171008","motif":"desert"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"Ororoot Empire (West)"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - West Empire"},{"type":"p","text":"The Western Empire, also known as the Ororoot Empire, stands as a majestic realm on the western coast of the 2nd continent. Governed by a strict class system with the Emperor at its pinnacle slaves as its base, this nation thrives on a complex economy driven by trade, magical innovations, and a unique synergy with both monsters and beastmen. Its capital, Quang, a bustling port city, serves as the heart of commerce, benefiting from strategic geographic advantages and a diverse cultural fabric. The empire's economy is bolstered by the Adventurer's and Merchant's Guilds, which navigate the challenges and opportunities presented by the realm's magical landscapes and creatures. With slavery and monster Taming, regulated by rituals under the Church Faction's watch, the Western Empire remains a beacon of power, tradition, and magical prowess, standing resilient against both internal and external forces seeking to disrupt its celestial harmony."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/west-01.webp","alt":"west lore image 1"},{"type":"h2","text":"Country - West Empire"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/west-02.webp","alt":"west lore image 2"},{"type":"p","text":"At the zenith of the Western Empire's intricate hierarchy sits the Emperor, embodying the nation's supreme authority. The title of Emperor, inherited through the bloodline of the ruling family, signifies not just political dominion but also spiritual leadership, cementing the Emperor's status as the axis around which the empire revolves. This empire mirrors a complex yet rigidly structured governance system, emphasizing stability, hierarchy, and the sanctity of the imperial lineage which has lasted for centuries."},{"type":"p","text":"Directly beneath the Emperor are the High Counselors, a small, elite group of advisers and officials handpicked by the Emperor himself. These individuals typically hail from prestigious noble families or have demonstrated exceptional loyalty or skill. The positions within the High Counselors are not hereditary but are granted by the Emperor, who considers the candidate's merit, loyalty, and potential to contribute to the empire's governance. The families of the high counselors are all of previous or possibly future ruling family bloodlines."},{"type":"p","text":"Following the High Counselors are the Lords of the Provinces, who govern the empire's vast territories. The title of a Lord is often hereditary, passed down through noble families that have sworn fealty to the Emperor. However, in cases of extraordinary merit or necessity, the Emperor can bestow lordship on a deserving individual outside the hereditary nobility. These Lords are tasked with managing their provinces, collecting taxes, and ensuring the local populace adheres to the laws and edicts of the empire."},{"type":"p","text":"The fourth tier of leadership comprises the Imperial Magistrates, appointed officials responsible for the empire's judicial and bureaucratic functions. These positions are earned through rigorous examinations and proof of loyalty to the empire. The Imperial Magistrates are crucial in implementing the laws, overseeing public projects, and maintaining order within the empire. Their role, while not as prestigious as the Lords or High Counselors, is vital in ensuring the smooth operation of the empire's vast administrative machine."},{"type":"p","text":"The country's leadership governs a vast land filled with a variety of peoples. Some dwell in the deserts of the east, others from the frozen forests of the south, many to the northern grasslands, and the most in the central and western marshlands and temperate forests. Aside from native borns, they also govern over an extensive slave and tamed monster population."},{"type":"h3","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/west-03.webp","alt":"west lore image 3"},{"type":"h3","text":"Population - 5.8 million"},{"type":"p","text":"The population is mostly made of Beastmen but there are several humans as well. More than the East Empire before the war, several Fae have found the west empire to be to their liking of those that strayed from the teachings and magical forests of the Fae See. Constructs also have some presence but barely due to their treatment being little better than what they would find in East Empire. At least in West Empire they are not immediately put in chains. West Empire also has one of the largest Monster populations in the 2nd Continent due to their ability to tame monsters. Their society follows a strict Caste System:"},{"type":"p","text":"Imperial Family - they are the rulers of the nation and the heads of the noble faction. - always beastmen with no recorded exceptions"},{"type":"p","text":"High Nobility - they are mainly the Counselors, Lords, and Courtiers"},{"type":"p","text":"Lesser Nobility - They are the Magistrates and those allowed to own lands - 2nd and 3rd class are rarely creatures other than beastmen with a few humans in their number"},{"type":"p","text":"Clergy and Mages - Magic users and Church faction leadership"},{"type":"p","text":"Guild Members - these are members of Adventure or Merchant guilds. - 4th and 5th class are the first to see some fae among their number and more humans"},{"type":"p","text":"Commoners - most of the populace consisting of unskilled laborers and farmers - highest class possible for Constructs"},{"type":"p","text":"Slaves/Criminals - all slaves consisting of all races. they do not count as creatures that can have crimes committed against them - most slaves are of human, fae, and construct races"},{"type":"p","text":"Despite being tamed, animals and monsters in the possession of tamers are not considered part of the population and are not even protected like property in the same way slaves are."},{"type":"p","text":"The higher classes live lives of indulgence and decadence embracing the 'truths' of being a beastman and part of nature (in stark contrast to the restrained and simple lives of Republic beastmen) while the lower classes live lives of hardship and thanklessness. Public disrespect against someone of an upper class can lead to severe consequences."},{"type":"h3","text":"Slavery"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/west-04.webp","alt":"west lore image 4"},{"type":"p","text":"In the Western Empire, the institution of slavery is deeply entwined with both magical practices and divine edicts, creating a system where individuals may be bound to servitude through means that go beyond mere physical constraints. This system, sanctioned by ancient pacts with the gods, involves a ceremonial rite that imbues the process of enslavement with both a legal and a spiritual dimension."},{"type":"h4","text":"The Binding Ceremony"},{"type":"p","text":"The initiation of an individual into slavery within the Western Empire is marked by the Binding Ceremony, a ritual that involves the invocation of specific deities worshipped within the empire, who oversee the realms of loyalty, servitude, and bondage. During the ceremony, a magical contract is created between the slave and the master, which is then sealed by the gods' power. This contract is not only a written document but also a magical bond that inscribes itself upon the soul of the enslaved individual, manifesting as a visible magic mark. Those with supernatural sight may be able to see the terms of the binding within the mark."},{"type":"p","text":"This mark serves several purposes: it identifies the person as a slave, outlines the terms of their servitude (such as the duration, most are forever, and the nature of their service), and binds them to their master in a way that discourages disobedience through a series of built-in magical compulsion. The severity of these compulsions can range from mild discomfort when disobeying orders to severe physical torment for more grievous acts of defiance, such as attempting escape or harming their master."},{"type":"h4","text":"Pathways to Freedom"},{"type":"p","text":"Despite the seemingly inescapable nature of this magical bondage, freedom is not always beyond one's grasp. Methods of escape include:"},{"type":"p","text":"- Completion of Service: For those whose terms of servitude are defined by a specific duration (nearly non-existent), the completion of this period automatically dissolves the magical contract, freeing the individual."},{"type":"p","text":"- Manumission: A master may choose to release a slave from service, a decision that must be ratified through a Releasing Ceremony, which invokes the gods once more to dissolve the bond. More common than completion of service and generally in exchange for incredible service and benevolence on both parts."},{"type":"p","text":"- Escape and Sanctuary: Running away, while risky due to the magical mark that can track an escaped slave, is possible. Certain temples and orders dedicated to gods of freedom and justice offer sanctuary to runaways. These sanctuaries are protected by powerful wards that obscure the magical mark, giving the escaped slave a chance to live free from immediate recapture. Additionally, there are rare rituals and artifacts capable of erasing or overriding the magical bond, though these are often guarded, hidden, or deemed illegal by the empire. Such sanctuaries are destroyed and their clergy put to death by impalement for public display whenever they are found."},{"type":"p","text":"- Trial by the Gods: In exceptional cases, a slave may appeal directly to the gods through a perilous ritual known as the Trial by the Gods, seeking to prove their worthiness for freedom. Success depends on the individual's virtue, strength, and the whims of the gods but can result in the instantaneous dissolution of the magical bond."},{"type":"h3","text":"Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"At its core, the economy is driven by trade, both domestic and international, facilitated by the capital port city of Quang. Quang's advantageous position by a massive river and its access to the sea make it a hub for goods flowing from the interior to the wider world, including exotic spices, textiles, and magical artifacts salvaged or created within the empire."},{"type":"p","text":"A significant aspect of the economy is the Empire's relationship with monsters and beastmen, which not only defines its military prowess but also contributes to its economic activities. The Adventurer's Guild, consisting largely of skilled Monster tamers, plays a crucial role in managing the monster populations, turning potential threats into assets. These tamed monsters are utilized in various sectors, from agriculture to transportation, enhancing productivity and innovation."},{"type":"p","text":"The Merchant's Guild leverages the Empire's extensive trade networks, dealing in both mundane and magical goods. Their operations are vital for the economic well-being of the empire, ensuring a steady flow of wealth and resources. This guild often collaborates with adventurers to acquire rare items and materials from dangerous territories, further enriching the empire's markets."},{"type":"p","text":"The Noble Faction, with its control over vast tracts of land and resources, plays a significant role in agriculture and resource extraction, contributing to the economy's stability and growth. Their involvement in the slave trade, sanctioned and regulated by the Church through magical rituals, also impacts the labor market."},{"type":"p","text":"Despite the empire's strong economy, challenges remain, including tensions with neighboring territories, the ethical complexities of slavery, and the need to balance economic growth with the maintenance of harmony between the natural, magical, and beastman realms."},{"type":"h3","text":"Security"},{"type":"p","text":"Within the Western Empire, the maintenance of peace and security is of paramount importance, and the empire has developed unique methods to enforce its laws and order, complementing the use of technology like the black orb."},{"type":"h4","text":"The Sentinel Beasts"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/west-05.webp","alt":"west lore image 5"},{"type":"p","text":"The Western Empire harnesses its unique relationship with monsters through the creation of Sentinel Beasts, a special breed of tamed monsters(primarily) trained specifically for law enforcement and public safety. These monsters are paired with skilled handlers, forming units that patrol the streets of cities like Quang and the broader empire. Sentinel Beasts possess innate abilities that allow them to sense malintent and track individuals marked as slaves or with titles of infamy, such as \"Thief,\" \"Murderer,\" or \"Vandal.\" Their keen senses are augmented by magical enhancements, enabling them to detect concealed individuals or those attempting to mask their criminal titles through magic or subterfuge. While they cannot perceive a creatures actual titles, if they perceive the magic used to conceal them, that alone is a punishable offense in the empire."},{"type":"h4","text":"The Harmony Edicts"},{"type":"p","text":"Leveraging the empire's rich magical heritage, the Western Empire has instituted the Harmony Edicts, a set of magical laws woven into the very fabric of society. These edicts are enforced through a network of enchanted structures and artifacts distributed throughout the empire, capable of emitting a subtle, harmonizing magic that influences the populace towards more peaceful behavior. While not strong enough to control minds or eradicate free will, the Harmony Edicts subtly reduce aggressive tendencies and enhance feelings of community and solidarity among the citizens."},{"type":"p","text":"This magical influence is particularly concentrated in areas prone to conflict, such as marketplaces, taverns, and the borders of the empire. Specialized magistrates, trained in both law and arcane arts, oversee the maintenance of these edicts, adjusting their intensity and reach as needed to preserve the delicate balance between peace and personal freedom. It was such magical prowess that enabled the Duchy to overcome the edicts and successfully rebel against the west empire several decades prior."},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel"},{"type":"p","text":"Aside from the portals that cover the 2nd continent, the Western Empire has additional unique modes of transportation to complement that network."},{"type":"h4","text":"Sky Caravans"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/west-06.webp","alt":"west lore image 6"},{"type":"p","text":"Sky Caravans are an awe-inspiring sight in the Western Empire, combining the ancient art of Monster taming with sophisticated magical engineering (although lacking compared to Duchy advances). These caravans consist of large, floating platforms that are tethered to and pulled by giant flying creatures, such as dragons, griffins, or specially merged magical monsters. The platforms are enchanted to carry significant weight, making them ideal for transporting goods, passengers, or even entire contingents of soldiers across the empire's expansive territories."},{"type":"p","text":"The magic that enables the Sky Caravans is the enchantments on the platforms themselves, which make them buoyant and capable of stable flight when lifted and propelled by comparably unstable creature flight."},{"type":"p","text":"Sky Caravans offer several advantages:"},{"type":"p","text":"- Speed and Accessibility: While portals provide instant travel between fixed points, Sky Caravans can reach areas where portals are not present or accessible, offering flexibility in travel routes."},{"type":"p","text":"- Security: The presence of powerful creatures and the height at which Sky Caravans travel make them relatively safe from ground-based threats, including bandits and monstrous hordes."},{"type":"p","text":"- Cultural Significance: Travelling by Sky Caravan is a prestigious and revered tradition in the empire, often used for diplomatic missions, ceremonial journeys, or transporting important artifacts."},{"type":"h4","text":"Shadow Paths"},{"type":"p","text":"Another distinct mode of transportation unique to the Western Empire is the use of Shadow Paths, secretive routes that utilize the empire's latent magical energies. Shadow Paths are magical trails that weave through the very fabric of reality, allowing travelers to move swiftly and unseen across short distances. Accessible only to those knowledgeable in the empire's ancient magics or those in possession of specific enchanted items, these paths offer a clandestine alternative to the more visible Sky Caravans or portals."},{"type":"p","text":"Shadow Paths are like an open secret: known by most but rarely used by the common populace due to the requirements and their locations typically being secret. The use of these paths is tightly regulated by the empire, requiring special permits or the sanction of high-ranking officials or magistrates to be used in a legal capacity."},{"type":"h3","text":"Capital - Quang"},{"type":"p","text":"The capital of the Western Empire, stands as a bustling port city nestled in a strategic bay where a massive river meets the sea. Architecturally magnificent, it serves as the empire's economic heart, with trade routes stretching east to the Duchy and around the southern coast to the Fae See. The city's diverse districts, from the Imperial heartland of opulence to the vibrant Trade and Market District, showcase a rich tapestry of cultures and goods. Quang thrives as a cultural and commercial hub, its docks alive with international merchants and exotic wares. The city is well-protected by both its formidable walls and a unique defense system that incorporates tamed monsters, symbolizing the Western Empire's blend of tradition, power, and a touch of the magical, making it a pivotal player in the realm's geopolitics and economy."},{"type":"h3","text":"Factions"},{"type":"p","text":"In the complex tapestry of the Western Empire's society, various factions vie for influence, power, and survival. Each faction has its distinct role within the empire, contributing to the dynamic interplay of interests that shape the empire's politics, economy, and culture."},{"type":"h3","text":"Nobles"},{"type":"p","text":"The Noble Faction comprises the empire's hereditary aristocracy and those handpicked by its leadership, high-ranking military officers, and those with ancient titles. This faction holds significant power, rooted in land ownership, control over the empire's military forces, and close ties to the imperial family. They are key players in governance and often influence imperial policy through their advisory roles or by serving as High Counselors. The Nobles often find themselves in a delicate balance of cooperation and competition with the other factions, particularly in matters of trade and law. Their power is substantial and is a defining force in the empire's stability and direction."},{"type":"h3","text":"Adventurer's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"A collective of explorers, monster hunters, and quest-seekers, holds a unique place within the Western Empire, particularly noted for comprising the majority of the nation's Monster tamers. This specialization not only enhances their role in the empire's defense against monsters but also cements their status as essential contributors to the empire's economy and cultural heritage. The ability to tame and bond with monsters adds a layer of respect and mystique to the guild, enabling its members to undertake missions that would be impossible for ordinary individuals."},{"type":"p","text":"Their beast-taming skills make them invaluable to the empire, providing a steady supply of tamed monsters for various purposes, ranging from labor to defense. This capability fosters a symbiotic relationship with the Noble Faction, as nobles often rely on adventurers for securing and training Monsters that can be used in their armies or as symbols of prestige. Meanwhile, their dealings with the Merchant's Guild involve the trade of rare creatures and magical beasts, adding a lucrative dimension to their ventures."},{"type":"p","text":"Adventurers with monster-taming prowess are also seen as natural allies of the Church Faction, given the Church's interest in maintaining the balance between the natural and supernatural realms. Their expertise is occasionally sought in rituals and ceremonies that require the presence or use of tamed magical creatures."},{"type":"p","text":"Despite the dangers associated with their profession, members of the Adventurer's Guild enjoy a status that blends respect, fear, and admiration from the general populace."},{"type":"h3","text":"Merchant's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"The Merchant's Guild is the backbone of the empire's economy, controlling trade routes, markets, and the flow of goods both within and beyond the empire's borders. Their wealth grants them substantial influence, enabling them to sway economic policies and regulations. They are often in negotiation or competition with the Nobles, who control the lands through which their trade routes pass. Their relationship with the Adventurer's Guild is symbiotic, as adventurers provide them with rare goods and protection. The Merchants hold considerable power, especially in urban centers and trading hubs, and can be a persuasive force in political matters through their economic leverage."},{"type":"h3","text":"Church"},{"type":"p","text":"The Church in the West Empire wields its influence through spiritual authority and its central role in the administration of the empire's magical and divine practices, especially those surrounding slavery. As the custodians of the Binding Ceremony, the Church has a significant say in the initiation and regulation of slavery within the empire. This control over the slavery rituals places them at a critical junction of moral, ethical, and practical power, as they not only facilitate the creation of these bonds but also possess the knowledge and authority to dissolve them under certain conditions."},{"type":"p","text":"Their interactions with the Noble Faction are nuanced, given their shared interests in maintaining social order and stability, but also marked by tension due to the Church's unique powers over an institution that many nobles rely on. The Church's relationship with the other factions, such as the Merchant's and Adventurer's Guilds, involves a mix of cooperation and moral guidance, with the Church often advocating for the humane treatment of slaves and offering spiritual services to guild members."},{"type":"h3","text":"Criminal Faction"},{"type":"p","text":"The Criminal Faction, though operating outside the official law, plays a role in the empire's underbelly. This faction includes thieves' guilds, black market dealers, and other outlawed groups. They wield a different kind of power, rooted in the control of illegal trade, information brokerage, and the ability to influence through fear or bribery. Their relationship with the other factions is primarily adversarial, though they often engage in covert dealings with the Merchant's Guild and, occasionally, corrupt nobles. Their power is difficult to quantify, as it operates in the shadows, but they are capable of significant influence within certain domains and situations."},{"type":"h3","text":"Religion"},{"type":"p","text":"The Church Faction embodies several, mostly, beastmen gods. However, one particular religion stands above the others in West Empire."},{"type":"p","text":"Path of Celestial Harmony"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Quang, Capital City"},{"type":"p","text":"The capital of the Western Empire stands as a bustling port city nestled in a strategic bay where a massive river meets the sea. Architecturally magnificent, it serves as the empire's economic heart, with trade routes stretching east to the Duchy and around the southern coast to the Fae See. From the Imperial Heartland of Opulence to the vibrant Trade and Market District, each locale showcases a rich tapestry of cultures and goods. Quang thrives as a cultural and commercial hub, its docks alive with international merchants and exotic wares. The city is well-protected by both its formidable walls and a unique defense system that incorporates tamed monsters, symbolizing the Western Empire's blend of tradition, power, and a touch of the magical, making it a pivotal player in the realm's geopolitics and economy."},{"type":"p","text":"There is a slaver's guild run by the magistrate named Orlan. (Source)"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Shikoba Village"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/west-07.webp","alt":"west lore image 7"},{"type":"p","text":"A village in the northeastern part of the West Empire ruled by a powerful and well-respected Matriarch. Inhabited almost exclusively by harpies of varying intellect--the most intelligent often serving as scouts in the West Empire military."},{"type":"h3","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"h4","text":"NPCs"},{"type":"p","text":"Matriarch"},{"type":"h2","text":"Family - Desrosiers"},{"type":"p","text":"The Desrosiers form a large family of haregons/rabbitfolk that are heavily invested into the training and trading of slaves. The relation between the members of the family tends to be rather business-oriented and has little show of (unearned) family kindness. They would not hesitate to enslave one of their own, should they fail too badly."},{"type":"p","text":"The Desrosiers Estate is a large estate on the outskirts of Quang in the Ororoot Empire, owned by the mistress of the Desrosiers family. It has nearly exclusively beast staff (the free and proper kind) working on it, as the mistress is said to not even wish to look upon non-Beasts, despite trading in them as slaves."},{"type":"h4","text":"NPCs"},{"type":"p","text":"Mistress Desrosier"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Simiyu Desert"},{"type":"p","text":"Infamous for being a base of slaver operations, especially legally ambiguous trade."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Rotem City"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in the West Empire's central (Simiyu) desert, the city is particularly difficult to travel to without proper guides. Surrounded by hazards, both natural and otherwise, the city has been overlooked and neglected by governing bodies. In the resulting vacuum, Rotem developed its own autonomous system with which to rule its inhabitants. The West Empire tolerates Rotem's autonomy so long as it benefits the slave trade."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - ???"},{"type":"p","text":"A desert area on the border of the Kingdom and West Empire"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Hondoshire Harbor"},{"type":"p","text":"On the central west coast of the West Empire, warm rays grace the bustling coastal town of Hondoshire Harbor. It has a lavish mediterranean-style aesthetic with red-tiled roofs popping against white shoreside cliffs and the lush green hills beyond. The scenic bay is a popular tourist attraction, drawing the random traveler as well as wealthy merchants. Additionally, this harbor is an important stop for ships traveling further to the capital, providing a boon to West Empire maritime. The town is flanked by two major rivers, so it also affects trade and travel inland."},{"type":"p","text":"Rumor - The locals murmur about something called 'the Agrigore', a creature with outlandish descriptions."},{"type":"h3","text":"Drink the Sea Festival!"},{"type":"p","text":"Submitted by Hecotoro"},{"type":"p","text":"Festival Scene:"},{"type":"p","text":"Season / Time of Year: Mid Summer"},{"type":"p","text":"What It Celebrates / Purpose: It celebrates the union of different cultures, races and the love for beer and food."},{"type":"p","text":"How They Celebrate / Traditions: The idea is to prove who can chug down more beer. You divide into groups, representing your town, nation, race, whatever you choose to represent. You gather a team of your five best drinkers and compete in different events."},{"type":"h4","text":"Event #1"},{"type":"p","text":"Potion Maker! Bring your best alchemist, your best farmer, bartender, chef or whoever you think can create the best tasting and strongest beer."},{"type":"h4","text":"Event #2"},{"type":"p","text":"The Will to Live! Get your endless belly ready, because this is an endurance test! Your participant will drink as much beer as they can... out on the sea! Last one standing, or that didn't empty their stomach, wins!"},{"type":"h4","text":"Event #3"},{"type":"p","text":"Survival of the Fittest! Your strongest member must not only carry barrels of beer up a hill, but they must finish it before being able to come down and get another one! The one with the most empty barrels at the end wins!"},{"type":"h4","text":"Event #4"},{"type":"p","text":"Too Drunk To Walk Home? Time to put your drunk mind to work. Find a way out of this maze, but not before being put into a drunken state by our amazing wizards and witches! Have fun!"},{"type":"h4","text":"Event #5"},{"type":"p","text":"Teamwork Makes the Dream Work! All members must gather in front of the ocean, get on their team boats and drink as much beer as possible!"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Vaitiare Town"},{"type":"p","text":"Vaitiare Town is situated in the Vaitiare Barony in the West Empire's southeast along its border with the Fae See. Lady Vaitiare, the bearkin nan (West Empire term for baron), presides over the region. As demonstrated by the enforcement of the caste system in her local bathhouse, Lady Vaitiare's ideologies are firmly in line with her nation's views on harmony, slavery and religion (as a follower of Shuixian). Even so, she possesses a curiosity not seen in her peers for neighbouring cultures and habits. Through this unusual inclination, Lady Vaitiare searches for future cooperation opportunities."},{"type":"h4","text":"NPCs"},{"type":"p","text":"Lady Vaitiare"},{"type":"p","text":"Rohit, Personal Guard"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Cipactli Forest"},{"type":"p","text":"Cipactli Forest is a densely forested area situated on both sides of the West Empire-Grand Duchy border. The area is known to be overrun by monsters and has become a popular destination for those that train and enslave such creatures."},{"type":"p","text":"The West Empire side of the Cipactli Forest is known as the Moss-dead Territory due to being largely overgrown with moss-covered trees. The widespread covering of moss provides perfect camouflage to a particular breed of tiny, moss monsters that call this territory home. There is also an entity known as the Wood Guardian that stalks the area. See West Empire bestiary for more info."},{"type":"h3","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Monster Tamer Estate"},{"type":"p","text":"A luxurious mansion in the middle of the monster-infested Cipactli Woods in the north-east of the Western Empire. It is owned by Bozho Desrosiers and staffed exclusively by enslaved monsters."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Gnollbone Village"},{"type":"p","text":"A former village in the West Empire's north that was inhabited mostly by gnolls until it was burned down by a fire elemental. Some settlers have returned recently with hopes of rebuilding."},{"type":"h3","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Vaitaire's Wonderful Waters"},{"type":"p","text":"Vaitiare's Wonderful Waters offers a subscription service for access to the baths. Other than that no one knew the place existed."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Xi'en Mountain"},{"type":"p","text":"A mountain on the eastern side of the Empire, whose peak is constantly hidden by clouds. It is known among cultivators for being the spot where three dragon veins met, making it a potent spot of power useful for achieving breakthrough. The veins meet at the summit, meaning the mountain’s danger level rises as one climbs higher. It is said that whoever reaches the summit and survives there long enough will attain immortality."}]},{"id":"lake","name":"Continental Lake","aliases":["Continental Lake","Isekai Hell - Continental Lake"],"summary":"The centrally located lake that's as massive as some nations. It is located in the 2nd continent. Predominantly occupied by aquatic variants of beastmen, humans, and fae, all settlements are underwater habitats. Despite the habitats being large domed cities filled with fluid, their great desire to be an accommodating place for tourism means the fluid is breathable by surface dwellers. Ever since the recent era of pea","theme":{"accent":"#76cde8","accent2":"#2c6e9c","glow":"#b6ecff","deep":"#06121a","motif":"water"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"Continental Lake"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - Continental Lake"},{"type":"p","text":"The centrally located lake that's as massive as some nations. It is located in the 2nd continent. Predominantly occupied by aquatic variants of beastmen, humans, and fae, all settlements are underwater habitats. Despite the habitats being large domed cities filled with fluid, their great desire to be an accommodating place for tourism means the fluid is breathable by surface dwellers. Ever since the recent era of peace on the 2nd continent, the lake nation has been making big strides to be one of the largest tourism destinations on the continent. Every year, thousands of passengers ride massive fish vessels to the dark depths where the cities lay on the lake bed or in deeper fissures. They do not experience seasons in the same way due to being so deep in the water, so they have no off season. Their seafood is about as unique and fresh as it comes and they have all manner of unique flora and fauna they cultivate very all manner of accommodations. Borrowing from The Duchy, they have made strides in the music and entertainment industry, leveraging their aquatic homes to add special effects and distortions to the entertainment that make it one of a kind. They are a tame subset of the undersea nations that spread into the greater sea beyond the lake. They are attacked by monsters due to the ocean depths also accumulating manna, but not nearly as much as the deep ocean settlements in the great sea. Visitors are encouraged to keep an eye on their possessions during their visits, however, due to sea dwellers following a strict finders keepers policy that seems to not give them criminal titles."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/lake-01.webp","alt":"lake lore image 1"},{"type":"h2","text":"Country - Continental Lake"},{"type":"p","text":"Country or nation is a strong word to use for the underwater cities. They govern themselves independently in city states but are allied against monsters and land dwellers should any incursions arise. Devoid of seasons and the passage of the sun, their days and months are governed by tides, currents, water flows, and the migratory patterns of the various sea life. Contrasting popular perceptions of the lake bottom, there is a very diverse biome on the lake floor of trenches, seaweed forests, vents and other geo thermal areas, extreme elevation differences from crushing depths to tight but survivable depths. Rumor has it much of the continental lake was dry land at one time."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/lake-02.webp","alt":"lake lore image 2"},{"type":"h3","text":"Population - ???"},{"type":"p","text":"Census information is incredibly difficult to gather. Between the constant influx and exit of outsiders coupled with the aqua folks' intense reluctance to be numbered and counted, estimates put the population at minimum in the hundreds of thousands. However, some theorize it could be in the millions depending on how many underwater cities there are that are perhaps yet unknown to the surface or simply forgotten. Constructs are particularly few in number. Despite their resilience to the depths and not needing the breath in some cases, their inability to properly travel the depths they were not designed for keeps most away. There's also a fear of how the fluids may impact their inorganic shells. It's not clear who has greater sway under water among the beastmen, fae, and humans."},{"type":"h3","text":"Capital - Crustanton"},{"type":"p","text":"One of the biggest known underwater cities, it was said to have once been a great city by a different name, but has since taken on its current name and guise as number one entertainment destination under the water anywhere. It takes days of travel by living vessels to reach. Surface dwellers are generally encouraged to eat a type of seaweed called \"horgorh\" which helps land dwellers experience fewer symptoms of sea sickness or other complications from deep sea diving and living. Unique to the city, there's a massive archive of preserved records of the old world back when Crustanton went by a different name and supposedly still experienced the sun."},{"type":"h3","text":"Security"},{"type":"p","text":"The lake cities enforce several checks before land dwellers ever get to their streets under the water. They must pass criminal and monster checks before boarding vessels and again with deeper inspections before entering any city through their port. The means to get to the cities by great fish is generally intentionally delayed and marketed as a luxury experience and acclimating period, but in reality, some of that time is to see if any individual aboard the ships is unfit for prolonged undersea exposure mentally. Some of it is also to give criminals and undercover monsters type to perpetrate criminality that may get them caught and expelled before they get to the cities."},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel"},{"type":"p","text":"The severe depths some of the cities find themselves at limits travel even for aquatic races. The pressure is too great to withstand without magical or biological supports above and beyond the normal. For this reason, travel of long distances is generally by great living vessel fish. Travel over short distances can be done by protected chariots and carriages pulled by aquatic animals. For relatively quick jobs outside, aqua folk may apply certain magics or don suits to manage tasks and errands before returning indoors. However, the last part is least common due to most citizens living inside massive domed cities that offer all manner of transports around. Most of which needs to be paid for unless you know a guy."},{"type":"h3","text":"Factions"},{"type":"h4","text":"Noble/Leadership Faction"},{"type":"p","text":"The Abyssal Court: Each city-state is governed by a noble ruler known as an Abyssal Lord/Lady. They're generally from the oldest and most powerful families within their respective city-states. All Abyssal Lords/Ladies convene at Crustanton for the Abyssal Court, a grand assembly that discusses and makes decisions regarding common threats, laws, and agreements amongst the city-states. Despite the united front they put up, there is a constant, fluid power play amongst the Abyssal Court, making them as treacherous as the depths they inhabit."},{"type":"h4","text":"Merchant Guild - The Deep Trade Consortium"},{"type":"p","text":"This guild holds significant sway due to their control over the distribution of goods both within and beyond the Continental Lake. They're primarily responsible for organizing tourism, from selling ride tickets on the living vessel fish to arranging accommodation and entertainment for the tourists. They also control the sale of unique seafood and other aquatic resources. They maintain a careful balance of power with the Abyssal Court, as their services are integral to the prosperity of the lake nation."},{"type":"h4","text":"Church/Faith Groups - The Currents of the Lake"},{"type":"p","text":"Spirituality amongst the aquatic folks revolves around the respect and reverence for the lake and the creatures within it. The currents, tides, and migratory patterns are seen as messages from higher powers. Various temples located throughout the city-states are maintained by different sects within The Currents, each focusing on a different aspect of lake life. These faith groups are deeply respected and often consulted by the Abyssal Court on major decisions."},{"type":"h4","text":"Adventurer's Guild - The Trench Wanderers"},{"type":"p","text":"Named after the adventurers who brave the deepest and most dangerous parts of the lake, the Trench Wanderers are often the first line of defense against monsters. They also explore unknown territories, discover new resources, and occasionally salvage artifacts from forgotten or hidden underwater cities. Their members range from brave aquatic folks to daring surface dwellers looking for adventure."},{"type":"h4","text":"Thieves Guild - The Kelp Shadows"},{"type":"p","text":"This group takes advantage of the \"finders keepers\" policy. They're experts in stealth, sleight of hand, and making the most of the lake's darker corners. While they're seen as a menace by tourists, the local population often turns a blind eye to their activities, considering them a part of life in the Continental Lake. The Abyssal Court is aware of them but tolerates their existence as they serve as a source of information and can be useful in delicate situations."},{"type":"h4","text":"Entertainment Industry - The Song of the Depths"},{"type":"p","text":"This faction has grown in power with the rise of tourism. Composed of artists, musicians, performers, and more, they leverage the unique underwater habitats to create one-of-a-kind entertainment experiences. They often work closely with the Deep Trade Consortium and have a significant influence on the lake's culture and reputation."},{"type":"h3","text":"Religion - Currents of the Lake"},{"type":"p","text":"The \"Currents of the Lake\" is an animistic faith deeply embedded in the underwater societies, revering deities representing various natural forces within the lake. Deities include the Deep Mother, symbolizing the lake and life, the Current Master, representing currents and tides, the Vent Father, embodying geothermal vents, and the Seabed Sentinel, reflecting the lake bed's stability and fertility."},{"type":"p","text":"Worship practices align with daily and seasonal lake rhythms, with temples often built near natural features connected to the deities. Devotees partake in Current Dances, mimic the flow of water, leave offerings at geothermal vents, and gather for the Seabed Planting, a communal event for planting new crops. The faith encourages respect for nature, influences societal norms, and fosters a sense of community, acceptance, and a deep connection with the lake environment."},{"type":"h3","text":"Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"The economy of the Continental Lake nation is multi-faceted, largely driven by its booming tourism industry, unique underwater flora and fauna trade, and arts & entertainment scene. Tourism, facilitated by their breath-malleable fluid environments and unique aquatic entertainment, brings in substantial revenue, making it a top priority. Aquaculture plays a key role in local sustenance and provides seafood delicacies for export. Unique underwater plant and animal products, often not found elsewhere, contribute significantly to trade. Lastly, the entertainment industry, boosted by their unique aquatic performances, adds a creative and cultural dimension to their economy. Despite their thriving industries, a \"finders keepers\" policy creates an informal economy where lost and found items can become someone else's wealth, fostering a sort of underwater treasure hunting culture."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/lake-03.webp","alt":"lake lore image 3"},{"type":"h2","text":"Creature - Prismatic Lobster"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/lake-04.webp","alt":"lake lore image 4"},{"type":"p","text":"An uncommonly found creature, with a prismatic shell that is considered a rare ingredient used in potion-making."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - Elizabeth Huffmaster"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Abandoned Island Town"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/lake-05.webp","alt":"lake lore image 5"},{"type":"p","text":"An odd Island Town in the Continental Lake, which used to be a thieves' hideout, but currently stands empty. Located on a key point between magical Ley Lines, good for teleportation magic. (Reference, [Isekai Hell] Faster than the Fastest)"},{"type":"p","text":"The isle has since been reclaimed by adventurers and merchants wishing to do more lake trade free of existing port taxes. A portal was created within the town—making the trip to the island much easier. Residents of the ocean regularly visit for trade or brief vacations."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - Jan Joost Verhoef"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Crustanton, Library"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/lake-06.webp","alt":"lake lore image 6"},{"type":"p","text":"A library found deep within the Continental Lake, located in Crustanton. It is sorted by signs, in [Beastial], which reveal the contents of each section in the library’s labyrinth of bookshelves. The library holds an assorted variety of modern leather-bound books, centuries-old scrolls and millennia-old tablets. Finding specific materials may require the help of the many library assistants."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - Raffaela Lerch"}]},{"id":"duchy","name":"The Grand Duchy","aliases":["The Grand Duchy","Isekai Hell - The Grand Duchy"],"summary":"The Grand Duchy of Roran, an advanced nation of less than a million humans, beastmen, fae, and constructs, stands as a marvel of magic-infused technology in a medieval world. It boasts towering vertical cities navigable by flight, teleportation, and various modes of transport, with a sophisticated magical network facilitating information exchange and currency transactions. Known for its mighty magical academy, the Et","theme":{"accent":"#b59af1","accent2":"#664fb2","glow":"#d6c8ff","deep":"#100a1b","motif":"arcane"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"The Grand Duchy"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - The Grand Duchy"},{"type":"p","text":"The Grand Duchy of Roran, an advanced nation of less than a million humans, beastmen, fae, and constructs, stands as a marvel of magic-infused technology in a medieval world. It boasts towering vertical cities navigable by flight, teleportation, and various modes of transport, with a sophisticated magical network facilitating information exchange and currency transactions. Known for its mighty magical academy, the Ethereal Luminary, Roran has become a beacon of magical research and development. Its capital, Aslan, is a fortified port city that uses magic to bar entry to criminals and monsters. Despite its advanced state, the duchy's natural landscape consists of temperate forests and plains, with rainforests near the Continental Lake, and encroaching desertification at its western borders. Governed by a council of high-level mages, Roran leans towards political neutrality but opposes slavery, although struggles with recognizing constructs as more than magical creations. Its society is deeply rooted in religious beliefs, particularly those connected to magic and sorcery, originating from the western empire."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/duchy-01.webp","alt":"duchy lore image 1"},{"type":"h2","text":"Country - The Grand Duchy"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/duchy-02.webp","alt":"duchy lore image 2"},{"type":"p","text":"The Grand Duchy of Roran is situated next to the Continental Lake on the 2nd continent. The region's climate varies from the lush rainforests near the lake to temperate forests and grassy plains around its western borders, to an encroaching desert on its westernmost edges. This variation in ecosystems provides an abundant source of both magical and natural resources."},{"type":"h3","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/duchy-03.webp","alt":"duchy lore image 3"},{"type":"h3","text":"Population < 1,000,000"},{"type":"p","text":"The nation is inhabited by a blend of races including humans, beastmen, fae, and constructs, resulting in a population of fewer than one million. It's a cosmopolitan population with diverse needs and aspirations, united by the shared goal of preserving their independence and pursuing magical advancements. Beastmen are surprisingly one of the more numerous in the region despite the typical struggle beastmen have with attaining great levels of magic."},{"type":"h3","text":"Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"The Duchy's economy is magically infused, using a magical currency tracked via a magical network. Internally, this allows for efficient, fraud-free transactions. For external trade, they have developed a unique system that converts magical currency into a common trade currency, rykes. The Duchy's primary import is mithril, a crucial element in magical research, in exchange for controlled exports of their magical innovations. Careful not to destabilize the world or lose their advantage, they maintain a meticulous balance in their foreign trade. Additionally, sectors like illusion-based entertainment and vertical architecture contribute significantly to their GDP, providing unique economic dimensions."},{"type":"h3","text":"Security"},{"type":"p","text":"The Duchy's security is maintained through the widespread use of sophisticated magical barriers that detect criminal or monstrous intent, making it one of the safest nations to reside in. They have a well-organized system of checks and balances that maintain peace, both within their borders and at their frontier, constantly warding off the West Empire and other potential threats."},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel"},{"type":"p","text":"The Duchy's advanced magical technology extends to its transportation systems. A mixture of flight, teleportation, and a variety of magically-aided land, air, and sea carriages are used for getting around, making for efficient and interesting travel experiences."},{"type":"h3","text":"Capital - Aslan"},{"type":"p","text":"The capital city, Aslan, is a marvel of magical architecture, with structures reaching skyward, surpassing what would be typically possible in a non-magical society. It is a bustling port with a magical barrier that effectively wards off any ill-intent individuals or monsters, allowing only the law-abiding to pass through. It is the go to place for magical pursuits and magically enhanced diversions."},{"type":"p","text":"Aslan employs a unique barrier (mechanically, asset [barrier]) that serves the general function of the black orbs in detecting undesirables (monsters/criminals). If such a creature crosses its threshold, guardian statues at the gate are animated to deal with the problem."},{"type":"h3","text":"Factions"},{"type":"h4","text":"Nobles"},{"type":"p","text":"The noble class, a class of high ranking mages in the Grand Duchy of Roran, holds a unique place due to their intricate knowledge and command over complex magical spells, allowing them to establish their settlements into awe-inspiring vertical architectures. Their influence extends to areas of cultural preservation and setting societal norms, with many nobles serving as patrons to the magical arts. Their political power, however, is balanced by the other factions to prevent any undue concentration of control. Political titles in ascending order are Lord Mage, Dread Mage, Archmagus, and Councilor/Thaumarch (compare to Baron, Count, Duke, King/Council, respectively)."},{"type":"p","text":"Dread Mage Ammadeus Belmonte"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/duchy-04.webp","alt":"duchy lore image 4"},{"type":"p","text":"An alchemist of the Duchy of Roran. Focused on the development of magical potions and elixirs, as well as other chemical uses of plants and other substances."},{"type":"h4","text":"Merchants"},{"type":"p","text":"The Merchant's Guild is the lifeline of the Duchy's economy. They have perfected the art of negotiating with other nations for resources, particularly mithril, a vital component for their magical research and advances. Additionally, they manage the innovative magic-to-ryke currency exchange, facilitating trade with less magically inclined nations. Despite their commercial interests, the Guild's influence is limited in political matters, ensuring a balance of power."},{"type":"h4","text":"Church"},{"type":"p","text":"The Church of Magical Enlightenment isn't merely a religious institution; it serves as a moral compass in a nation where magic can potentially override ethics. They endorse deities associated with magic, encouraging ethical use and advancing knowledge about magical arts. Their influence extends to education, as they run many institutions teaching about magic, faith, and their interconnectedness."},{"type":"h4","text":"Adventurer's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"The Adventurer's Guild in Roran is not just about exploration and monster hunting. They serve as scouts, intelligence agents, and often diplomats handling relations with the neighboring Beastmen Republic and Fae See. They provide early warning for any encroachments from the West Empire, making them an essential component of the Duchy's security."},{"type":"h4","text":"Criminal Factions"},{"type":"p","text":"Even with the sophisticated magical barriers, some criminal factions operate within the Duchy. However, their scope is significantly different, primarily focused on magical contraband and information brokering. The Roran Council keeps them in check, often using their networks for intelligence, resulting in a complex, begrudging symbiosis."},{"type":"h3","text":"Religion"},{"type":"p","text":"In the Duchy, the primary religion is a complex belief system centered around magic. The Church of Magical Enlightenment worships various deities associated with different aspects of magic and magical creatures. A prevalent deity is Zephyrus, the Ascendant Mage, symbolizing the ideal balance between magical prowess and wisdom. Religious practices often involve meditation, magical incantations, and celestial observations, reflecting their mystical, intellectual culture."},{"type":"h2","text":"Construct - Living Books"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/duchy-05.webp","alt":"duchy lore image 5"},{"type":"p","text":"What is better used to guide people through expansive libraries than a book? Nothing. Hence the Duchy uses magic book [constructs] as guides. Found most common in the capital, Aslan."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - Katrin Minko"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Amaru's Bathhouse of Miracles"},{"type":"p","text":"A magical bathhouse located in the city of Aslan, in the Grand Duchy. Its proprietor, a snake woman by the name of Amaru, uses magic to customize each guest's experience, altering the scenery, scents, and temperature."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/duchy-06.webp","alt":"duchy lore image 6"},{"type":"p","text":"Amaru, Bathhouse Proprietor"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/duchy-07.webp","alt":"duchy lore image 7"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Wise Owl Library"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in the center of Aslan proper, it is one of the biggest libraries in the Grand Duchy. It is heavily secure with multiple checkpoints before entry and contains many restricted sections beyond even that. Guests are often met by Flying Book [Constructs] that guide them through the library's many labyrinthine shelves and departments."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - Kaitan"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - MAGE MANOR MAGNIFIQUE"},{"type":"p","text":"An establishment located reasonably close to the Grand Duchy's capital city Aslan, the Manor is advertised as having \"libraries, magic demonstrations and events, leisure and entertainment areas, places of stay, relaxation facilities, and more books\". It is known as a place where weirdo mages like to gather to play intense card games and dabble in shape changing."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Ethereal Luminary"},{"type":"p","text":"The Ethereal Academy possesses a testing ground enchanted with a spell that prevents death and, upon receiving otherwise fatal damage, those within the cave are transported back to a designated spot known as the \"Waiting Room\". This testing ground enables the academy to provide its students with an opportunity to practice combat exercises with lethal force without endangering one another."},{"type":"h2","text":"Aurora Umova (Aurora of Minds)"},{"type":"p","text":"Submitted by Jon the Archivist"},{"type":"h3","text":"What It Celebrates / Purpose:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Aurora Umova is a festival celebrating the strength of intellect of the many minds that fueled the Technological and Magical advancements of the nation, and it’s very holistic in its approach. Strategic thinking, physical effort and development, creative spirit, invention, anything and everything that either goes into developing the mind or showcasing intellectual effort is explored and celebrated. Part festival, part expo, all celebration, Aurora Umova represents the culmination up to that point of all the collective efforts of the Grand Duchy and the brilliant minds that work and grow there."},{"type":"h3","text":"How They Celebrate / Traditions:"},{"type":"p","text":"There are a multitude of traditions that have come and gone over the years, but the core ones today are listed either due to long term relevance, or “modern” significance."},{"type":"h4","text":"Fuller Wargames"},{"type":"p","text":"Utilizing custom, home-grown fullers, these competitions are a collective showcase of engineering and magic prowess, and martial skill, celebrating technical, tactical, and strategic strength of mind."},{"type":"h4","text":"Grand Ethereal Expo"},{"type":"p","text":"This is a collective expose of magical and technological concepts, inventions, and advancements that any brilliant mind can apply for a spot in, so long as they have a feasible idea to present. Fullers and other technologies were first introduced to the public in this way"},{"type":"h4","text":"Twilight Olympics"},{"type":"p","text":"Events for this are typically held in “the cool of the day,” when heat stroke is less likely, hence why it is named for the colors of the sky at those times. Long has it been acknowledged that physical growth, effort, and development contributes to the growth and strength of the mind, so a selection of contestants will participate in a series of physical and martial sports both cooperatively and competitively as a nod to the importance of physical effort in personal and collective growth."},{"type":"h4","text":"Mindforge Kolektiv"},{"type":"p","text":"Just as it sounds, this tradition is a collective effort. The Mindforge Kolektiv is an open volunteer workshop hosted throughout the duration of the festival, allowing mages, inventors, and laborers to come together in challenging, creative, and inventive efforts. These can take forms ranging from intellectual discourse and conceptual workshopping, to active prototyping and initial manufacturing. Many projects that would later reshape the Duchy and surrounding kingdoms began here."},{"type":"h4","text":"Gozba Sumraka (Twilight Feast)"},{"type":"p","text":"The end of the festival has always involved a grand feast where great minds bring their culinary creativity together in a collective celebratory effort. The cooking takes place in participating kitchens all throughout the final day, with their efforts served at the grand feast itself, held at Dusk."},{"type":"h4","text":"Forum Stellarum Campi (Starfield Market)"},{"type":"p","text":"Like any great festival, a grand pop-up market is going to be par for the course. Held throughout the festival’s duration, artisans the world over, from every field and industry will showcase and market wares of their own creation, showcasing their intellectual and creative skill in a tangible form that festival-goers can take home with them."},{"type":"p","text":"Season / Time of Year: Mid-Summer, two weeks long"},{"type":"p","text":"Festival Scene:"}]},{"id":"kingdom","name":"Kingdom of Rotia","aliases":["Kingdom of Rotia","Isekai Hell - Kingdom"],"summary":"The northern human country for this roleplay and likely one of the last visited countries due to its distance and dangerousness after Ryke. Has a medieval European theme and aesthetic. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to canon for Kingdom. Each winter, the sea between the dark continent and Kingdom freezes enough to","theme":{"accent":"#e2c46c","accent2":"#395e9e","glow":"#dce9ff","deep":"#080e18","motif":"crown"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"Kingdom of Rotia"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - Kingdom"},{"type":"p","text":"The northern human country for this roleplay and likely one of the last visited countries due to its distance and dangerousness after Ryke. Has a medieval European theme and aesthetic. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to canon for Kingdom. Each winter, the sea between the dark continent and Kingdom freezes enough to allow for monster hordes to pour out. Kingdom is the tip of the spear that blunts the advancing attack upon the 2nd continent. Led by nobles uniquely qualified to pilot massive mecha called Fullers, they lead the knights of Kingdom in a never ending battle. The new Queen is young, as all new kingdom rulers are, replacing her late father and king who dead in battle. She now pilots her father's Fuller. Aside from the nobles that take their duty seriously, there are others that still find the time to scheme. There are whispers the late king did not die in battle in the way all might believe. The nation is also regularly plagued by disease brought on by the mass amounts of mana and chaos that washes upon the nation's shores. Mana enough to twist the minds of men, send beasts into a rage, or taint the ground. A truly harsh place."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/kingdom-01.webp","alt":"kingdom lore image 1"},{"type":"h2","text":"Country - Kingdom"},{"type":"p","text":"The Kingdom of Rotia is a northern country characterized by cooler temperatures and a diverse topography, featuring a couple of significant lakes and major rivers. The landscape consists of vast forests, rolling hills, and fertile valleys, with the occasional rocky outcrop dotting the horizon. The northern reaches are cold or frozen and severely scarred by battle. The southern parts of the nation are barren and inhospitably arid."},{"type":"h3","text":"On World Map"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/kingdom-02.webp","alt":"kingdom lore image 2"},{"type":"h3","text":"Population - 2,700,000"},{"type":"p","text":"Rotia has a population of 2.7 million, with the majority being humans, followed by beastmen as the second most common race. The inhabitants are hardy and resourceful, often relying on their resilience and adaptability to survive in a land frequently plagued by monster invasions. Most soldiers are not taken into the army before fathering at least one child. Most of the nation lives in stonewalled cities and towns. Villages are generally short-lived in Kingdom."},{"type":"h3","text":"Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"Rotia's economy is centered around supporting the ongoing war effort against the invading monsters. The nation allocates substantial resources to maintain its defenses and supply the frontlines with food, weapons, and other necessities. Despite the hardships, Rotia's economy remains stable, as the populace is united in their determination to protect their homeland. Trade and industry are focused on sustaining the military and defensive efforts, with a strong emphasis on self-sufficiency and resource management."},{"type":"h3","text":"Security"},{"type":"p","text":"The Kingdom of Rotia's security relies on two main elements: Fullers and Black Orbs. Fullers are advanced mecha, piloted by noble operators, designed to combat the relentless waves of invading monsters. Black Orbs are magical items that reveal the presence of monsters and criminals. Monsters are destroyed with extreme prejudice, while criminals are enlisted to battle the monstrous forces, serving as expendable assets in the ongoing conflict."},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel"},{"type":"p","text":"Travel in Rotia is challenging due to the constant threat of monster invasions. Magic portals provide one option for fast and secure transportation, allowing people to traverse vast distances quickly. However, these portals are heavily guarded and can be costly to use. Travelers must also contend with the dangers of traversing monster-infested lands, making journeys outside of the cities risky endeavors."},{"type":"h3","text":"Capital - Hornbach"},{"type":"p","text":"Hornbach is the bustling capital city of Rotia, strategically situated on a river between the sea and one of the major lakes. The city serves as the political and economic hub of the nation, with a well-fortified center and an impressive array of defensive structures. Hornbach is also the seat of the royal family and the central command for the nation's defense forces."},{"type":"h3","text":"Factions"},{"type":"h4","text":"Nobles"},{"type":"p","text":"The aristocracy of Rotia are responsible for operating the powerful Fullers and leading the defense against the monster hordes. They play a crucial role in the nation's survival and the maintenance of order. All nobles of Rotia are human, and their children inherit their seats. While some may be hybrids, all are human. There is no rule of law keeping it thus, but that is how it's been since the founding of the country."},{"type":"p","text":"Hornbach: The Hornbach's are the current royal family and control the seat of commerce and the capital of the country. Their proximity to the frontline has ensured nothing but the strongest of their line lives to lead the charge each season. They are one of the few houses given the choice of Fullers when new ones are made available by the duchy (providing they have the money to afford it)."},{"type":"p","text":"Schligachi: The Schligachi are the smallest of the houses that lead the war effort. While the Hornbachs take the lion share of the war spoils, the Schligachi get enough to persist. Were a house to crumble or fold into the others, it is expected to be theirs in time."},{"type":"p","text":"Steibach: Brother in arms to Hornbach since time immemorial, the Steibach are also frontline positioned and have a larger land area than the Hornbachs. They are not the tip of the spear, so they have the luxury and responsibility in handling other issues of the nation, like transit, immigration, and some production. If Hornbach is the spear and Schligachi is the side arm, then Steibach is the shield."},{"type":"p","text":"Kangenland: Kangenland is the biggest landmass and population in the country. Their distance from the front and vast swaths of land leave them with the priority of food production and acquisition. As such, they possess stores plentiful enough to feed the nation during particularly harsh years or springs that don't come fast enough. Kangenland's size and distance from the war lends to some civil rivalries among the lords that govern the land, which are further agitated by widespread envy for Hornbach's prized capital and ruler seat. It's not uncommon for spring to bring skirmishes among the nobles and \"accidents\" during war."},{"type":"h4","text":"Merchants"},{"type":"p","text":"This faction ensures that the war effort continues uninterrupted, managing the distribution of supplies and resources to keep the nation running smoothly in the face of adversity."},{"type":"p","text":"Church: The church is responsible for maintaining the morale of the people and training generations of monster slayers skilled in divine magics. They offer spiritual guidance and solace during these challenging times."},{"type":"h4","text":"Adventurer's Guild"},{"type":"p","text":"Primarily focused on dealing with monster threats and criminal elements in the countryside that evade the nation's army, the Adventurer's Guild plays a vital role in maintaining stability throughout Rotia."},{"type":"h2","text":"Religion - Valcorism"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/kingdom-03.webp","alt":"kingdom lore image 3"},{"type":"p","text":"The predominant religion in Rotia, Valcorism, centers around the worship of divine beings known as the Valcori. These celestial guardians are revered for their role in protecting humanity and guiding them in their struggle against the monstrous forces that threaten their existence."},{"type":"p","text":"The Valcori are a pantheon of divine beings, each embodying specific aspects and virtues that the people of Rotia hold dear. A few notable Valcori include:"},{"type":"p","text":"Ranthor, the Protector: Ranthor is the chief deity among the Valcori and the embodiment of courage, strength, and protection. He is often depicted as a mighty warrior, clad in gleaming armor and wielding a powerful, radiant sword. Ranthor leads the Valcori in their eternal battle against the monstrous forces, ensuring the safety of the mortal realm."},{"type":"p","text":"Sylithia, the Healer: Sylithia is the goddess of healing, compassion, and restoration. She is seen as a benevolent figure who mends the wounds of the injured and the hearts of the broken. Her followers include healers and medical practitioners who invoke her blessings to aid in their work."},{"type":"p","text":"Varek, the Tactician: Varek is the god of strategy, wisdom, and cunning. He represents the importance of cleverness and resourcefulness in overcoming adversity. Varek is often portrayed as a master strategist, providing guidance to leaders and tacticians in their efforts to outmaneuver their monstrous foes."},{"type":"p","text":"Elara, the Lightbringer: Elara is the goddess of hope, perseverance, and inner strength. She serves as a beacon of light in the darkness, guiding the people of Rotia through their most challenging times. Her followers find solace in her teachings, which emphasize resilience and the power of the human spirit."},{"type":"p","text":"Valcorism is a religion that unites the people of Rotia in their shared struggle against the monstrous threats that plague their land. Its divine beings offer strength, guidance, and comfort to the people, giving them hope in the face of overwhelming odds."},{"type":"h2","text":"House - House Talton"},{"type":"p","text":"An affluent noble house from the Kingdom of Rotia, which has made investments in great minds from The Magic Duchy and Widersia for the development of technological advancements in fullers and forms of defense against monsters. The Taltons are known for having skilled Fuller pilots in the family."},{"type":"p","text":"Members"},{"type":"p","text":"Affonso"},{"type":"p","text":"Eliza"},{"type":"p","text":"Adriano"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Myathevale"},{"type":"p","text":"A small temporary settlement that is abandoned during the winter season and repaired if needed for occupation during the warm seasons. It acts as a temporary port during the end of fall."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/kingdom-04.webp","alt":"kingdom lore image 4"},{"type":"p","text":"Credits - Myathevale: DarkKitsune"}]},{"id":"sky","name":"Sky Nation","aliases":["Sky Nation","Isekai Hell - Sky Nation"],"summary":"Sky nation is made up of several islands that free float around the world. Most are hidden in clouds or other phenomena that make discovery not simple.","theme":{"accent":"#d8ecff","accent2":"#6ca4cf","glow":"#ffffff","deep":"#09131a","motif":"sky"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"Sky Nation"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - Sky Nation"},{"type":"p","text":"Sky nation is made up of several islands that free float around the world. Most are hidden in clouds or other phenomena that make discovery not simple."},{"type":"p","text":"The sky nation believes in the creator. Supposedly an entity higher than [god]. But the will of the creator is under much debate which has led to theological division among the tribes as to the actual will of the creator leading to various forms of worship and doctrine."},{"type":"h2","text":"Faction - Hallson Tribe"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/sky-01.webp","alt":"sky lore image 1"},{"type":"h3","text":"The Great Skra"},{"type":"p","text":"A grand library in the Sky Kingdom found in Hallson tribe land. The library is large and features multiple floors which are suitable to its flying denizens, on top of the library is a rounded arena area where events take place from the Sages debating to magic duels to theater."},{"type":"h4","text":"Trials of Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"On the top floor there is a door which requires a key to be opened. Beyond this door is where one can attempt the trials. Successful completion grants access to the library's oldest area--which is off limits to the average person--where advanced or more valuable information is kept."}]},{"id":"widersia","name":"Widersia","aliases":["Widersia","Isekai Hell - Widersia"],"summary":"On the southern edge near the eastern border squeezed between The See and The East Empire on the 2nd continent is one of the more scientifically advanced nations in the world. In a world of magic, the people of Widersia strove to advance their understanding of the natural world by divorcing themselves from war, decadence, and the gods. It has influences from both the See and The East Empire, but it is very much a clo","theme":{"accent":"#c99355","accent2":"#616c74","glow":"#efd0a4","deep":"#12100e","motif":"gear"},"blocks":[{"type":"h1","text":"Widersia"},{"type":"h1","text":"Isekai Hell - Widersia"},{"type":"p","text":"On the southern edge near the eastern border squeezed between The See and The East Empire on the 2nd continent is one of the more scientifically advanced nations in the world. In a world of magic, the people of Widersia strove to advance their understanding of the natural world by divorcing themselves from war, decadence, and the gods. It has influences from both the See and The East Empire, but it is very much a clockwork and steam powered fantasy of its own making. Any persons, places, things, or events of note may go here so long as it came from a graded roleplay that was deemed acceptable to add to the canon for Widersia."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/widersia-01.webp","alt":"widersia lore image 1"},{"type":"h3","text":"Current Situation"},{"type":"p","text":"Widersia is caught between The See and the East Empire who are at war. It is growing increasingly difficult to keep the war away from their front steps and bleed into their country. What defenses they had that allowed them to gain their independence would be put to the test if the war effort to turn against them for any reason."},{"type":"h2","text":"Country - Widersia"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/widersia-02.webp","alt":"widersia lore image 2"},{"type":"p","text":"Situated between two warring empires, a small, peaceful and relatively isolated country that is known for its advanced steam and clockwork technology sits. The government of Widersia is a constitutional monarchy, with a monarch (effectively a king/queen, but commonly referred to as 'regent' or 'crown regent') who serves as a figurehead and a parliament that holds the majority of the political power. The country and government were formed by a group tired of the warring between the Fae See and the Human Empire. Humans and Small Fae who felt their natural talents were being overlooked defected from their nations and took with them their land holdings. The new nation, crafted from the land of the See and Empire, was quickly contested but the invaders were repelled. No longer held back by the strict tenets of their faith or the slothfulness of waning empire, Widersia brought together some of the best craftsmen and inventors available at the time. Rather than developing magical advances, they tried to make a world better suited and manageable by the common man/creature. The result was an alternative line of technology a few hundred years ahead of its time."},{"type":"h3","text":"Population - ~100,000"},{"type":"p","text":"The population of Widersia is primarily composed of humans and small fae races, such as gnomes and halflings, who are known for their ingenuity and technological expertise. There is also a small population of other common Fae who primarily live on the west side of the country. Constructs are welcome, created, and are the most plentiful in Widersia after the East Empire. Beastmen rarely make it down to the country of steam in clockwork. Their warrior natures do not mesh well with the more automated and civil living that allows even the weak to hold political or economic sway with the right tools and friends. Monsters are next to non-existent in the Widersia"},{"type":"h3","text":"Capital - Clockhaven"},{"type":"p","text":"The capital of Widersia is known as Clockhaven, a bustling city that is home to many of the nation's most talented engineers and inventors. Steam billows from the many factories and refineries around the city day and night. Airships, relying on floating gas and mechanical propulsion, are often seen coming in and out of the city after docking at the tallest buildings made with airports. Meanwhile, a timely steam engine chimes regularly throughout the day and night as it moves cargo and passengers around the country."},{"type":"h3","text":"Security"},{"type":"p","text":"Widersia maintains its security through a combination of methods constructions, such as clockwork guards and steam-powered security systems. The nation is also protected by a powerful network of underground tunnels and hidden fortifications that are difficult to penetrate. Tunnels and rails throughout the nation make its logistics and ability to ambush or fortify second to none. Massive land clearing for the sake of its industries have also made the land somewhat bare and difficult for the Forest dwelling See to properly invade with their full strength."},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel"},{"type":"p","text":"The most common forms of travel in Widersia are by airship and steam-powered train. The nation's extensive network of railways and airfields connect the major cities and outlying regions, making it easy for travelers to move quickly and safely across the country. The rugged terrain makes other forms of travel difficult at best. Portals are relatively scarce in the small nation as well."},{"type":"h3","text":"Factions"},{"type":"p","text":"Widersia has a relatively balanced power structure, with the nobles, merchants (predominantly industrialists), and adventurers all holding a roughly equal amount of political and economic power. The parliament serves as a neutral arbiter of disputes and conflicts, ensuring that all voices are heard and that no one group dominates the others. The exception to the rule, the church holds the least amount of power and only exists at all in Widersia to cater to those that have not yet let go or forgotten the ways of the former nations."},{"type":"h4","text":"Nobles"},{"type":"p","text":"Baron Fromm - A construct Baron in charge of some of Clockhaven's outer districts (not the entire city), backed by a powerful supporter as a 'test' to see how far 'artificial' intelligence can come when given such an important task."},{"type":"p","text":"Appearance:"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/widersia-03.webp","alt":"widersia lore image 3"},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - Amy Cornelson on ArtStation"},{"type":"h4","text":"Criminal"},{"type":"p","text":"Don Domenico “Big Dom” Calabrese - Don Domenico Calabrese, usually called Big Dom by those with enough sense, is a large and imposing mob boss with a loud temper, expensive tastes, and a talent for turning any private meeting into both a business negotiation and a personal grievance. He operates out of the back rooms of La Stella Rossa, an upscale restaurant in the racing district, where his influence is felt through hired muscle, backroom favors, stable investments, and quiet threats."},{"type":"p","text":"Big Dom is theatrical, sentimental, dangerous, and deeply prideful. He can swing from grieving patriarch to murderous fury in the same breath, especially when he feels disrespected. He treats loyalty, food, family, and business as almost the same thing. To refuse hospitality from him is risky, especially when that hospitality is a mountain plate of gabagool, which he treats with near-religious seriousness. Though often ridiculous in manner, Big Dom is not harmless. His rage is real, his connections are wide, and his men understand that his orders are not suggestions. He prefers matters handled quietly, but when insulted, he is perfectly willing to make an example of someone."},{"type":"p","text":"His most prized asset is Serafina “Velvet Comet” Bellaflora, a famous horse-girl racer whom he often refers to as “my little champion” or “my little comet.” His attachment to her is a mix of business interest, personal affection, possessiveness, and public pride. When she was kidnapped before the Derby, Dom hired adventurers off the books rather than through the Adventurer’s Guild, both to avoid public humiliation and to keep control of the situation."},{"type":"p","text":"Role: Underworld patron, racing investor, restaurant owner, and local powerbroker."},{"type":"p","text":"Common mannerisms: He speaks loudly, gestures with cigars, offers gabagool as if refusal were a moral failing, calls incompetent underlings “numbnuts,” and treats disrespect as a personal injury."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical quote: “Sit. Eat. Anybody says no to the gabagool, I’m taking it personal.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Appearance:"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/widersia-04.webp","alt":"widersia lore image 4"},{"type":"h3","text":"Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"Widersia's economy is primarily driven by its advanced steam and clockwork technology, which is shared in controlled amounts to other nations in exchange for valuable resources and goods. The nation also has a significant agricultural sector, particularly in the outlying regions where farmers grow crops and raise livestock."},{"type":"h3","text":"Religion"},{"type":"p","text":"Widersia is a relatively secular nation, with no single dominant religion or faith. Most citizens practice a blend of spiritual and scientific beliefs, believing in the power of technology to solve problems and improve the lives of all people, while still believing in the power of the Elements or the Old Greek/Roman gods of the Empire for things science can't or hasn't yet answered."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/widersia-05.webp","alt":"widersia lore image 5"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location – Clockhaven"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/widersia-06.webp","alt":"widersia lore image 6"},{"type":"p","text":"The capital of Widersia, Clockhaven, lies in the center of the eastern side of the country. A bustling technological metropolis of commerce and industry, Clockhaven leads the continent in scientific advancement, preferring the laws of physics to those of magic. With people and resources in demand all over the city, at all times, a complex and comprehensive system of railways connect the major city centers. Steam and exhaust constantly rise from the towers of factories that dot the city, while the cacophony of clock chimes, train whistles, and motors prevent any possibility of peace. The population, like the rest of Widersia, is mostly human, with a large number of gnomes, dwarves, and halflings. Constructs make up much of the manual labor, though a few have risen to grander ranks. Other Fae and Beasts rarely make it to the city, preferring the quieter, less developed parts of the country. The wealthiest parts of the city, areas designed for the affluent or to attract tourists for profit, boast gas lamps that light the streets throughout the night."},{"type":"p","text":"Dr. Gregorius House - Tinkerer, doctor, inventor. His shop is located in Clockhaven. His genius is only matched by his toxic personality, being sarcastic and cantankerous even when dispensing praise to others. Dr. House isn't a [Native]. (Character Grade B)"},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - Gioncarlo Niccolai on Saatchiart"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location - Railworker's Crossing"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/lore/widersia-07.webp","alt":"widersia lore image 7"},{"type":"p","text":"A busy intersection of roadways in Clockhaven. Popular location for people to meet when they don't trust each other as there are many escape routes. The trains that travel through the location journey between the many factories, warehouses, and air docks in the district. A nearby station acts as a hub for the few passenger cars that reach this far out. While steam powers the engines of the trains, the gnomish and dwarvish mechanical engineering involved in the design of the tracks keeps the vehicles running on a clockwork system, ensuring there are no accidents or delays."},{"type":"p","text":"Art Credit - CODENAME S.T.E.A.M. (dubious)"},{"type":"h3","text":"Location – Third Factory Street"},{"type":"p","text":"A smoke-filled place on the outskirts of [Clockhaven], where sunlight rarely touches. Abundant with abandoned factories and laboratories—what once was the centre of Widersia's technological advances, is now a degrading area of the past with few factories still fully operative."},{"type":"h2","text":"Construct - Worker Bots"},{"type":"p","text":"Small constructs used for simple tasks, such as repairs on airships. Can communicate in Analog, but can only think in their primary objectives."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Shire"},{"type":"p","text":"A peaceful area in Widersia, predominantly inhabited by [Halflings], who keep to old methods in their community; attempting to more so coexist with nature in contrast with those of [Clockhaven]. The inhabitants aim to create contraptions which promote a balance between magic, people and the environment via harnessing ambient mana, however, they have yet to achieve a surplus necessary for community growth."},{"type":"p","text":"Artist - Etienne Hebinger"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Robotics & Steelwork Inc."},{"type":"p","text":"Formerly one of the biggest steam-work [Construct] factories in all the realm, but production now runs at a paltry fraction of its heyday after being outpaced by competitors. It still operates making Worker Bots, but at far less than its total capacity."},{"type":"p","text":"Art Credit - Ben Lo (Artstation)"},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - The Slippery Soaperation"},{"type":"p","text":"A relatively new experimental bathhouse in the leisure district of Clockhaven. It features construct guides to welcome guests and explain how the bathhouse works (though they might occasionally glitch out and reboot to newer versions of themselves)."},{"type":"p","text":"It has a relatively normal outdoor pool, if you ignore the sudden jet-streams and questionable machine for dispensing swimwear. It also features an indoor pool and traditional bath."},{"type":"p","text":"Its Dwarven owner is continuously looking to improve the bathhouse by adding new features or modifying existing ones, like the technology to censor erotic or unsightly forms with rays of light."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location - Brasshaven"},{"type":"p","text":"A coastal fortress at the south of Widersia. While its artillery remains active, always in search of threats to its democratic state, it also serves as a military courtroom."},{"type":"p","text":"The following panel of judges (pictured below in order) presides over the courtroom, while also having duties in the Widersian Military:"},{"type":"p","text":"Rear Admiral Portia Rakeley"},{"type":"p","text":"Captain Barrister Ottilie Skarn"},{"type":"p","text":"Commander Edda Vannes"},{"type":"p","text":"Construct Adjutant G12 Gavel"},{"type":"p","text":"Colonel Silas Mach"},{"type":"p","text":"Major-Constructor Halden Ryft"},{"type":"p","text":"Commodore Lucia Brandt"}]}],"source":"World Lore.docx"};
